{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_54","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,92p' TASK.md; sed -n '2260,2345p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/API.md'; sed -n '240,285p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/API.md'; sed -n '785,835p' PLAN.md; cat PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE: Wii Fit\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, the riftlight engine kit. Keep the engine (pixel-engine.js) as it ships, as its guide says, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\n\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\n\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## This computer\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\n\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\n\n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\n### DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS: readonly TouchButton[]\n```\n\nDefault buttons for PlatformerCharacter (see character/controls.ts KEYMAP).\n\n### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n```\n\nStandard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\nKEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n\n### interface GamepadLike\n\nThe parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects).\n\n- `readonly connected?: boolean`\n- `readonly mapping?: string`\n- `readonly axes: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value?: number }[]`\n\n### class Input\n\nKeyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n- Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\n  code (`consumePress`). Queued presses expire after `pressWindow` s of game time.\n- Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\n  right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\n  (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\n- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\n  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\n  the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\n  finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\n  a frame is not lost.\n- Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game…\n\n- `new Input(target: Window | null = window)`\n- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\n- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\n- `wheel: number`: Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out).\n- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\n- `readonly analog: { x: number; y: number; }`: Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active.\n- `readonly padAxis: { x: number; y: number; }`: Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward).\n- `gamepadConnected: boolean`: True while any gamepad is connected.\n- `readonly preventKeys: Set<string>`: Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\n- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\n- `gamepadDeadzone: number`: Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1).\n- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\n- `now: number`: Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`.\n- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\n- `pressWindow: number`: Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped.\n- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\n- `dispose(): void`: Remove every listener this Input added (window and canvas).\n- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\n- `beginFrame(now: number, dt: number, pads?: readonly (GamepadLike | null)[]): void`: Engine: begin a frame at game time `now` (seconds). Polls gamepads and drops expired queued presses. `pads` defaults to `navigator.getGamepads()`; tests can pass fakes.\n- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\n- `isDown(...codes: string[]): boolean`\n- `anyDown(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `isDown` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array (fixed-step code).\n- `wasPressed(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press (valid for the current render frame).\n- `consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean`: True once per physical key press, kept until consumed or until it is older than `pressWindow` (150 ms of game time). Use from fixed-step code (which may run zero or several times per frame) so no press is dropped, while a stale press (made during a pause, a l…\n- `consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean`: `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array.\n- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\n- `setState(s: InputState, now: number): void`: Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go.\n- `get queuedPresses: string[]`: Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests).\n- `clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void`: Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input).\n- `moveAxis(): { x: number; y: number }`: -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\n- `endFrame(): void`: Call at the end of each rendered frame.\n- `setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void`: Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false).\n- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\n- `setButtons(bits: number): void`: Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would.\n- `get mouseButtons: number`: Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`.\n- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\n- `send(command: unknown): void`: Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked, a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keep…\n- `get commands: readonly unknown[]`: This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\n- `deliver(): void`: Engine: a live frame begins to run: what was sent since the last one becomes its `commands`.\n- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\n- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\n- `playBefore(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, before the engine's `beginFrame`: the frame's held keys and presses (presses queue at the time they would have arrived, the frame before's game time).\n- `playAfter(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection.\n- `shouldRun(now: number): boolean`\n\n### frameView()\n\n```ts\nfunction frameView(viewport: Viewport, base: Resolution, aspect: AspectMode, current: Resolution): { framing: Framing; resolution: Resolution }\n```\n\nThe framing and art resolution of a view (PixelRenderer's canvas, or a HeadlessView's viewport):\n`computeFraming`, and the art size as a resolution. Identity is kept where nothing changed: the\n`current` object while the art size stays, else `base` itself when the art size equals it (a\nfixed or 16:9 view reports the preset it was given), else a new one.\n\n### interface Framing\n\n- `readonly artWidth: number`: Art (internal) resolution actually rendered. Equals `internal` in fixed mode.\n- `readonly artHeight: number`\n- `readonly scale: number`: Device pixels per art pixel. Integer whenever `integer` is true.\n- `readonly integer: boolean`: True when every art pixel maps to an integer block of device pixels.\n- `readonly canvasWidth: number`: Canvas backing-store size in device pixels.\n- `readonly canvasHeight: number`\n- `readonly cssWidth: number`: Canvas CSS size and offset inside the viewport, in CSS pixels.\n- `readonly cssHeight: number`\n- `readonly offsetX: number`\n- `readonly offsetY: number`\n\n### interface Game\n\nA game is a plain object. The engine owns rendering, physics stepping, camera,\nlighting and debug UI; the game only builds its world and reacts to input.\n\n- `readonly name: string`\n- `readonly args?: unknown`: The plain JSON the game was made with, when its name alone can't rebuild it (a lab's depth and seed, the door a room was entered by): kept in its recordings (`Recording.args`), so a tool can make the same game again to replay one (`npm run replay`, src/games.…\n- `readonly assets?: readonly string[]`: Models `setup` will load (`ctx.loadModel` URLs). Optional: listing them lets the engine start downloading while the renderer and physics initialise.\n- `setup(ctx: GameContext): Promise<void> | void`: Build the level: load models, add colliders, spawn entities.\n- `fixedUpdate?(ctx: GameContext, dt: number): void`: Runs before every fixed 60 Hz physics step. Move characters/apply forces here.\n- `ready?(ctx: GameContext): void`: Runs when the engine starts running this game: after `Engine.start` (just before `__PIXEL_READY__` resolves) and after each `loadGame`. Install page handles for tools here (`window.__MYGAME__`), so they never exist before the engine can step. An exception is…\n- `update?(ctx: GameContext, dt: number): void`: Runs once per rendered frame after physics (animation, pickups, UI state).\n- `cameraTarget(ctx: GameContext): Vector3`: World position the camera follows.\n- `eyePosition?(ctx: GameContext): Vector3`: First-person eye position (defaults to cameraTarget + 0.7 up).\n- `status?(ctx: GameContext): string`: One-line status for the debug UI (score, lives...).\n- `fingerprint?(ctx: GameContext): string`: The game's own state as a short string or hash, for `engine.fingerprint()`: what lives outside physics and `ctx.random` (positions, life, counters, the game's own random streams), so two runs that should match (a replay) can be compared. Only what a replay mu…\n- `snapshot?(ctx: GameContext): unknown`: The game's own state as plain data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): everything a later frame reads that the engine does not keep (its entities, timers, random streams; the handles of its physics bodies). With `restore`, the game has save-states.\n- `restore?(ctx: GameContext, state: unknown): void | Promise<void>`: Put the game back to what `snapshot` returned (`engine.restore()`): the same game, already set up. Find physics bodies again by handle (`ctx.physics.world.getRigidBody(h)`).\n- `beforeRestore?(ctx: GameContext): void | Promise<void>`: Optional: leave whatever mode the game is in before a restore changes anything (a mode with a camera of its own, a dialog, a level): `engine.restore()` calls it first, then checks the snapshot fits (the camera preset) and puts the engine's part back, then `re…\n- `onCameraChange?(ctx: GameContext): void`: Called after `engine.setCamera()` swapped the camera preset mid-game. The world, physics and player are untouched; adjust anything that depends on the preset (e.g. side-scroller lane lock, hiding the player model in first person).\n- Start ✔: `Engine.start(new Boot(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), aspect: 'fill', touch: false, settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }, quality: info ? 'medium' : 'high', seed, background: PALETTE.sky, camera }))`.\n- Each scene is a `Game`, swapped with `engine.loadGame(scene, { camera })`. It frees everything per level; keep persistent state in `App`. Transition: `await screen.cover('iris')`, `await loadGame`, `await screen.reveal('iris')`.\n- `BaseScene` owns the frame order: `update` → `App.device.update` → overlays (pause, dialogue, dev) take input first → the scene's own update → `hud.clear()` → scene draw → overlays draw. Gameplay goes in `fixedUpdate`, skipped automatically while `timeScale` is 0.\n- **Rules from the guide that matter here:** gameplay in `fixedUpdate` with `consumePress`; `wasPressed` only in `update`; all randomness from `ctx.random` forks (never `Math.random`); time from `ctx.time` (never `performance.now`); no `new PointLight`. Modules guard `document`, `window`, `navigator` and `localStorage`, so **everything runs in Node** ✔.\n- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\n- **Debug API**, kept in the shipped game (`globalThis.__GAME__ = App`): `go(id, args)`, `state()` as JSON, `setDriver(skill)`, `tunables`. Give every scene a real `status()` line (`activity hoop | play | t 31.2 | score 412`) and a `fingerprint()` (score, Dot state).\n\n---\n\n## 17. Verified recipes\n\n### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n\n```js\n// tools/build.mjs (esbuild is on this machine)\nexecFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--platform=browser', '--target=esnext', '--charset=utf8', '--outfile=.build/bundle.js', '--log-level=warning'], { stdio: 'inherit' });\nconst safe = (s) => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script').replace(/<!--/g, '<\\\\!--');\nconst html = `<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>${readFileSync('vendor/hub/session.js', 'utf8')}</script>\n${HUB_METAS}\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\"><title>${TITLE}</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div>\n<script type=\"module\">${safe(readFileSync('.build/bundle.js', 'utf8'))}</script>\n</body></html>`;\nwriteFileSync(OUTPUT_HTML, html);   // OUTPUT_HTML: the deliverable name your brief gives, in root\n```\n\nThe session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Output is about 5.4 MB.\n\n### Browser flags ✔\n\n**Use all five.** With only the three in the machine notes, `renderer.capture()` failed: `mapAsync ... A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`.\n\n```\n--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\n```\n\n### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n\n`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder. Then `node check.mjs <page> --keys KeyD*30` works on the built html if it's copied into the dev folder.\n\n### Screenshots ✔\n\nThe live loop rejects `capture()`, and a WebGPU canvas may screenshot blank. So step first, and composite the HUD:\n\n```js\nconst e = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__; e.step(30);          // switches to manual time\n# Progress\n\n## Project\n- Title selected by `crypto.randomInt` from 50 candidates: **A Little Off Balance**.\n- Deliverable basename: `A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846`.\n- Read `TASK.md`; working through `PLAN.md`, the engine kit, and the AI Hub client.\n\n## Work plan\n1. Read the complete design and integration documentation; obtain the unmodified engine and hub client.\n2. Build the core game, island, activities, progression, input, audio, and multiplayer.\n3. Bundle the standalone HTML, run focused playthrough and viewport tests, and fix findings.\n4. Complete About/Credits, `exit-interview.json`, and this progress record.\n\n## Constraints\n- Only work in this directory and the required development subfolder; use OS-assigned localhost ports and stop only our own processes.\n- Keep `pixel-engine.js` unchanged; synthesize audio in code; default music volume 10%.\n- Test small phones, tablets, wide screens, WebKit, and scripted game flows; no physical controller or real iOS device is available.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"reasoning","text":"**Writing initial code patch**"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846' && apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: package.json\n+{\\\"name\\\":\\\"a-little-off-balance\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\",\\\"private\\\":true,\\\"type\\\":\\\"module\\\",\\\"scripts\\\":{\\\"build\\\":\\\"node tools/build.mjs\\\",\\\"test\\\":\\\"node tests/run.mjs\\\"}}\n*** Add File: src/data/title.js\n+export const TITLE = 'A Little Off Balance';\n*** Add File: src/data/activities.js\n+export const ACTIVITIES = [\n+  { id:'tree', name:'Apologetic Tree', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:1, duration:25, ring:.40, instruction:'KEEP YOUR DOT IN THE RING', quip:'THE TREE ACCEPTS YOUR APOLOGY.' },\n+  { id:'heron', name:'Startled Heron', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:1, duration:25, ring:.36, instruction:'LEAN AGAINST THE WANDERING WIND', quip:'A MOST RESPECTABLE BIRD.' },\n+  { id:'squats', name:'Squats of Regret', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:1, duration:38.4, instruction:'MATCH THE MOVING MARKER', quip:'THAT WAS THE LAST ONE. PROBABLY.' },\n+  { id:'hoop', name:'Hoop Economics', family:'hoop', place:'Beat Beach', day:1, duration:40, instruction:'CIRCLE YOUR STICK OR ROLL W D S A', quip:'THE ECONOMY REMAINS CIRCULAR.' },\n+  { id:'header', name:'Coconut Header', family:'header', place:'Beat Beach', day:2, duration:40, instruction:'LEAN LEFT OR RIGHT TO HEAD COCONUTS', quip:'A SOUND FINANCIAL HEADBUTT.' },\n+  { id:'lunges', name:'Apology Lunges', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:2, duration:38.4, instruction:'MATCH THE MARKER AND ALTERNATE SIDES', quip:'YOUR LEGS HAVE BEEN NOTIFIED.' },\n+  { id:'warrior', name:'Reluctant Warrior', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:2, duration:30, ring:.32, breath:8, instruction:'HOLD THE RING. BREATHE WITH THE BAR', quip:'A WARRIOR, UNDER PROTEST.' },\n+  { id:'step', name:'Step Department', family:'step', place:'Town Square', day:3, duration:40, instruction:'PRESS F OR J WHEN NOTES HIT THE LINE', quip:'YOUR STEPS HAVE BEEN FILED.' },\n+  { id:'slackline', name:'Slackline of Doubt', family:'slack', place:'Lookout', day:3, duration:45, instruction:'STAY CENTERED. STEP TO WALK', quip:'THE ROPE BELIEVES IN YOU.' },\n+  { id:'chair', name:'The Chair Nobody Asked For', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:3, duration:30, ring:.30, breath:8, instruction:'HOLD THE RING. BREATHE WITH THE BAR', quip:'SOMEWHERE A CHAIR FEELS SEEN.' },\n+  { id:'tray', name:'Vitamin Tray', family:'tray', place:'Cafe', day:4, duration:40, instruction:'KEEP THE VITAMINS ON THE TRAY', quip:'NUTRITION HAS NEVER BEEN SO TENSE.' },\n+  { id:'mortgage', name:'Overhead Mortgage', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:4, duration:36, instruction:'PUSH UP TO MATCH THE MARKER', quip:'INTEREST COMPOUNDS. SO DOES SWEAT.' },\n+  { id:'tax', name:'Tax Season', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:4, duration:30, ring:.28, breath:6, instruction:'LEAN AND BREATHE THROUGH THE AUDIT', quip:'YOUR EXTENSION HAS BEEN APPROVED.' },\n+  { id:'jog', name:'Island Jog', family:'jog', place:'Island Trail', day:5, duration:45, instruction:'ALTERNATE F AND J TO RUN', quip:'YOU HAVE LAPSED A COCONUT.' },\n+  { id:'pier', name:'Pier Jump', family:'jump', place:'Pier', day:5, duration:40, instruction:'STEP TO THE EDGE. BREATHE TO JUMP', quip:'THE WATER GIVES YOU A TEN.' },\n+  { id:'plank', name:'Plank Negotiation', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:5, duration:35, ring:.24, breath:6, instruction:'KEEP THE DOT IN THE RING. BREATHE', quip:'YOUR CORE HAS COUNTEROFFERED.' },\n+];\n+\n+export const DAY_NAMES = ['A FRESH START','THE HEAD OF IT','A NARROW VIEW','WEALTH AND HEALTH','THE LONG WAY ROUND','A LITTLE MORE','THE LONG STAND'];\n+export const FRIENDS = ['COACH PLUMB','MABEL','FRANK','KEVIN'];\n+export function activityForDay(day) { return ACTIVITIES.filter(activity => activity.day <= Math.min(day, 5)); }\n*** Add File: src/core/dot.js\n+export const DEFAULT_TUNABLES = Object.freeze({dotLag:.6,dotInstability:3,dotAuthority:3.4,dotDamping:.8,dotNoise:.08,timeScale:1});\n+export class Dot {\n+  constructor(random = Math.random) {\n+    this.x=0; this.y=0; this.vx=0; this.vy=0; this.ux=0; this.uy=0; this.t=0;\n+    this.ph=Array.from({length:4},()=>random()*Math.PI*2);\n+  }\n+  step(dt,inX,inY,tuning=DEFAULT_TUNABLES,modifiers={}) {\n+    this.t+=dt;\n+    const lag=Math.min(1,dt/Math.max(.01,tuning.dotLag));\n+    this.ux+=(inX-this.ux)*lag; this.uy+=(inY-this.uy)*lag;\n+    const noise=tuning.dotNoise*(modifiers.noise??1), instability=tuning.dotInstability*(modifiers.inst??1), authority=tuning.dotAuthority*(modifiers.auth??1);\n+    const noiseX=noise*(Math.sin(1.7*this.t+this.ph[0])+.6*Math.sin(3.1*this.t+this.ph[1]));\n+    const noiseY=noise*(Math.sin(1.3*this.t+this.ph[2])+.6*Math.sin(2.7*this.t+this.ph[3]));\n+    this.vx+=(instability*this.x+authority*this.ux-tuning.dotDamping*this.vx+noiseX+(modifiers.bx??0))*dt;\n+    this.vy+=(instability*this.y+authority*this.uy-tuning.dotDamping*this.vy+noiseY+(modifiers.by??0))*dt;\n+    this.x+=this.vx*dt; this.y+=this.vy*dt;\n+    const distance=Math.hypot(this.x,this.y);\n+    if(distance>1.2){const scale=1.2/distance;this.x*=scale;this.y*=scale;this.vx*=.3;this.vy*=.3;}\n+  }\n+}\n*** Add File: src/core/session.js\n+import { Dot, DEFAULT_TUNABLES } from './dot.js';\n+\n+const clamp=(value,low,high)=>Math.max(low,Math.min(high,value));\n+export function makeProfile(name='PLAYER') {return {name,day:1,drips:0,stars:0,history:[],played:{},goal:'FIND YOUR BALANCE',revealed:false,completedDays:[]};}\n+export function wobbleAge(profile) {\n+  const scores=profile.history.slice(-3);\n+  const average=scores.length?scores.reduce((sum,value)=>sum+value,0)/scores.length:.5;\n+  return clamp(Math.round(20+60*(1-average)-Math.min(20,profile.stars*.5)),18,95)+(profile.revealed?0:7);\n+}\n+export class ActivitySession {\n+  constructor(activity,options={}) {\n+    this.activity=activity; this.hard=\"'!!options.hard; this.duration=options.duration??activity.duration;\n+    this.dot=new Dot(options.random); this.elapsed=0; this.points=0; this.samples=0; this.breathSync=.5;\n+    this.rep=.0; this.hoopLift=.65; this.lastAngle=null; this.angleSpeed=0; this.goodSteps=0; this.lastStep=-2; this.hits=0;\n+    this.tuning={...DEFAULT_TUNABLES,...options.tuning}; this.finished=false; this.distance=0; this.lastDirection=0;\n+    this.eventCount=0; this.lastBeat=-1; this.notes=[];\n+  }\n+  update(dt,input={}) {\n+    if(this.finished)return;\n+    dt=clamp(dt,0,.1); this.elapsed+=dt;\n+    const {x=0,y=0,breath=false,left=false,right=false}=input;\n+    const family=this.activity.family, t=this.elapsed;\n+    const breathIn=this.activity.breath?Math.sin(t*Math.PI*2/this.activity.breath)>0:false;\n+    if(this.activity.breath) this.breathSync+=(Number(breath===breathIn)-this.breathSync)*Math.min(1,dt*2);\n+    const modifiers={noise:this.activity.breath?1.25-.55*this.breathSync:1};\n+    if(this.activity.id==='\"'heron')modifiers.bx=.12*Math.sin(t*.7);\n+    if(this.activity.id==='tax')modifiers.bx=.18*Math.sin(t*.9);\n+    if(this.activity.id==='chair')modifiers.noise*=1+.5*t/this.duration;\n+    if(this.activity.id==='plank')modifiers.inst=1.2;\n+    this.dot.step(dt,x,y,this.tuning,modifiers);\n+    const distance=Math.hypot(this.dot.x,this.dot.y);\n+    let quality=0;\n+    if(family==='still'||family==='tray'||family==='slack'||family==='jump'){\n+      const ring=(this.activity.ring??(family==='slack'?.32:.48))*(this.hard?.8:1);\n+      quality=distance<ring?1:0;\n+      if(this.activity.breath)quality=.8*quality+.2*this.breathSync;\n+      if(family==='slack'){\n+        if((left||right)&&t-this.lastStep>.14){this.lastStep=t;this.goodSteps++;this.distance+=distance<.75?1:.15;}\n+        quality*=.45+.55*clamp(this.goodSteps/(t*1.5),0,1);\n+      }\n+      if(family==='jump'&&breath&&t-this.lastStep>2){this.lastStep=t;this.goodSteps++;this.distance+=distance<.6?1:0;}\n+      if(family==='jump') quality*=.5+.5*clamp(this.goodSteps/Math.max(1,t/5),0,1);\n+    } else if(family==='reps'){\n+      const phase=(t/3.2)%1;\n+      const target=phase<.4?phase/.4:phase<.55?1:phase<.9?1-(phase-.55)/.35:0;\n+      const requested=this.activity.id==='lunges'?Math.abs(x):this.activity.id==='mortgage'?Math.max(0,y):Math.max(0,-y);\n+      this.rep+=(requested-this.rep)*Math.min(1,dt/((this.activity.id==='mortgage'?.15:.10)));\n+      quality=clamp(1-1.6*Math.abs(this.rep-target),0,1);\n+    } else if(family==='hoop'){\n+      const magnitude=Math.hypot(x,y);\n+      if(magnitude>.5){const angle=Math.atan2(y,x);if(this.lastAngle\"'!==null){let delta=angle-this.lastAngle;while(delta>Math.PI)delta-=Math.PI*2;while(delta< -Math.PI)delta+=Math.PI*2;this.angleSpeed+=(Math.abs(delta)/Math.max(dt,.001)-this.angleSpeed)*Math.min(1,dt/.25);}this.lastAngle=angle;}else{this.angleSpeed*=Math.max(0,1-dt*3);this.lastAngle=null;}\n+      const inBand=this.angleSpeed>4.5&&this.angleSpeed<18;\n+      this.hoopLift=clamp(this.hoopLift+(inBand?.35:-.15)*dt,0,1);quality=this.hoopLift;\n+    } else if(family==='\"'step'||family==='jog'){\n+      const beat=Math.floor(t/.7);\n+      if(beat\"'!==this.lastBeat){this.lastBeat=beat;this.eventCount++;}\n+      if((left||right)&&t-this.lastStep>.12){const side=left?-1:1;const phase=Math.abs((t/.7)-Math.round(t/.7));if(family==='\"'jog'?side\"'!==this.lastDirection:phase<.23){this.goodSteps++;}this.lastDirection=side;this.lastStep=t;}\n+      quality=clamp(this.goodSteps/Math.max(1,this.eventCount-1),0,1);\n+    } else if(family==='\"'header'){\n+      const beat=Math.floor(t/2.4);\n+      if(beat\"'!==this.lastBeat){this.lastBeat=beat;this.eventCount++;const target=beat%2===0?-1:1;if(Math.sign(x)===target)this.hits++;}\n+      quality=this.hits/Math.max(1,this.eventCount);\n+    }\n+    this.points+=quality*dt;this.samples+=dt;\n+    if(this.elapsed>=this.duration)this.finished=true;\n+  }\n+  result(){const score=Math.round(100*this.points/Math.max(.001,this.samples));const thresholds=this.activity.family==='\"'reps'?[55,75,90]:[45,70,90];const stars=thresholds.filter(value=>score>=value).length;return {score,stars,drips:2+stars*3+Math.floor(this.duration/30),seconds:this.duration};}\n+}\n*** Add File: src/data/audio.js\n+export const ISLAND_SONG={bpm:100,stepsPerBeat:4,tracks:{bell:{wave:'triangle',volume:.22,attack:.01,decay:.18,sustain:.2,release:.22},bass:{wave:'sine',volume:.15,attack:.03,decay:.2,sustain:.5,release:.18}},patterns:{a:{bell:'C5 . . . E5 . . . G5 . E5 . D5 . . .',bass:'C3 . . . . . . . G2 . . . . . . .'},b:{bell:'A4 . . . C5 . . . E5 . D5 . C5 . . .',bass:'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .'}},order:['a','b']};\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\ncd .. && apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: PROGRESS.md\n@@\n-- Read \"'`TASK.md`; working through `PLAN.md`, the engine kit, and the AI Hub client.\n+- Read `TASK.md` and `PLAN.md`; downloaded the unmodified Pixel Engine 0.46.0 and AI Hub client into the development folder.\n+- Implemented activity catalog, unstable balance physics, scoring/progression primitives, and synthesized music data. Building the playable scenes and interface next.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_56","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846' && apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: package.json\n+{\\\"name\\\":\\\"a-little-off-balance\\\",\\\"version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\",\\\"private\\\":true,\\\"type\\\":\\\"module\\\",\\\"scripts\\\":{\\\"build\\\":\\\"node tools/build.mjs\\\",\\\"test\\\":\\\"node tests/run.mjs\\\"}}\n*** Add File: src/data/title.js\n+export const TITLE = 'A Little Off Balance';\n*** Add File: src/data/activities.js\n+export const ACTIVITIES = [\n+  { id:'tree', name:'Apologetic Tree', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:1, duration:25, ring:.40, instruction:'KEEP YOUR DOT IN THE RING', quip:'THE TREE ACCEPTS YOUR APOLOGY.' },\n+  { id:'heron', name:'Startled Heron', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:1, duration:25, ring:.36, instruction:'LEAN AGAINST THE WANDERING WIND', quip:'A MOST RESPECTABLE BIRD.' },\n+  { id:'squats', name:'Squats of Regret', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:1, duration:38.4, instruction:'MATCH THE MOVING MARKER', quip:'THAT WAS THE LAST ONE. PROBABLY.' },\n+  { id:'hoop', name:'Hoop Economics', family:'hoop', place:'Beat Beach', day:1, duration:40, instruction:'CIRCLE YOUR STICK OR ROLL W D S A', quip:'THE ECONOMY REMAINS CIRCULAR.' },\n+  { id:'header', name:'Coconut Header', family:'header', place:'Beat Beach', day:2, duration:40, instruction:'LEAN LEFT OR RIGHT TO HEAD COCONUTS', quip:'A SOUND FINANCIAL HEADBUTT.' },\n+  { id:'lunges', name:'Apology Lunges', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:2, duration:38.4, instruction:'MATCH THE MARKER AND ALTERNATE SIDES', quip:'YOUR LEGS HAVE BEEN NOTIFIED.' },\n+  { id:'warrior', name:'Reluctant Warrior', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:2, duration:30, ring:.32, breath:8, instruction:'HOLD THE RING. BREATHE WITH THE BAR', quip:'A WARRIOR, UNDER PROTEST.' },\n+  { id:'step', name:'Step Department', family:'step', place:'Town Square', day:3, duration:40, instruction:'PRESS F OR J WHEN NOTES HIT THE LINE', quip:'YOUR STEPS HAVE BEEN FILED.' },\n+  { id:'slackline', name:'Slackline of Doubt', family:'slack', place:'Lookout', day:3, duration:45, instruction:'STAY CENTERED. STEP TO WALK', quip:'THE ROPE BELIEVES IN YOU.' },\n+  { id:'chair', name:'The Chair Nobody Asked For', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:3, duration:30, ring:.30, breath:8, instruction:'HOLD THE RING. BREATHE WITH THE BAR', quip:'SOMEWHERE A CHAIR FEELS SEEN.' },\n+  { id:'tray', name:'Vitamin Tray', family:'tray', place:'Cafe', day:4, duration:40, instruction:'KEEP THE VITAMINS ON THE TRAY', quip:'NUTRITION HAS NEVER BEEN SO TENSE.' },\n+  { id:'mortgage', name:'Overhead Mortgage', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:4, duration:36, instruction:'PUSH UP TO MATCH THE MARKER', quip:'INTEREST COMPOUNDS. SO DOES SWEAT.' },\n+  { id:'tax', name:'Tax Season', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:4, duration:30, ring:.28, breath:6, instruction:'LEAN AND BREATHE THROUGH THE AUDIT', quip:'YOUR EXTENSION HAS BEEN APPROVED.' },\n+  { id:'jog', name:'Island Jog', family:'jog', place:'Island Trail', day:5, duration:45, instruction:'ALTERNATE F AND J TO RUN', quip:'YOU HAVE LAPSED A COCONUT.' },\n+  { id:'pier', name:'Pier Jump', family:'jump', place:'Pier', day:5, duration:40, instruction:'STEP TO THE EDGE. BREATHE TO JUMP', quip:'THE WATER GIVES YOU A TEN.' },\n+  { id:'plank', name:'Plank Negotiation', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:5, duration:35, ring:.24, breath:6, instruction:'KEEP THE DOT IN THE RING. BREATHE', quip:'YOUR CORE HAS COUNTEROFFERED.' },\n+];\n+\n+export const DAY_NAMES = ['A FRESH START','THE HEAD OF IT','A NARROW VIEW','WEALTH AND HEALTH','THE LONG WAY ROUND','A LITTLE MORE','THE LONG STAND'];\n+export const FRIENDS = ['COACH PLUMB','MABEL','FRANK','KEVIN'];\n+export function activityForDay(day) { return ACTIVITIES.filter(activity => activity.day <= Math.min(day, 5)); }\n*** Add File: src/core/dot.js\n+export const DEFAULT_TUNABLES = Object.freeze({dotLag:.6,dotInstability:3,dotAuthority:3.4,dotDamping:.8,dotNoise:.08,timeScale:1});\n+export class Dot {\n+  constructor(random = Math.random) {\n+    this.x=0; this.y=0; this.vx=0; this.vy=0; this.ux=0; this.uy=0; this.t=0;\n+    this.ph=Array.from({length:4},()=>random()*Math.PI*2);\n+  }\n+  step(dt,inX,inY,tuning=DEFAULT_TUNABLES,modifiers={}) {\n+    this.t+=dt;\n+    const lag=Math.min(1,dt/Math.max(.01,tuning.dotLag));\n+    this.ux+=(inX-this.ux)*lag; this.uy+=(inY-this.uy)*lag;\n+    const noise=tuning.dotNoise*(modifiers.noise??1), instability=tuning.dotInstability*(modifiers.inst??1), authority=tuning.dotAuthority*(modifiers.auth??1);\n+    const noiseX=noise*(Math.sin(1.7*this.t+this.ph[0])+.6*Math.sin(3.1*this.t+this.ph[1]));\n+    const noiseY=noise*(Math.sin(1.3*this.t+this.ph[2])+.6*Math.sin(2.7*this.t+this.ph[3]));\n+    this.vx+=(instability*this.x+authority*this.ux-tuning.dotDamping*this.vx+noiseX+(modifiers.bx??0))*dt;\n+    this.vy+=(instability*this.y+authority*this.uy-tuning.dotDamping*this.vy+noiseY+(modifiers.by??0))*dt;\n+    this.x+=this.vx*dt; this.y+=this.vy*dt;\n+    const distance=Math.hypot(this.x,this.y);\n+    if(distance>1.2){const scale=1.2/distance;this.x*=scale;this.y*=scale;this.vx*=.3;this.vy*=.3;}\n+  }\n+}\n*** Add File: src/core/session.js\n+import { Dot, DEFAULT_TUNABLES } from './dot.js';\n+\n+const clamp=(value,low,high)=>Math.max(low,Math.min(high,value));\n+export function makeProfile(name='PLAYER') {return {name,day:1,drips:0,stars:0,history:[],played:{},goal:'FIND YOUR BALANCE',revealed:false,completedDays:[]};}\n+export function wobbleAge(profile) {\n+  const scores=profile.history.slice(-3);\n+  const average=scores.length?scores.reduce((sum,value)=>sum+value,0)/scores.length:.5;\n+  return clamp(Math.round(20+60*(1-average)-Math.min(20,profile.stars*.5)),18,95)+(profile.revealed?0:7);\n+}\n+export class ActivitySession {\n+  constructor(activity,options={}) {\n+    this.activity=activity; this.hard=\"'!!options.hard; this.duration=options.duration??activity.duration;\n+    this.dot=new Dot(options.random); this.elapsed=0; this.points=0; this.samples=0; this.breathSync=.5;\n+    this.rep=.0; this.hoopLift=.65; this.lastAngle=null; this.angleSpeed=0; this.goodSteps=0; this.lastStep=-2; this.hits=0;\n+    this.tuning={...DEFAULT_TUNABLES,...options.tuning}; this.finished=false; this.distance=0; this.lastDirection=0;\n+    this.eventCount=0; this.lastBeat=-1; this.notes=[];\n+  }\n+  update(dt,input={}) {\n+    if(this.finished)return;\n+    dt=clamp(dt,0,.1); this.elapsed+=dt;\n+    const {x=0,y=0,breath=false,left=false,right=false}=input;\n+    const family=this.activity.family, t=this.elapsed;\n+    const breathIn=this.activity.breath?Math.sin(t*Math.PI*2/this.activity.breath)>0:false;\n+    if(this.activity.breath) this.breathSync+=(Number(breath===breathIn)-this.breathSync)*Math.min(1,dt*2);\n+    const modifiers={noise:this.activity.breath?1.25-.55*this.breathSync:1};\n+    if(this.activity.id==='\"'heron')modifiers.bx=.12*Math.sin(t*.7);\n+    if(this.activity.id==='tax')modifiers.bx=.18*Math.sin(t*.9);\n+    if(this.activity.id==='chair')modifiers.noise*=1+.5*t/this.duration;\n+    if(this.activity.id==='plank')modifiers.inst=1.2;\n+    this.dot.step(dt,x,y,this.tuning,modifiers);\n+    const distance=Math.hypot(this.dot.x,this.dot.y);\n+    let quality=0;\n+    if(family==='still'||family==='tray'||family==='slack'||family==='jump'){\n+      const ring=(this.activity.ring??(family==='slack'?.32:.48))*(this.hard?.8:1);\n+      quality=distance<ring?1:0;\n+      if(this.activity.breath)quality=.8*quality+.2*this.breathSync;\n+      if(family==='slack'){\n+        if((left||right)&&t-this.lastStep>.14){this.lastStep=t;this.goodSteps++;this.distance+=distance<.75?1:.15;}\n+        quality*=.45+.55*clamp(this.goodSteps/(t*1.5),0,1);\n+      }\n+      if(family==='jump'&&breath&&t-this.lastStep>2){this.lastStep=t;this.goodSteps++;this.distance+=distance<.6?1:0;}\n+      if(family==='jump') quality*=.5+.5*clamp(this.goodSteps/Math.max(1,t/5),0,1);\n+    } else if(family==='reps'){\n+      const phase=(t/3.2)%1;\n+      const target=phase<.4?phase/.4:phase<.55?1:phase<.9?1-(phase-.55)/.35:0;\n+      const requested=this.activity.id==='lunges'?Math.abs(x):this.activity.id==='mortgage'?Math.max(0,y):Math.max(0,-y);\n+      this.rep+=(requested-this.rep)*Math.min(1,dt/((this.activity.id==='mortgage'?.15:.10)));\n+      quality=clamp(1-1.6*Math.abs(this.rep-target),0,1);\n+    } else if(family==='hoop'){\n+      const magnitude=Math.hypot(x,y);\n+      if(magnitude>.5){const angle=Math.atan2(y,x);if(this.lastAngle\"'!==null){let delta=angle-this.lastAngle;while(delta>Math.PI)delta-=Math.PI*2;while(delta< -Math.PI)delta+=Math.PI*2;this.angleSpeed+=(Math.abs(delta)/Math.max(dt,.001)-this.angleSpeed)*Math.min(1,dt/.25);}this.lastAngle=angle;}else{this.angleSpeed*=Math.max(0,1-dt*3);this.lastAngle=null;}\n+      const inBand=this.angleSpeed>4.5&&this.angleSpeed<18;\n+      this.hoopLift=clamp(this.hoopLift+(inBand?.35:-.15)*dt,0,1);quality=this.hoopLift;\n+    } else if(family==='\"'step'||family==='jog'){\n+      const beat=Math.floor(t/.7);\n+      if(beat\"'!==this.lastBeat){this.lastBeat=beat;this.eventCount++;}\n+      if((left||right)&&t-this.lastStep>.12){const side=left?-1:1;const phase=Math.abs((t/.7)-Math.round(t/.7));if(family==='\"'jog'?side\"'!==this.lastDirection:phase<.23){this.goodSteps++;}this.lastDirection=side;this.lastStep=t;}\n+      quality=clamp(this.goodSteps/Math.max(1,this.eventCount-1),0,1);\n+    } else if(family==='\"'header'){\n+      const beat=Math.floor(t/2.4);\n+      if(beat\"'!==this.lastBeat){this.lastBeat=beat;this.eventCount++;const target=beat%2===0?-1:1;if(Math.sign(x)===target)this.hits++;}\n+      quality=this.hits/Math.max(1,this.eventCount);\n+    }\n+    this.points+=quality*dt;this.samples+=dt;\n+    if(this.elapsed>=this.duration)this.finished=true;\n+  }\n+  result(){const score=Math.round(100*this.points/Math.max(.001,this.samples));const thresholds=this.activity.family==='\"'reps'?[55,75,90]:[45,70,90];const stars=thresholds.filter(value=>score>=value).length;return {score,stars,drips:2+stars*3+Math.floor(this.duration/30),seconds:this.duration};}\n+}\n*** Add File: src/data/audio.js\n+export const ISLAND_SONG={bpm:100,stepsPerBeat:4,tracks:{bell:{wave:'triangle',volume:.22,attack:.01,decay:.18,sustain:.2,release:.22},bass:{wave:'sine',volume:.15,attack:.03,decay:.2,sustain:.5,release:.18}},patterns:{a:{bell:'C5 . . . E5 . . . G5 . E5 . D5 . . .',bass:'C3 . . . . . . . G2 . . . . . . .'},b:{bell:'A4 . . . C5 . . . E5 . D5 . C5 . . .',bass:'A2 . . . . . . . F2 . . . . . . .'}},order:['a','b']};\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\ncd .. && apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: PROGRESS.md\n@@\n-- Read \"'`TASK.md`; working through `PLAN.md`, the engine kit, and the AI Hub client.\n+- Read `TASK.md` and `PLAN.md`; downloaded the unmodified Pixel Engine 0.46.0 and AI Hub client into the development folder.\n+- Implemented activity catalog, unstable balance physics, scoring/progression primitives, and synthesized music data. Building the playable scenes and interface next.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH'","aggregated_output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA package.json\nA src/data/title.js\nA src/data/activities.js\nA src/core/dot.js\nA src/core/session.js\nA src/data/audio.js\nSuccess. Updated the following files:\nM PROGRESS.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
