{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'dotInstability|dotAuthority|dotDamping|dotNoise|dotLag|Source Information|exit-interview|Engine.start|new Engine' PLAN.md TASK.md 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'/examples -g '*.js' | head -28; sed -n '1,90p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/data/activities.js'; cat 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/package.json'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_102","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'dotInstability|dotAuthority|dotDamping|dotNoise|dotLag|Source Information|exit-interview|Engine.start|new Engine' PLAN.md TASK.md 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'/examples -g '*.js' | head -28; sed -n '1,90p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/data/activities.js'; cat 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/package.json'\"","aggregated_output":"TASK.md:92:## Source Information\nTASK.md:93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\nTASK.md:109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\nPLAN.md:6:- **Paths are relative to your dev folder.** \"Root\" means its parent, where your brief puts the deliverable html and the exit-interview file. Use the names your brief gives.\nPLAN.md:126:    const k = Math.min(1, dt / T.dotLag);\nPLAN.md:128:    const n = T.dotNoise * (m.noise ?? 1), inst = T.dotInstability * (m.inst ?? 1), auth = T.dotAuthority * (m.auth ?? 1);\nPLAN.md:131:    this.vx += (inst * this.x + auth * this.ux - T.dotDamping * this.vx + nx + (m.bx ?? 0)) * dt;\nPLAN.md:132:    this.vy += (inst * this.y + auth * this.uy - T.dotDamping * this.vy + ny + (m.by ?? 0)) * dt;\nPLAN.md:138:// Defaults: dotInstability 0.6, dotAuthority 3.0, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise 0.8, dotLag 0.08\nPLAN.md:274:- Defaults ✔ (simulated): effective instability 1.2 standing and 2.6 walking, so `m.inst = 1.2 / T.dotInstability` and `T.slackWalkInst / T.dotInstability`; `m.noise` 1.25; gusts every 6 m, `m.bx` ±1.6 for 1 s, telegraphed 1.5 s by flags and wind lines; fall at `|x| > 1`. Lock y (`dot.y = dot.vy = 0` after each step). Bots walk only while `|x| < .45`.\nPLAN.md:529:| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\nPLAN.md:587:const engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\nPLAN.md:591:If `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\nPLAN.md:768:src/main.js                                     boot: session check, Engine.start, first scene\nPLAN.md:785:- Start ✔: `Engine.start(new Boot(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), aspect: 'fill', touch: false, settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }, quality: info ? 'medium' : 'high', seed, background: PALETTE.sky, camera }))`.\nPLAN.md:940:Credits; \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"; **Source Information** (every field your brief lists; `unknown` for anything you can't confirm; Usage: `added on import`); **Testing Feedback**; **Engine Feedback**; **Prompt Feedback**; the kit's `CREDITS.md`, shipped as the kit asks: a summary page, then the full text in a scrollable view.\nPLAN.md:942:**Keep one source of truth:** `src/data/about.js` feeds the screen, and `tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview file from it, then re-parses it to confirm it is valid JSON. Answer the feedback questions honestly, from your real run, not from this plan.\nPLAN.md:944:For Source Information: Source is Wii Fit; Genre and Perspective as in section 1; Tech: Pixel Engine with its version, three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it, esbuild for packaging; Art: the engine's native pixel look; Animation: engine `ClipDef`s with `AnimationMixer`; Audio: engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant voice; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local. For Research, describe what you did yourself, and note that the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\nPLAN.md:957:It must contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as your brief says.\nPLAN.md:991:| Source Information and all feedback in the chat reply and About/Credits | §20 |\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/examples/looks.js:104:await Engine.start(new LookLab(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.3 }, look: STORYBOOK_HEROES }));\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/examples/side-scroller.js:167:await Engine.start(new CliffRun(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'side', zoom: 1.2 }, background: PALETTE.sky }));\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/examples/market.js:72:await Engine.start(new MarketCorner(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.6 } }));\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/examples/top-down.js:162:await Engine.start(new LanternNight(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'topdown', zoom: 1.1 }, look: LOOK_PRESETS.dream }));\nexport const ACTIVITIES = [\n  { id:'tree', name:'Apologetic Tree', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:1, duration:25, ring:.40, instruction:'KEEP YOUR DOT IN THE RING', quip:'THE TREE ACCEPTS YOUR APOLOGY.' },\n  { id:'heron', name:'Startled Heron', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:1, duration:25, ring:.36, instruction:'LEAN AGAINST THE WANDERING WIND', quip:'A MOST RESPECTABLE BIRD.' },\n  { id:'squats', name:'Squats of Regret', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:1, duration:38.4, instruction:'MATCH THE MOVING MARKER', quip:'THAT WAS THE LAST ONE. PROBABLY.' },\n  { id:'hoop', name:'Hoop Economics', family:'hoop', place:'Beat Beach', day:1, duration:40, instruction:'CIRCLE YOUR STICK OR ROLL W D S A', quip:'THE ECONOMY REMAINS CIRCULAR.' },\n  { id:'header', name:'Coconut Header', family:'header', place:'Beat Beach', day:2, duration:40, instruction:'LEAN LEFT OR RIGHT TO HEAD COCONUTS', quip:'A SOUND FINANCIAL HEADBUTT.' },\n  { id:'lunges', name:'Apology Lunges', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:2, duration:38.4, instruction:'MATCH THE MARKER AND ALTERNATE SIDES', quip:'YOUR LEGS HAVE BEEN NOTIFIED.' },\n  { id:'warrior', name:'Reluctant Warrior', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:2, duration:30, ring:.32, breath:8, instruction:'HOLD THE RING. BREATHE WITH THE BAR', quip:'A WARRIOR, UNDER PROTEST.' },\n  { id:'step', name:'Step Department', family:'step', place:'Town Square', day:3, duration:40, instruction:'PRESS F OR J WHEN NOTES HIT THE LINE', quip:'YOUR STEPS HAVE BEEN FILED.' },\n  { id:'slackline', name:'Slackline of Doubt', family:'slack', place:'Lookout', day:3, duration:45, instruction:'STAY CENTERED. STEP TO WALK', quip:'THE ROPE BELIEVES IN YOU.' },\n  { id:'chair', name:'The Chair Nobody Asked For', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:3, duration:30, ring:.30, breath:8, instruction:'HOLD THE RING. BREATHE WITH THE BAR', quip:'SOMEWHERE A CHAIR FEELS SEEN.' },\n  { id:'tray', name:'Vitamin Tray', family:'tray', place:'Cafe', day:4, duration:40, instruction:'KEEP THE VITAMINS ON THE TRAY', quip:'NUTRITION HAS NEVER BEEN SO TENSE.' },\n  { id:'mortgage', name:'Overhead Mortgage', family:'reps', place:'Rep Shed', day:4, duration:36, instruction:'PUSH UP TO MATCH THE MARKER', quip:'INTEREST COMPOUNDS. SO DOES SWEAT.' },\n  { id:'tax', name:'Tax Season', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:4, duration:30, ring:.28, breath:6, instruction:'LEAN AND BREATHE THROUGH THE AUDIT', quip:'YOUR EXTENSION HAS BEEN APPROVED.' },\n  { id:'jog', name:'Island Jog', family:'jog', place:'Island Trail', day:5, duration:45, instruction:'ALTERNATE F AND J TO RUN', quip:'YOU HAVE LAPSED A COCONUT.' },\n  { id:'pier', name:'Pier Jump', family:'jump', place:'Pier', day:5, duration:40, instruction:'STEP TO THE EDGE. BREATHE TO JUMP', quip:'THE WATER GIVES YOU A TEN.' },\n  { id:'plank', name:'Plank Negotiation', family:'still', place:'Pavilion', day:5, duration:35, ring:.24, breath:6, instruction:'KEEP THE DOT IN THE RING. BREATHE', quip:'YOUR CORE HAS COUNTEROFFERED.' },\n];\n\nexport const DAY_NAMES = ['A FRESH START','THE HEAD OF IT','A NARROW VIEW','WEALTH AND HEALTH','THE LONG WAY ROUND','A LITTLE MORE','THE LONG STAND'];\nexport const FRIENDS = ['COACH PLUMB','MABEL','FRANK','KEVIN'];\nexport function activityForDay(day) { return ACTIVITIES.filter(activity => activity.day <= Math.min(day, 5)); }\n{\"name\":\"a-little-off-balance\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"private\":true,\"type\":\"module\",\"scripts\":{\"build\":\"node tools/build.mjs\",\"test\":\"node tests/run.mjs\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
