{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; rg -n '\"'^#|ctx.scene|ambient|lighting|cameraTarget|class '\"' \\\"\"'$D/examples/market.js\" | head -30; sed -n '\"'1,72p' \\\"\"'$D/examples/market.js\"; sed '\"'s/}/}\\\\n/g' \\\"\"'$D/src/ui/style.css\" | tail -42; sed -n '\"'92,115p;145,175p' TASK.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_106","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"D='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; rg -n '\"'^#|ctx.scene|ambient|lighting|cameraTarget|class '\"' \\\"\"'$D/examples/market.js\" | head -30; sed -n '\"'1,72p' \\\"\"'$D/examples/market.js\"; sed '\"'s/}/}\\\\n/g' \\\"\"'$D/src/ui/style.css\" | tail -42; sed -n '\"'92,115p;145,175p' TASK.md\"","aggregated_output":"21:class MarketCorner {\n30:    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\n63:  cameraTarget() {\n// Market Corner: library models and the game's own fruit stall on a cobbled square at dusk.\n// Nothing to play: a scene to look at, and to build yours from (ASSETS.md).\nimport { addModelColliders, buildModel, DEFAULT_TEXEL, Engine, hudSprite, PALETTE, TEXTURE_LIBRARY, textureMap, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { MODELS } from './market-models.js';\n\nconst { Color, Mesh, PlaneGeometry, Vector3 } = THREE;\n\n// [id, position, options]: buildModel's options (params, palette, seed, light) and a turn in degrees\nconst SCENE = [\n  ['fruit-stall', [0, 0, -1.4]], // ours (market-models.js)\n  ['market-stall', [-4, 0, 0.6], { turn: 90, palette: { cloth: 'blue' } }], // re-coloured\n  ['lamp-post', [1, 0, 1.6], { light: { intensity: 10 } }], // it carries a light: brighter\n  ['well', [3.8, 0, -2.2]],\n  ['fence', [-0.5, 0, -3.4], { params: { length: 7 } }],\n  ['barrel', [-1.8, 0, 1.2]],\n  ['crate', [-1.1, 0, 1.7], { turn: 20 }],\n  ['sack', [2.4, 0, 1], { params: { h: 0.6 } }],\n  ['oak', [-3.2, 0, -3.4], { params: { h: 3 }, seed: 2 }],\n];\n\nclass MarketCorner {\n  name = 'Market Corner';\n  placed = [];\n  lights = [];\n  target = new Vector3(-0.3, 1, -0.9);\n\n  setup(ctx) {\n    const { scene, physics, engine } = ctx;\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.4; // dusk, so the lamp shows (the engine resets it for the next game)\n    engine.ambient.color.setHex(PALETTE.navy);\n    scene.background = new Color(PALETTE.night);\n\n    // The floor: a library surface on a plain mesh. A 32-texel tile at 8 texels a metre covers\n    // 4 m, so the UVs count tiles (the map is cached and shared: never scale it).\n    const tile = TEXTURE_LIBRARY.get('cobbles').size[0] / DEFAULT_TEXEL;\n    const ground = new PlaneGeometry(16, 16).rotateX(-Math.PI / 2);\n    ground.attributes.uv.array.forEach((v, i, uv) => (uv[i] = (v * 16) / tile));\n    const floor = new Mesh(ground, toonMaterial(PALETTE.white, { map: textureMap('cobbles') }));\n    floor.receiveShadow = true;\n    scene.add(floor);\n    physics.addStaticBox({ position: [0, -0.5, 0], halfExtents: [8, 0.5, 8] });\n\n    for (const [id, at, { turn = 0, ...options } = {}] of SCENE) {\n      const m = buildModel(id, { ...options, catalog: MODELS });\n      m.object.position.set(...at);\n      m.object.rotation.y = (turn * Math.PI) / 180;\n      m.object.updateMatrixWorld();\n      scene.add(m.object);\n      addModelColliders(physics, m, at, m.object.rotation.y);\n      // a model's light is in its own space: place it with the model\n      if (m.light) this.lights.push(ctx.lights.request({ ...m.light, position: m.object.localToWorld(new Vector3(...m.light.at)) }));\n      this.placed.push(m);\n    }\n    this.icon = hudSprite('gold-icon');\n  }\n\n  update(ctx) {\n    ctx.hud.clear();\n    ctx.hud.sprite(6, 6, this.icon.rows, this.icon.colors);\n    ctx.hud.text(26, 10, 'MARKET CORNER', { color: 'sand' });\n  }\n\n  cameraTarget() {\n    return this.target;\n  }\n\n  status() {\n    return `market: ${this.placed.length} models, ${this.lights.length} light`;\n  }\n}\n\nawait Engine.start(new MarketCorner(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso', zoom: 1.6 } }));\n.glass{padding:23px;border-radius:24px}\n.title{font-size:clamp(52px,15vw,72px);margin:20px 0 11px}\n.lede{font-size:14px}\n.menu{margin-top:18px}\n.button{min-height:49px}\n.hero-note{display:none}\n.fallback-island{width:100vw;height:35vw;right:-15%;top:8%}\n.fallback-island:after{left:43%;top:-60%}\n.island-screen{align-items:flex-end}\n.island-screen .panel{width:100%}\n.scroll-list{max-height:31vh}\n.game-hud{padding:14px}\n.game-title{max-width:70vw}\n.game-title small{font-size:9px}\n.game-bottom{align-items:flex-end}\n.balance-card{padding:10px;border-radius:18px}\n.balance-inner{gap:9px}\n.dial{width:120px}\n.balance-text{width:90px}\n.balance-text strong{font-size:15px}\n.balance-text p{font-size:10px}\n.game-tip{max-width:130px;font-size:10px;padding:9px}\n.touch-notice{top:12px;right:12px}\n.footnote{margin-top:14px}\n.heading{font-size:33px}\n}\n@media(max-height:600px) and (min-width:701px){.screen{padding:18px 35px}\n.glass{padding:22px}\n.title{font-size:55px;margin:12px 0}\n.lede{font-size:14px}\n.menu{margin-top:12px}\n.button{min-height:43px}\n.footnote{margin-top:12px}\n.scroll-list{max-height:34vh}\n}\n@media(max-width:360px){.balance-text{display:none}\n.game-tip{font-size:9px}\n.title{font-size:48px}\n.glass{padding:19px}\n.menu-row{gap:6px}\n}\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
