{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_256","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- required deliverables and interview ---\\\\n'; sed -n '35,150p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- screen flows ---\\\\n'; sed -n '30,95p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/main.js' | fold -s -w 190\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_256","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' PLAN.md; printf '\\\\n--- required deliverables and interview ---\\\\n'; sed -n '35,150p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- screen flows ---\\\\n'; sed -n '30,95p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/main.js' | fold -s -w 190\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Game plan: an original fitness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n13:## 1. The game\n21:### Pillars (use these to settle any open question)\n28:### What it takes from the source, and how it stays original\n47:## 2. World and cast\n64:## 3. Structure of play\n66:### Menu map\n80:### Starting a week\n84:### A day in The Week\n91:### The week\n103:### Progress\n113:## 4. The core: the Dot\n117:### The model ✔ (simulated with human-like bots; these are the defaults)\n143:### Lean input\n154:### Bots ✔\n183:## 5. Activities\n185:### Shared flow (`src/scenes/activity/base.js`)\n205:### 5.1 Holding Still (Pavilion, yoga)\n222:### 5.2 The Rep Shed (strength)\n239:### 5.3 Hoop Economics (Beat Beach, aerobics)\n250:### 5.4 Step Class (Beat Beach, rhythm)\n260:### 5.5 Coconut Header (Lagoon Games, balance)\n269:### 5.6 Slackline (Lagoon Games, balance)\n280:### 5.7 Vitamin Tray (Lagoon Games, balance)\n289:### 5.8 Island Jog (Jogging Path, aerobics)\n299:### 5.9 Pier Jump (Lagoon Games, balance)\n310:### 5.10 The Long Stand (finale, Day 7)\n333:## 6. Weigh-In and Wobble Age\n354:## 7. The island hub\n380:## 8. Writing\n434:## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n438:### Layout rules\n445:### Mixed-case text ✔\n473:### Input map\n493:### Prompts and glyphs\n498:### Screens\n505:### Pause menu\n511:### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\n515:### Touch-only devices\n521:## 10. Dev mode\n541:## 11. Attract mode\n552:## 12. Multiplayer\n556:### The Medley\n560:### On its own: Family Hour\n566:### In AI Hub: ghost mode\n604:## 13. Art direction\n610:### Avatars ✔\n646:### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n672:### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n678:### Surfaces and scene effects\n688:## 14. Animation\n717:## 15. Audio\n721:### Music\n738:### SFX\n742:### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n761:## 16. Architecture\n794:## 17. Verified recipes\n796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n818:### Browser flags ✔\n826:### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n830:### Screenshots ✔\n845:### Gamepad stub ✔\n856:### Hub harness ✔\n869:### Headless facts ✔\n879:## 18. Testing\n916:## 19. Build order\n934:## 20. Finishing\n938:### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\n946:### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\n955:### Your final chat reply\n961:## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n\n--- required deliverables and interview ---\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\n\n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n\n--- screen flows ---\n  if(app.screen==='title'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}<h1 class=\"title\">${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(0,2).join(' '))}<br><span>${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(2).join(' '))}.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">A week of \nmovement, a talking scale, and absolutely no pressure to be graceful.</p><div class=\"title-tag\">YOUR ISLAND IS READY</div>${notice()?`<p class=\"description\" \nstyle=\"margin-top:18px\"><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong></p><div class=\"menu\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}</div>`:`<div class=\"menu\">${button('Begin your \nweek','slots','','primary')}<div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Drop-in','dropin','','ghost')}${button('Family Hour','family','','ghost')}</div><div \nclass=\"menu-row\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}${button('About','about','','ghost')}</div></div>${footer()}`}`,'title-screen')+`<div class=\"hero-note\">WELCOME TO LITTLE \nISLAND<strong>Take it one wobble at a time.</strong>EST. WHENEVER YOU ARE READY</div>`;\n  }else if(app.screen==='slots'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">YOUR WEEK</span></div>${heading('A PLACE TO BEGIN','Who is stepping on?','Choose a profile. Your island remembers \nyour progress on this device.')}<div class=\"stack\">${app.profiles.map((item,index)=>`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"slot\" data-index=\"${index}\"><span \nclass=\"icon\">${index+1}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${item?escape(item.name):'Start a new week'}</span><span class=\"sub\">${item?`DAY ${item.day} · ${item.drips} DRIPS`:'EMPTY \nPROFILE'}</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`).join('')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='island'){\n    const player=profile(), day=Math.min(player.day,7), activities=activityForDay(day);\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge sun\">✦ ${player.drips} DRIPS</span></div>${heading(`DAY ${day} / 7 · ${DAY_NAMES[day-1]}`,'Good to see you. \n',`Ounce says: “${day===7?'Today, we stand together. And I owe you an explanation.':'The island is ready when you are.'}”`)}<div class=\"stats\"><span \nclass=\"badge\">${escape(player.name)}</span> <span class=\"badge\">${player.stars} STARS</span> <span class=\"badge\">WOBBLE AGE ${player.history.length?wobbleAge(player):'—'}</span></div><div \nclass=\"stack\"><button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"weigh\"><span class=\"icon\">◉</span><span><span class=\"name\">Daily weigh-in</span><span class=\"sub\">THREE LITTLE BALANCE \nCHECKS</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>${day===7?`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"finale\"><span class=\"icon\">✦</span><span><span class=\"name\">The Long \nStand</span><span class=\"sub\">YOUR WEEK FINALE</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`:''}</div><div class=\"eyebrow\" style=\"margin-top:20px\">PICK A PRACTICE · \n${activities.length} OPEN</div><div class=\"scroll-list stack\">${activities.map(activity=>`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"intro\" data-id=\"${activity.id}\"><span \nclass=\"icon\">${iconFor(activity.family)}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${escape(activity.name)}</span><span class=\"sub\">${escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())} · ${activity.duration} SEC \n${player.played[activity.id]?`· ${'★'.repeat(player.played[activity.id])}`:''}</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu-row\" \nstyle=\"margin-top:12px\">${button('Day report','day-report','','small')}${button('Settings','settings','','small ghost')}</div>${footer()}`,'island-screen');\n  }else if(app.screen==='intro'){\n    const activity=app.activity;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back(app.returnScreen||'island')}<span class=\"badge sun\">${escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())}</span></div>${heading('TODAY’S \nPRACTICE',escape(activity.name),escape(activity.instruction)+'.')}<div class=\"instruction-card\"><strong>LET’S KEEP IT SIMPLE</strong><p>Lean with the left stick or WASD. Press Space / R2 to \nbreathe; use F and J / L1 and R1 to step.</p><p>Find your own rhythm. Ounce is not a medical professional, despite the nametag.</p></div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Let’s \ngo','start','','primary')}${button(`Hard mode: ${app.hard?'ON':'OFF'}`,'hard','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='game'){\n    const activity=app.session.activity;\n    content=`<section class=\"screen game-screen\"><div class=\"game-hud\"><div class=\"game-top\"><div class=\"game-title\"><small>${app.attract?'ISLAND DEMO · PRESS ANY KEY TO \nPLAY':app.hubRound?'AI HUB · THREE-EVENT MEDLEY':escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())}</small><strong>${escape(activity.name)}</strong></div><div class=\"game-time\" \nid=\"seconds\">${Math.ceil(app.session.duration)}</div></div><div class=\"game-bottom\"><div class=\"balance-card\"><div class=\"balance-inner\"><div class=\"dial\" id=\"dial\" aria-label=\"Balance \nindicator\"><div class=\"dial-ring\"></div><div class=\"dot\" id=\"balance-dot\"></div></div><div class=\"balance-text\"><strong>Find your center.</strong><p id=\"live-score\">A little wobble is \nnormal.</p><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"meter\" style=\"width:0%\"></span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"game-tip\">${escape(activity.instruction)}<br><strong \nid=\"live-cue\"></strong><br><span class=\"key\">WASD / L</span> LEAN <span class=\"key\">SPACE / R2</span> BREATHE<br><span class=\"key\">F / J · L1 / R1</span> STEP · ESC \nPAUSE</div></div></div></section>`;\n  }else if(app.screen==='pause'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge\">TAKE YOUR TIME</span></div>${heading('PAUSED','A little breather.','Your island will be right here.')}<div \nclass=\"menu\">${button('Resume','resume','','primary')}${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}${button('Dev tools','dev','','ghost')}${button('Leave \npractice','leave','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='results'){\n    const result=app.result;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">PRACTICE COMPLETE</span></div>${heading('NICE WORK',escape(app.activity.name),escape(app.activity.quip||'THE ISLAND IS PROUD \nOF YOU.'))}<div class=\"score-hero\">${result.score}<small style=\"font-size:20px;color:#8ca397\"> / 100</small></div><div \nclass=\"stars\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars)}${'☆'.repeat(3-result.stars)}</div><div class=\"result-box\"><span>+ ${result.drips} DRIPS</span><span>${Math.round(result.seconds)} SECONDS OF YOU \nTIME</span></div><div class=\"menu\">${button(app.medley?'Next player / event':app.weigh?'Continue weigh-in':'Back to the \nisland','continue','','primary')}${!app.medley&&!app.weigh?button('Try again','start','','ghost'):''}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='weigh-result'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge\">DAILY CHECK-IN</span></div>${heading('A NUMBER, NOT A VERDICT','Your wobble age','Ounce has reviewed your three balance checks \nwith tremendous confidence.')}<div class=\"score-hero\">${wobbleAge(profile())}</div><p class=\"description\">This is just a playful score, not a measure of health. Keep moving at your own \npace.</p><div class=\"menu\">${button('Back to the island','island','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='day-report'){\n    const player=profile();\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('island')}<span class=\"badge sun\">DAY ${player.day}</span></div>${heading('YOUR DAY REPORT','Every wobble counts.',`You have collected \n${player.drips} drips and ${player.stars} stars. You showed up; the rest is gravy.`)}<div class=\"instruction-card\"><strong>OUNCE’S NOTE</strong><p>${player.day===6?'Tomorrow is the Long \nStand. Ounce seems unusually quiet.':player.day>=7?'The island is still yours to enjoy.':'A little movement is better than a perfectly planned nap. Usually.'}</p></div><div \nclass=\"menu\">${button(player.day>=7?'Back to the island':'Start the next day','next-day','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='reveal'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('THE LONG STAND','Ounce comes clean.','“I added seven years to everyone’s wobble age. I thought you would come back if the number worried you. That was \nwrong.”')}<p class=\"description\" style=\"margin-top:16px\">The island agrees: a number should never tell you your worth. Your wobble age is now honest, and the island remains open.</p><div \nclass=\"menu\">${button('A fresh start','island','','primary')}</div>`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='family'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">LOCAL MULTIPLAYER</span></div>${heading('PASS THE CONTROLLER','Family Hour','One to four players take turns \nthrough a three-event medley. Highest total wins; kindness is mandatory.')}<div class=\"stack\">${[1,2,3,4].map(number=>button(`${number} \n${number===1?'player':'players'}`,'family-start',`data-count=\"${number}\"`,number===2?'primary':'ghost')).join('')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='medley-board'){\n    const ranking=app.medley.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">FAMILY HOUR</span></div>${heading('MEDLEY COMPLETE','A standing ovation.','Every player gets a turn in the spotlight.')}<div \nclass=\"stack\">${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div class=\"list-item\"><span class=\"icon\">${index+1}</span><span><span class=\"name\">PLAYER ${entry.index+1}</span><span \nclass=\"sub\">${entry.score} POINTS</span></span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Back to title','title','','primary')}</div>`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='settings'||app.screen==='dev'){\n    const dev=app.screen==='dev';\n    const ranges=dev?Object.entries(app.tuning).map(([key,value])=>`<div class=\"field\"><label for=\"${key}\">${escape(key)}</label><input id=\"${key}\" data-tune=\"${key}\" type=\"range\" \nmin=\"${key==='timeScale'?.25:0}\" max=\"${key==='timeScale'?4:key==='dotLag'?.5:8}\" step=\".01\" value=\"${value}\"></div>`).join(''):`<div class=\"field\"><label for=\"music\">Music \n${Math.round(app.settings.music*100)}%</label><input id=\"music\" data-setting=\"music\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\".05\" value=\"${app.settings.music}\"></div><div class=\"field\"><label \nfor=\"effects\">Effects ${Math.round(app.settings.effects*100)}%</label><input id=\"effects\" data-setting=\"effects\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\".05\" \nvalue=\"${app.settings.effects}\"></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"glyphs\">Controller prompts</label><select id=\"glyphs\" data-setting=\"glyphs\"><option value=\"ps\" \n${app.settings.glyphs==='ps'?'selected':''}>PlayStation</option><option value=\"xbox\" ${app.settings.glyphs==='xbox'?'selected':''}>Xbox</option></select></div><div class=\"field\"><label \nfor=\"contrast\">High contrast</label><input id=\"contrast\" data-setting=\"contrast\" type=\"checkbox\" ${app.settings.contrast?'checked':''}></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"motion\">Reduce \nmotion</label><input id=\"motion\" data-setting=\"motion\" type=\"checkbox\" ${app.settings.motion?'checked':''}></div>`;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('settings-back')}<span class=\"badge\">${dev?'LIVE TUNING':'MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE'}</span></div>${heading(dev?'DEVELOPER TOOLS':'YOUR \nPREFERENCES',dev?'Tune the wobble.':'Settings',dev?'Changes apply immediately, including during a paused practice.':'Make the island feel like yours.')}<div \nclass=\"stack\">${ranges}</div><div class=\"menu\">${dev?button('Reset tuning','reset-tuning','','ghost'):''}${button('Done','settings-back','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='about'){\n    const section=(title,entries)=>`<h3>${title}</h3>${entries.map(entry=>`<p>${escape(entry)}</p>`).join('')}`;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">CREDITS</span></div>${heading('THE FINE PRINT','About the island','A Little Off Balance is a playful tribute, not \nmedical advice.')}<div class=\"about-text\">${section('Source Information',Object.entries(about.sourceInformation).map(([key,value])=>`${key}: ${value}`))}${section('Testing \nFeedback',about.testingFeedback)}${section('Engine Feedback',about.engineFeedback)}${section('Prompt Feedback',about.promptFeedback)}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='hub-card'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('AI HUB · GHOST MEDLEY','Ready to wobble?','Three events, one shared clock. Earn points and watch your fellow islanders as ghosts.')}<div \nclass=\"menu\">${button('Ready','hub-ready','','primary')}${button('I need more time','hub-more','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }\n  ui.innerHTML=content;\n  app.focus=0;\n  const first=ui.querySelector('button:not(:disabled)');if(first&&app.inputKind==='gamepad')first.classList.add('focused');\n}\n\nfunction go(screen){app.screen=screen;render();}\nfunction begin(activity,options={}){\n  app.activity=activity;app.session=new ActivitySession(activity,{hard:app.hard,tuning:app.tuning,...options});app.paused=false;go('game');\n}\nfunction finish(){\n  if(!app.session)return;\n  app.result=app.session.result();\n  if(app.attract){app.attractIndex++;startAttract();return;}\n  if(app.hubRound){advanceHub();return;}\n  \nif(app.weigh){app.weigh.push(app.result.score/100);if(app.weigh.length<3){startWeigh();return;}profile().history.push(...app.weigh);profile().history=profile().history.slice(-3);app.weigh=nu\nll;save();go('weigh-result');return;}\n  if(app.medley){app.medley.scores[app.medley.player]+=app.result.score;go('results');return;}\n  if(profile()){const \nplayer=profile();player.drips+=app.result.drips;player.stars+=Math.max(0,app.result.stars-(player.played[app.activity.id]||0));player.played[app.activity.id]=Math.max(app.result.stars,player\n.played[app.activity.id]||0);if(app.activity.id==='finale'){player.revealed=true;save();go('reveal');return;}save();}\n  sound.effect('good');go('results');\n}\nfunction startWeigh(){const index=app.weigh.length;const names=['Still water','A gentle shift','Chase the \nbreeze'];begin({...ACTIVITIES[0],id:['tree','heron','tax'][index],name:names[index],place:'Weigh-in',duration:8,ring:.38,instruction:['KEEP YOUR DOT IN THE RING','COUNTER THE DRIFT','STAY \nNEAR THE CENTER'][index]});}\nfunction startMedley(){const sequence=['tree','hoop','step'];const id=sequence[app.medley.event];begin({...ACTIVITIES.find(activity=>activity.id===id),name:`PLAYER ${app.medley.player+1} · \n${ACTIVITIES.find(activity=>activity.id===id).name}`},{duration:20});}\nfunction startAttract(){app.attract=true;const sequence=['tree','hoop','step','header','slackline'];const \nactivity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===sequence[app.attractIndex%sequence.length]);begin(activity,{duration:12});}\nfunction leaveAttract(){app.attract=false;app.session=null;app.lastInput=performance.now();go('title');}\nfunction act(action,element){\n  sound.unlock();sound.effect('select');app.lastInput=performance.now();\n  if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return;}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
