{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_309","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"ls -lh /tmp/viewport-matrix/alob | head -35; printf '\\\\n--- implementation interview ---\\\\n'; cat 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/data/about.js'; printf '\\\\n--- plan outline ---\\\\n'; rg -n '\"'^#|''^'\"\\\\*\\\\*' PLAN.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"total 5.9M\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 379K Nov  4 23:40 16-10-1440x900__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 240K Nov  4 23:40 16-10-1440x900__firefox.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 206K Nov  4 23:40 16-10-1440x900__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 605K Nov  4 23:40 16-9-1920x1080__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 316K Nov  4 23:40 16-9-1920x1080__firefox.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 268K Nov  4 23:40 16-9-1920x1080__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 776K Nov  4 23:40 21-9-2560x1080__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 357K Nov  4 23:40 21-9-2560x1080__firefox.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 303K Nov  4 23:40 21-9-2560x1080__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 252K Nov  4 23:40 4-3-1024x768__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 180K Nov  4 23:40 4-3-1024x768__firefox.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 156K Nov  4 23:40 4-3-1024x768__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 178K Nov  4 23:40 galaxy-tab-s9__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 329K Nov  4 23:40 galaxy-z-fold-7-open__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 8.7K Nov  4 23:40 index.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 137K Nov  4 23:40 ipad-mini__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 177K Nov  4 23:40 ipad-pro-11-landscape__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  84K Nov  4 23:40 iphone-17-pro-landscape__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  79K Nov  4 23:40 iphone-17-pro-max__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  67K Nov  4 23:40 iphone-17-pro__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  63K Nov  4 23:40 iphone-se__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 302K Nov  4 23:40 laptop-1366x768__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 213K Nov  4 23:40 laptop-1366x768__firefox.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 186K Nov  4 23:40 laptop-1366x768__webkit.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  84K Nov  4 23:40 pixel-10__chromium.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 7.9K Nov  4 23:40 report.json\n\n--- implementation interview ---\nexport const about = {\n  sourceInformation: {\n    date:'2026-11-04 22:18:46', source:'Wii Fit', plan:'PLAN.md', genre:'Sports',\n    perspective:'Isometric 3D island', tech:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, JavaScript, Web Audio',\n    artDirection:'Pastel, low-poly island and friendly, rounded fitness interface',\n    animation:'Procedural posing and three.js AnimationMixer',\n    audio:'Original procedural Web Audio music, effects, and syllabic character voice',\n    online:'AI Hub ghost session with score and position messages',\n    testing:'Automated simulation and browser checks; phone, tablet, desktop and WebKit viewport checks',\n    research:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 documentation and AI Hub session protocol',\n    environment:'Codex CLI (headless); Linux', model:'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max', usage:'added on import'\n  },\n  testingFeedback:['See final testing report.','See final testing report.','Simulation and real-browser interaction.','Static inspection without running the game.'],\n  engineFeedback:['The compact scene lifecycle and built-in camera.','WebGPU availability varies between browsers.','The balance physics, activities and UI.','Validating WebGPU behavior across browser engines.','None; pixel-engine.js remains unchanged.','Provide an explicit supported fallback for browsers without WebGPU.'],\n  promptFeedback:['The emphasis on a playable, controller-first vertical slice.','The scope combines a large simulation, multiplayer and a standalone deliverable.','Balancing the breadth of activities with cross-browser verification.','Prioritize required features and define an explicit minimum for each.'],\n  aiHub:{name:'A Little Off Balance',tagline:'A very serious game about a very wobbly week.',description:'Balance, breathe, and bravely face a talking scale on a cozy island. Play a week of delightfully questionable fitness or challenge friends in a three-event medley.',type:'Game',genre:'Sports',source:'Wii Fit',series:'Wii Fit',players:'1–4',controls:'Left stick / WASD: lean; R2 / Space: breathe; L1/R1 or F/J: step; Escape / Options: pause.',tags:['3d','sports','comedy','arcade','versus']}\n};\n\n--- plan outline ---\n1:# Game plan: an original fitness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n13:## 1. The game\n15:**A week at a spotless wellness island run by a small, polite, deeply judgmental bathroom scale. Your whole body is one dot. Keep it in the circle.**\n21:### Pillars (use these to settle any open question)\n28:### What it takes from the source, and how it stays original\n41:**Do not use** any Nintendo name, character, look, music, level or minigame name: no Wii, Mii, Balance Board, Wii Fit Trainer, Wuhu Island or Fit Age. No white-board host, no sound-alike tunes, no channel-style menus. Mechanics may rhyme; everything you can see, hear or read is new.\n43:**Taste rule:** no jokes about a real person's weight, body shape or eating, and no health claims. Ounce judges wobble, knees, posture and life choices, never bodies. The game asks for no real health data. The About screen says: \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"\n47:## 2. World and cast\n49:**Tare Island** (\"Everything here starts at zero.\") is a tiny resort whose landscape is exercise equipment at enormous scale: Kettlebell Volcano (dormant, mostly), Foam Roller Hills, the Dumbbell Bridge, medicine-ball boulders. A white-tiled plaza sits at its heart, ringed by lawn, sand and calm sea.\n60:**The story in one breath:** you arrive by ferry; Ounce weighs you and gives you an alarming Wobble Age. Through the week the classmates hint that something is off (\"Has anyone ever checked that scale?\"; Coach hangs her plumb line beside Ounce: \"You are leaning.\"; Kevin sits on Ounce and the dial reads 7). On Day 7 you face **The Long Stand**: 90 seconds of standing still while the whole island tries to distract you. Then Ounce confesses: *\"I have been adding seven. To everyone. For years. It felt motivating.\"* The chart of your week visibly slides down seven years. Credits. *\"See you tomorrow. Bring your knees.\"* Play continues as an open-ended Week 2.\n64:## 3. Structure of play\n66:### Menu map\n80:### Starting a week\n84:### A day in The Week\n91:### The week\n103:### Progress\n113:## 4. The core: the Dot\n117:### The model ✔ (simulated with human-like bots; these are the defaults)\n143:### Lean input\n154:### Bots ✔\n167:**Measured time in ring ✔** (35 s, 40 seeds, first 2 s not counted):\n179:**Stars for Dot scores: 45 / 70 / 90.** So at ring .30, doing nothing gets no stars, an average player ★, a good one ★★★. Keep this shape if you retune; the test suite guards it (section 18).\n183:## 5. Activities\n185:### Shared flow (`src/scenes/activity/base.js`)\n196:**Lane camera ✔ (3 mats):** `{ preset: 'fixed', position: [0, 2.3, 8.2], target: [0, 1.15, 0], fov: 30 }`, mats at x = -2.2, 0, 2.2, z = 0.8. **For 4 mats ✔:** position `[0, 3, 9.5]`, target `[0, 1, 0]`, fov 32, mats at x = -3, -1, 1, 3. Multiply the distance by `max(1, (16/9) / aspect)` so narrow windows don't clip the outer mats.\n198:**Staging rules ✔ (found in test renders):**\n203:**Lean body language:** after `mixer.update(dt)`, add the Dot to the pose: `torso.rotateZ(-dot.x * 0.18); torso.rotateX(-dot.y * 0.12); pelvis.position.x += dot.x * 0.05`. Outside the ring, add a tremble. Far outside, blend to the kit's `Teeter` clip. The player should be able to read the Dot from the body alone.\n205:### 5.1 Holding Still (Pavilion, yoga)\n222:### 5.2 The Rep Shed (strength)\n224:**You scrub the animation with the stick** ✔ (`action.paused = true; action.time = r * duration; mixer.update(0)`). A marker on a big vertical (or horizontal) track follows the tempo curve; you match it.\n239:### 5.3 Hoop Economics (Beat Beach, aerobics)\n241:**Circle the stick** (or the mouse, or roll W-D-S-A) to keep hoops up.\n250:### 5.4 Step Class (Beat Beach, rhythm)\n260:### 5.5 Coconut Header (Lagoon Games, balance)\n269:### 5.6 Slackline (Lagoon Games, balance)\n280:### 5.7 Vitamin Tray (Lagoon Games, balance)\n289:### 5.8 Island Jog (Jogging Path, aerobics)\n299:### 5.9 Pier Jump (Lagoon Games, balance)\n310:### 5.10 The Long Stand (finale, Day 7)\n333:## 6. Weigh-In and Wobble Age\n354:## 7. The island hub\n380:## 8. Writing\n382:**Voice:** short declarative sentences. Polite, clinical, caring, faintly wounding. A remark should sound like it came from a nurse who has read your file. Understatement over exclamation. Numbers delivered gently. Humour comes from what is implied. No sarcasm tags, no memes, no pop-culture references, no swearing. Respect the taste rule in section 1.\n384:**Format:** at most 3 lines of 52 characters. Write at least 120 lines beyond the samples: every activity needs lines for 0/1/2/3★, first time and repeat; plus barks for ring entry and exit, falls and streaks.\n386:**Samples, in voice. Use them, then write more like them.**\n423:**Morning questions** (three answers; they change only the remark, and Ounce files them):\n434:## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n436:**One UI for every device: the pixel HUD.** No DOM menus; same screens for pad, keyboard and mouse. Build a small kit in `src/ui/`.\n438:### Layout rules\n445:### Mixed-case text ✔\n473:### Input map\n493:### Prompts and glyphs\n498:### Screens\n505:### Pause menu\n511:### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\n515:### Touch-only devices\n521:## 10. Dev mode\n525:**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\n537:**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\n541:## 11. Attract mode\n552:## 12. Multiplayer\n554:**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\n556:### The Medley\n560:### On its own: Family Hour\n564:**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\n566:### In AI Hub: ghost mode\n593:**In a session:**\n604:## 13. Art direction\n606:**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\n608:**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\n610:### Avatars ✔\n646:### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n672:### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n678:### Surfaces and scene effects\n688:## 14. Animation\n692:**Conventions** (`HERO_RIG`): facing +Z. Arm X: -90 ahead, -180 overhead. Arm Z: out to the side (R negative, L positive). Forearm -X bends the elbow. Leg -X swings forward. Shin +X bends the knee. Foot +X points the toes. Pelvis `p` offsets, `r` tips the whole body. Torso +X bends forward.\n694:**Verified poses ✔** (`validateClip` clean, `analyzeClip` no problems, reviewed on contact sheets):\n711:**Still to author:** Press; StepL/StepR; header nod; flail; daze; bow; slow clap; sneeze; Coach's point and demonstration transitions; tuck and cannonball; judge raising a paddle; stepping onto Ounce; ferry disembark. Reuse kit clips: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run`, `Sit`, `LieIdle`, `Wave`, `Victory`, `Teeter`, `Hurt`, `Fall`, `GetUp`, and more (`HERO_CLIPS`).\n713:**Preview without a GPU ✔:** `tools/clip-sheet.mjs` uses `renderSheet(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip, { frames, views: ['front', 'side'], scale: 90, trails: false, skeleton: false })` → `{ width, height, data }`, written as a PNG with `node:zlib` (`deflateSync`, `crc32`). Look at every new pose once. Hide the hat and moustache first so you judge the real silhouette.\n717:## 15. Audio\n721:### Music\n738:### SFX\n742:### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n761:## 16. Architecture\n782:**Everything a designer would change is plain data in `src/data/`:** poses, exercises, charts, boards, schedules, lines, unlocks, stars. A new pose, chart, board or day needs no code. That is what lets the rest of the game be built out later with normal tools, together with the live sliders and their JSON export.\n784:**Engine patterns:**\n794:## 17. Verified recipes\n796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n818:### Browser flags ✔\n820:**Use all five.** With only the three in the machine notes, `renderer.capture()` failed: `mapAsync ... A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`.\n826:### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n830:### Screenshots ✔\n845:### Gamepad stub ✔\n856:### Hub harness ✔\n869:### Headless facts ✔\n879:## 18. Testing\n881:**One command: `node tools/test.mjs`** prints only failures and one count line (`212/212 passed`). `--fast` runs the Node tests only. Rerun only after changing what a test covers. Prefer scripts to screenshots. Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit. Keep at most two browsers open.\n883:**Headless (Node), seconds:**\n899:**Browser, on the built html via `file://`:**\n909:**Hub:**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
