 is in that range.\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:77:- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-78-- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-79-  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n--\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-92-after `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-93-\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:94:- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-95-  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-96-- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n--\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-109-- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-110-  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:111:- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-112-  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-113-  the game runs as it does on its own.\n--\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-139-\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-140-```js\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:141:AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-142-```\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-143-\n--\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-164-\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-165-Nothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:166:choices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-167-numbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-168-`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n--\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-182-\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-183-`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:184:`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-185-give or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-186-`start`.\n--\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-188-### Reporting\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-189-\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:190:- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-191-  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md-192-  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\nA Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md:193:- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n\n--- TASK INTERVIEW ---\n92:## Source Information\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n94-- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n95-- Source: the work it's based on\n96-- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n97-- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n98-- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n99-- Art Direction: style used\n100-- Animation: system used\n101-- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n102-- Online: network features used, or none\n103-- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n104-- Research: research done, or none\n105-- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n106-- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n107-- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n108-\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n110-{\n111:  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112-  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113-  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n114-  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n115-  \"aiHub\": {\n116-    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n117-    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n118-    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n119-    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n120-    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n121-    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n122-    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n123-    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n124-    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n125-    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n126-  }\n127-}\n128-The catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n129-\n130-Testing Feedback\n131-\n132-- How many issues did testing catch?\n133-- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n134-- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n135-- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n136-\n137-Engine Feedback\n138-\n139-- What did you like most about the engine?\n140-- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n141-- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n142-- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n143-- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n144-- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n145-\n146-Prompt Feedback\n147-\n148-- What did you like most about this prompt?\n149-- What was confusing?\n150-- What was the hardest thing to do?\n151-- What would you change in this prompt?\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
