{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_319","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\nname='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846.html'\nurl='http://127.0.0.1:39559/'+quote(name)\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n b=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'])\n page=b.new_page(viewport={'width':1440,'height':900}, device_scale_factor=1)\n page.goto(url,wait_until='load'); page.wait_for_selector('#world canvas', timeout=15000)\n page.locator('[data-action=\\\"slots\\\"]').click(); page.locator('[data-action=\\\"slot\\\"]').first.click(); page.locator('[data-action=\\\"intro\\\"][data-id=\\\"tree\\\"]').click(); page.locator('[data-action=\\\"start\\\"]').click(); page.wait_for_timeout(1500); page.screenshot(path='/tmp/alob-game.png'); print('screen:', page.evaluate('window.__GAME__.state().screen')); b.close()\nPY\nprintf '\\\\n--- PLAN STRUCTURE ---\\\\n'; rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' PLAN.md | head -110; printf '\\\\n--- HUB EVENTS ---\\\\n'; sed -n '130,225p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_319","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nfrom urllib.parse import quote\nname='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846.html'\nurl='http://127.0.0.1:39559/'+quote(name)\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n b=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'])\n page=b.new_page(viewport={'width':1440,'height':900}, device_scale_factor=1)\n page.goto(url,wait_until='load'); page.wait_for_selector('#world canvas', timeout=15000)\n page.locator('[data-action=\\\"slots\\\"]').click(); page.locator('[data-action=\\\"slot\\\"]').first.click(); page.locator('[data-action=\\\"intro\\\"][data-id=\\\"tree\\\"]').click(); page.locator('[data-action=\\\"start\\\"]').click(); page.wait_for_timeout(1500); page.screenshot(path='/tmp/alob-game.png'); print('screen:', page.evaluate('window.__GAME__.state().screen')); b.close()\nPY\nprintf '\\\\n--- PLAN STRUCTURE ---\\\\n'; rg -n '\"'^#{1,4} '\"' PLAN.md | head -110; printf '\\\\n--- HUB EVENTS ---\\\\n'; sed -n '130,225p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/README.md'\"","aggregated_output":"screen: game\n\n--- PLAN STRUCTURE ---\n1:# Game plan: an original fitness comedy inspired by Wii Fit\n13:## 1. The game\n21:### Pillars (use these to settle any open question)\n28:### What it takes from the source, and how it stays original\n47:## 2. World and cast\n64:## 3. Structure of play\n66:### Menu map\n80:### Starting a week\n84:### A day in The Week\n91:### The week\n103:### Progress\n113:## 4. The core: the Dot\n117:### The model ✔ (simulated with human-like bots; these are the defaults)\n143:### Lean input\n154:### Bots ✔\n183:## 5. Activities\n185:### Shared flow (`src/scenes/activity/base.js`)\n205:### 5.1 Holding Still (Pavilion, yoga)\n222:### 5.2 The Rep Shed (strength)\n239:### 5.3 Hoop Economics (Beat Beach, aerobics)\n250:### 5.4 Step Class (Beat Beach, rhythm)\n260:### 5.5 Coconut Header (Lagoon Games, balance)\n269:### 5.6 Slackline (Lagoon Games, balance)\n280:### 5.7 Vitamin Tray (Lagoon Games, balance)\n289:### 5.8 Island Jog (Jogging Path, aerobics)\n299:### 5.9 Pier Jump (Lagoon Games, balance)\n310:### 5.10 The Long Stand (finale, Day 7)\n333:## 6. Weigh-In and Wobble Age\n354:## 7. The island hub\n380:## 8. Writing\n434:## 9. UI and UX: 10 feet, controller first\n438:### Layout rules\n445:### Mixed-case text ✔\n473:### Input map\n493:### Prompts and glyphs\n498:### Screens\n505:### Pause menu\n511:### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\n515:### Touch-only devices\n521:## 10. Dev mode\n541:## 11. Attract mode\n552:## 12. Multiplayer\n556:### The Medley\n560:### On its own: Family Hour\n566:### In AI Hub: ghost mode\n604:## 13. Art direction\n610:### Avatars ✔\n646:### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n672:### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n678:### Surfaces and scene effects\n688:## 14. Animation\n717:## 15. Audio\n721:### Music\n738:### SFX\n742:### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n761:## 16. Architecture\n794:## 17. Verified recipes\n796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n818:### Browser flags ✔\n826:### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n830:### Screenshots ✔\n845:### Gamepad stub ✔\n856:### Hub harness ✔\n869:### Headless facts ✔\n879:## 18. Testing\n916:## 19. Build order\n934:## 20. Finishing\n938:### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\n946:### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\n955:### Your final chat reply\n961:## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n\n--- HUB EVENTS ---\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. By default the hub shows its own card over\nthe game. A game can make the card its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
