{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_335","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/vendor/hub/harness.html' | sed -n '1,200p'; printf '\\\\n--- hub setup ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'setupHub|hubRound|hubEvent|AIHub\\\\.send|AIHub\\\\.progress|hub\\\\.send|hub\\\\.progress|AIHub.time|hub\\\\.time' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/main.js'; printf '\\\\n--- plan hub ---\\\\n'; rg -n -C 3 'Hub Medley|55 seconds|55-second|network|harness|AIHub|hub medley' PLAN.md | tail -n 115\"","aggregated_output":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>AI Hub Session Harness</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Test a game against the AI Hub Session Protocol: 1–4 copies next to each other on a simulated network.\">\n<style>\n  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg: #0e0c14; --panel: #191623; --line: #2c2838; --ink: #ece8f4; --dim: #9a93ab; --ok: #4ade80; --bad: #f87171; --warn: #fbbf24; }\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; }\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); font: 14px/1.4 system-ui, sans-serif; }\n  body { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; }\n  header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 14px; align-items: center; padding: 8px 12px; background: var(--panel); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  header h1 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 8px 0 0; }\n  header label { color: var(--dim); display: inline-flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }\n  input, select, button { font: inherit; color: var(--ink); background: #241f31; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 8px; }\n  input[type=number] { width: 70px; }\n  input.game { width: 300px; }\n  button { cursor: pointer; }\n  button:hover { border-color: var(--dim); }\n  main { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 340px; min-height: 0; }\n  #grid { display: grid; gap: 6px; padding: 6px; min-height: 0; }\n  .cell { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border: 2px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; background: #000; }\n  .cell__bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; padding: 3px 8px; background: var(--panel); font-size: 12px; }\n  .cell__dot { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; }\n  .cell__state { margin-left: auto; color: var(--dim); }\n  .cell iframe { width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0; background: #000; }\n  .cell.is-out { opacity: .35; }\n  aside { display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto auto 1fr; min-height: 0; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--panel); }\n  aside section { padding: 8px 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }\n  aside h2 { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; color: var(--dim); margin: 0 0 6px; }\n  #checks li { list-style: none; }\n  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n  .ok::before { content: '✓ '; color: var(--ok); }\n  .bad::before { content: '✗ '; color: var(--bad); }\n  .wait::before { content: '… '; color: var(--warn); }\n  #log { overflow: auto; font: 12px/1.35 ui-monospace, monospace; padding: 8px 12px; margin: 0; white-space: pre-wrap; }\n  #round { white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 13px; }\n  .hint { color: var(--dim); }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<header>\n  <h1>AI Hub session harness</h1>\n  <label>Game <input class=\"game\" id=\"game\" placeholder=\"mygame.html or /games/mygame/index.html\"></label>\n  <label>Players <select id=\"players\"><option>1</option><option selected>2</option><option>3</option><option>4</option></select></label>\n  <label>Latency <input type=\"number\" id=\"latency\" min=\"0\" value=\"60\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Jitter <input type=\"number\" id=\"jitter\" min=\"0\" value=\"20\"> ms</label>\n  <label>Loss <input type=\"number\" id=\"loss\" min=\"0\" max=\"50\" value=\"0\"> %</label>\n  <button id=\"restart\" type=\"button\">New round</button>\n  <button id=\"release\" type=\"button\" title=\"End the splash now: the round starts once every game has loaded\">Start now</button>\n  <button id=\"timeup\" type=\"button\">Time up</button>\n  <label>Remove <select id=\"who\"></select></label>\n  <button id=\"remove\" type=\"button\">Remove player</button>\n  <button id=\"hide\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Hide host tab</button>\n</header>\n<main>\n  <div id=\"grid\"><p class=\"hint\" style=\"padding:16px\">Name a game above (a path or URL served alongside this page), then press New round. Click a player's frame to control that player.</p></div>\n  <aside>\n    <section><h2>Round</h2><div id=\"round\" class=\"hint\">No round yet.</div></section>\n    <section id=\"checks\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\"checklist\"><li class=\"hint\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\n    <pre id=\"log\" aria-live=\"off\"></pre>\n  </aside>\n</main>\n<script type=\"module\">\nimport { createBridge, attachFrame, postTo, createLocalNetwork } from './bridge.js';\nimport { createRound, limitFor, modeOf, seedsRandom, SELF_REPORTED, TIMINGS } from './round.js';\n\nconst NAMES = ['Red Fox', 'Blue Otter', 'Green Heron', 'Gold Lynx'];\nconst params = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nconst $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);\nconst auto = params.get('auto') === '1';\nconst scenario = params.get('scenario') || 'standard';\n/** ?scenario=server: the shared world runs on one more copy with no player of its own, as a dedicated server would run it. */\nconst serverMode = scenario === 'server';\nconst playMs = Number(params.get('play')) || 6000;\nconst SPLASH_MS = 10_000;\n\nfor (const [id, key] of [['game', 'game'], ['players', 'players'], ['latency', 'latency'], ['jitter', 'jitter'], ['loss', 'loss']]) {\n  if (params.has(key)) $(id).value = params.get(key);\n}\n\nconst net = createLocalNetwork({});\nlet current = null;\nlet roundNo = 0;\nconst logLines = [];\nfunction log(text) {\n  const t = (performance.now() / 1000).toFixed(2).padStart(7);\n  logLines.push(`${t}  ${text}`);\n  if (logLines.length > 400) logLines.splice(0, logLines.length - 400);\n  $('log').textContent = logLines.join('\\n');\n  $('log').scrollTop = $('log').scrollHeight;\n}\n\n/** The game's head metas, when the page can be fetched from here. */\nasync function metasOf(url) {\n  try {\n    const html = await (await fetch(url)).text();\n    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(html, 'text/html');\n    const meta = (name) => doc.querySelector(`meta[name=\"${name}\"]`)?.getAttribute('content')?.trim() ?? null;\n    return {\n      session: meta('hub:session'),\n      players: meta('hub:session-players'),\n      mode: meta('hub:session-mode'),\n      minutes: meta('hub:session-minutes'),\n    };\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * For a game tagged parallel or ghost, the seed rides in the address: the client seeds Math.random with it before the game's scripts run.\n * Only a page of this site is loaded: ?game= comes from the address bar, and a javascript: or another site's\n * address in an unsandboxed frame would run as this origin, where a signed-in player's session is kept.\n */\nconst gameUrl = (game, { tag, seed } = {}) => {\n  let url;\n  try {\n    url = new URL(game, location.href);\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n  if (url.origin !== location.origin || !/^https?:$/.test(url.protocol)) return null;\n  url.searchParams.set('aihub', '1');\n  if (seedsRandom(tag)) url.searchParams.set('aihub-seed', String(seed >>> 0));\n  return url.href;\n};\n\nfunction applyNet() {\n  Object.assign(net.settings, {\n    latency: Math.max(0, Number($('latency').value) || 0),\n    jitter: Math.max(0, Number($('jitter').value) || 0),\n    loss: Math.min(0.5, Math.max(0, (Number($('loss').value) || 0) / 100)),\n  });\n}\n\n/** Wrap what a game must not call in hub mode, where the page can reach it. */\nfunction instrument(cell) {\n  try {\n    const win = cell.frame.contentWindow;\n    for (const name of ['alert', 'confirm', 'prompt', 'open']) {\n      const original = win[name];\n      win[name] = (...args) => {\n        cell.violations.push(`${name}() called`);\n        log(`${cell.name}: ${name}() called — not allowed in a session`);\n        return name === 'confirm' ? false : name === 'prompt' ? null : undefined;\n      };\n      void original;\n    }\n    win.addEventListener('error', (e) => cell.violations.push(`error: ${e.message}`));\n    win.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => cell.violations.push(`unhandled rejection: ${e.reason?.message || e.reason}`));\n  } catch {\n    cell.instrumented = false;\n  }\n}\n\nasync function newRound() {\n  endCurrent();\n  applyNet();\n  const game = $('game').value.trim();\n  if (!game) return null;\n  if (!gameUrl(game)) {\n    log(`Not loading ${game}: the harness only plays pages from this site.`);\n    return null;\n  }\n  const n = Math.max(1, Math.min(4, Number($('players').value) || 2));\n  const metas = await metasOf(game);\n  const mode = modeOf(metas?.mode);\n  const limitMs = params.has('limit') ? Number(params.get('limit')) * 1000 : limitFor(metas?.minutes);\n  const seed = params.has('seed') ? Number(params.get('seed')) >>> 0 : crypto.getRandomValues(new Uint32Array(1))[0];\n  const round = ++roundNo;\n  const players = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, slot) => ({ key: `p${slot}`, slot, name: NAMES[slot] }));\n  const hubEnd = net.endpoint('hub');\n  const grid = $('grid');\n  grid.replaceChildren();\n  const copies = n + (serverMode ? 1 : 0);\n  grid.style.gridTemplateColumns = copies > 1 ? '1fr 1fr' : '1fr';\n  grid.style.gridTemplateRows = `repeat(${Math.ceil(copies / (copies > 1 ? 2 : 1))}, 1fr)`;\n\n  const state = { round, n, metas, mode, limitMs, seed, players, cells: [], hubEnd, status: null, record: null, hidden: false, splashUntil: performance.now() + SPLASH_MS, answers: { ready: new Set(), more: new Set() } };\n  current = state;\n  log(`round ${round}: ${n} player${n > 1 ? 's' : ''}, seed ${seed}, limit ${Math.round(limitMs / 1000)} s, mode ${mode || '(from hello)'}`);\n\n  state.coordinator = createRound({\n    round,\n    players,\n    hostKey: 'p0',\n    serverKey: serverMode ? 'server' : null,\n    mode,\n    seed,\n    limitMs,\n    gate: true,\n    deliver: (key, m) => hubEnd.send(key, { k: 'h', r: round, m }),\n    onStatus: (s) => { state.status = s; render(state); },\n    onEnd: (record) => {\n      state.record = record;\n      log(`round ${round} ${record.status}: ${record.reason}${record.standings ? ' — standings ' + JSON.stringify(record.standings) : ''}`);\n      render(state);\n    },\n\n--- hub setup ---\n12:const app={screen:'title',session:null,settings:{music:.1,effects:.7,glyphs:'ps',contrast:false,motion:false,...stored('alob-settings',{})},profiles:stored('alob-profiles',[null,null,null]),slot:0,activity:null,result:null,tuning:{...DEFAULT_TUNABLES},input:{x:0,y:0,breath:false,left:false,right:false},keys:new Set(),lastInput:performance.now(),inputKind:'keyboard',focus:0,paused:false,attract:false,attractIndex:0,medley:null,weigh:null,hubRound:false,hubEnded:false,hubScores:{},hubClock:0,gamepadButtons:[],driver:null};\n42:    content=`<section class=\"screen game-screen\"><div class=\"game-hud\"><div class=\"game-top\"><div class=\"game-title\"><small>${app.attract?'ISLAND DEMO · PRESS ANY KEY TO PLAY':app.hubRound?'AI HUB · THREE-EVENT MEDLEY':escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())}</small><strong>${escape(activity.name)}</strong></div><div class=\"game-time\" id=\"seconds\">${Math.ceil(app.session.duration)}</div></div><div class=\"game-bottom\"><div class=\"balance-card\"><div class=\"balance-inner\"><div class=\"dial\" id=\"dial\" aria-label=\"Balance indicator\"><div class=\"dial-ring\"></div><div class=\"dot\" id=\"balance-dot\"></div></div><div class=\"balance-text\"><strong>Find your center.</strong><p id=\"live-score\">A little wobble is normal.</p><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"meter\" style=\"width:0%\"></span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"game-tip\">${escape(activity.instruction)}<br><strong id=\"live-cue\"></strong><br><span class=\"key\">WASD / L</span> LEAN <span class=\"key\">SPACE / R2</span> BREATHE<br><span class=\"key\">F / J · L1 / R1</span> STEP · ESC PAUSE</div></div></div></section>`;\n83:  if(app.hubRound){advanceHub();return;}\n125:function pause(){if(app.screen==='game'&&!app.attract&&!app.hubRound){app.paused=true;go('pause');}else if(app.screen==='pause')act('resume');}\n157:    if(app.hubRound&&globalThis.AIHub.time()<0){if(seconds)seconds.textContent=`${Math.ceil(-globalThis.AIHub.time()/1000)}`;app.input.left=false;app.input.right=false;requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n170:    if(dial&&app.hubRound){dial.querySelectorAll('.ghost-dot').forEach(node=>node.remove());for(const ghost of Object.values(app.hubScores).slice(0,3)){if(!Number.isFinite(ghost?.x)||!Number.isFinite(ghost?.y))continue;const marker=document.createElement('span');marker.className='ghost-dot';marker.style.left=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,ghost.x))*38}%`;marker.style.top=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,ghost.y))*38}%`;dial.appendChild(marker);}}\n171:    if(app.hubRound&&now-app.hubClock>500){app.hubClock=now;const partial=app.hubTotal+app.session.result().score;globalThis.AIHub?.progress({score:partial,label:app.activity.name});globalThis.AIHub?.send({x:app.session.dot.x,y:app.session.dot.y,score:partial});}\n177:function advanceHub(){if(app.hubEnded)return;app.hubTotal+=app.session.result().score;app.hubEvent++;if(app.hubEvent>=3){app.hubEnded=true;globalThis.AIHub?.result({score:app.hubTotal});app.result={...app.session.result(),score:app.hubTotal,stars:0,drips:0};app.hubRound=false;go('results');}else begin({...ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===['tree','hoop','step'][app.hubEvent])},{duration:20});}\n178:function setupHub(){const hub=globalThis.AIHub;if(!hub?.active)return;hub.on('card',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;go('hub-card');});hub.on('start',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;app.hubRound=true;app.hubEnded=false;app.hubScores={};app.hubEvent=0;app.hubTotal=0;begin({...ACTIVITIES[0]},{duration:20});});hub.on('message',(data,from)=>{app.hubScores[from]=data;});hub.on('time-up',()=>{if(app.hubRound&&!app.hubEnded){const result=app.hubTotal+(app.session?.result().score||0);app.hubEnded=true;hub.result({score:result});app.result={...app.session.result(),score:result,stars:0,drips:0};app.hubRound=false;go('results');}});hub.on('end',()=>{app.hubRound=false;app.hubEnded=true;app.hubClosed=true;sound.context?.suspend();});hub.connect({mode:'ghost',seats:[1,4],card:true});hub.ready();}\n180:render();setupHub();startWorld(app).catch(error=>{console.warn('3D island unavailable:',error.message);});requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n\n--- plan hub ---\n551-\n552-## 12. Multiplayer\n553-\n554:**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\n555-\n556-### The Medley\n557-\n--\n583-\n584-```js\n585-let info = null;\n586:if (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n587-const engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\n588:if (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\n589-```\n590-\n591:If `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\n592-\n593-**In a session:**\n594:- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n595:- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\n596:- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\n597:- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\n598-- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\n599:- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\n600-- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\n601-\n602----\n--\n760-\n761-## 16. Architecture\n762-\n763:Download the kit (the URL is in your brief) and copy the contents of the zip's top-level `pixel-engine/` folder into the dev folder, so `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs` and the guides sit at its root. **Never edit `pixel-engine.js`**: record its sha256 in `vendor/pixel-engine.sha256` when you unzip, and a test compares it. Fetch the hub's `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and `README.md` into `vendor/hub/` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`.\n764-\n765-```\n766-pixel-engine.js  check.mjs  GUIDE.md ...        the kit, untouched\n767:vendor/hub/                                     hub client and harness, untouched\n768-src/main.js                                     boot: session check, Engine.start, first scene\n769-src/app.js                                      App: scene switching, save, settings, tunables, device, debug API\n770-src/core/      dot.js drivers.js actions.js device.js tunables.js save.js net.js clock.js\n--\n793-\n794-## 17. Verified recipes\n795-\n796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n797-\n798-```js\n799-// tools/build.mjs (esbuild is on this machine)\n--\n853-\n854-Read inputs through a frame: `moveAxis()` gave (0.8, 0.6) for axes (0.8, -0.6) in-game. Headless, `e.input.setKey('PadCross', true)` works without any stub ✔.\n855-\n856:### Hub harness ✔\n857-\n858:Copy the built html (as `game.html`) with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a temp folder inside the dev folder. Serve it with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` ✔, reading the port from its first output line and stopping it by its PID. An in-process `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1` and port 0 also works, but it must send `Content-Type: text/javascript` for `.js`, or the harness's module imports fail. Then for each of:\n859-\n860-```\n861:harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=1\n862:harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\n863:harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n864:harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n865-```\n866-\n867-wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`; print failed checks' `name` and `detail`. Each took 10-13 s with a light scene. Keep the card scene light so `ready()` lands inside the 20 s limit even with 4 software-rendered copies. Confirm the served page is yours (its title) before trusting a result. Then open the game outside a session and check it still runs.\n--\n908-\n909-**Hub:**\n910-\n911:21. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`. Each harness frame is a separate copy of the game, which covers the brief's \"no second player\" note.\n912:22. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\n913-\n914----\n915-\n--\n917-\n918-Finish each step with its tests green. Keep the game runnable and the deliverable building from step 1 on.\n919-\n920:1. **Skeleton.** Kit and hub files, build script, test runner, boot scene on `file://`, harness passing with a stub round. Takes minutes, because the recipes above are proven.\n921-2. **The Dot and the kit.** Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables; font, menu, dialogue, prompts, glyphs; App, scene switching, save; Settings; pause; dev sliders.\n922-3. **One activity, fully.** Holding Still end to end with avatars, Coach, results, voice and music. **Stop and judge the feel here**, since this is the whole game in miniature: check the bot table, then capture a run as frames and confirm the body language reads the Dot.\n923-4. **The island and the week.** Hub, Weigh-In, stations, Report, Jar, schedule, saves. Scripted playthrough started.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
