{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_461","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '80,200p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- harness interface ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'harness|hubClosed|hubRound|__GAME__|AIHub\\\\.time' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/main.js'; printf '\\\\n--- build ---\\\\n'; cat 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/tools/build.mjs'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_461","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '80,200p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- harness interface ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'harness|hubClosed|hubRound|__GAME__|AIHub\\\\.time' 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/src/main.js'; printf '\\\\n--- build ---\\\\n'; cat 'A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846/tools/build.mjs'\"","aggregated_output":"Narrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- harness interface ---\n13:const app={screen:'title',session:null,settings:{music:.1,effects:.7,glyphs:'ps',contrast:false,motion:false,...stored('alob-settings',{})},profiles:stored('alob-profiles',[null,null,null]),slot:0,activity:null,result:null,tuning:{...DEFAULT_TUNABLES},input:{x:0,y:0,breath:false,left:false,right:false},keys:new Set(),lastInput:performance.now(),inputKind:'keyboard',focus:0,paused:false,attract:false,attractIndex:0,medley:null,weigh:null,hubRound:false,hubEnded:false,hubScores:{},hubClock:0,gamepadButtons:[],driver:null};\n43:    content=`<section class=\"screen game-screen\"><div class=\"game-hud\"><div class=\"game-top\"><div class=\"game-title\"><small>${app.attract?'ISLAND DEMO · PRESS ANY KEY TO PLAY':app.hubRound?'AI HUB · THREE-EVENT MEDLEY':escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())}</small><strong>${escape(activity.name)}</strong></div><div class=\"game-time\" id=\"seconds\">${Math.ceil(app.session.duration)}</div></div><div class=\"game-bottom\"><div class=\"balance-card\"><div class=\"balance-inner\"><div class=\"dial\" id=\"dial\" aria-label=\"Balance indicator\"><div class=\"dial-ring\"></div><div class=\"dot\" id=\"balance-dot\"></div></div><div class=\"balance-text\"><strong>Find your center.</strong><p id=\"live-score\">A little wobble is normal.</p><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"meter\" style=\"width:0%\"></span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"game-tip\">${escape(activity.instruction)}<br><strong id=\"live-cue\"></strong><br><span class=\"key\">WASD / L</span> LEAN <span class=\"key\">SPACE / R2</span> BREATHE<br><span class=\"key\">F / J · L1 / R1</span> STEP · ESC PAUSE</div></div></div></section>`;\n86:  if(app.hubRound)return;\n128:function pause(){if(app.screen==='game'&&!app.attract&&!app.hubRound){app.paused=true;go('pause');}else if(app.screen==='pause')act('resume');}\n129:window.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(app.hubClosed)return;const wasNotice=notice();app.keyboardSeen=true;app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='keyboard';sound.unlock();if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return;}if(app.screen==='title'&&wasNotice)render();const key=event.key.toLowerCase();if(['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright',' ','escape'].includes(key))event.preventDefault();if(event.repeat)return;if(app.screen==='hub-card'&&(key==='enter'||key==='m')){event.preventDefault();globalThis.AIHub?.answer(key==='m'?'more':'ready');return;}app.keys.add(key);if(app.screen==='game'){if(key==='f')app.input.left=true;if(key==='j')app.input.right=true;if(key==='escape')pause();}else if(!['INPUT','SELECT'].includes(document.activeElement?.tagName)){if(key==='arrowdown'||key==='s')menuMove(1);else if(key==='arrowup'||key==='w')menuMove(-1);else if(key==='enter'){event.preventDefault();const buttons=Array.from(ui.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled)'));buttons[app.focus]?.click();}else if(key==='escape'){const backButton=ui.querySelector('.back');if(backButton)backButton.click();else if(app.screen==='pause')pause();}}});\n155:  if(app.hubClosed){requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n160:    if(app.hubRound&&!syncHub()){app.input.left=false;app.input.right=false;requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n173:    if(dial&&app.hubRound){dial.querySelectorAll('.ghost-dot').forEach(node=>node.remove());for(const ghost of Object.values(app.hubScores).slice(0,3)){if(ghost?.a!==app.hubEvent||!Number.isFinite(ghost?.x)||!Number.isFinite(ghost?.y))continue;const marker=document.createElement('span');marker.className='ghost-dot';marker.style.left=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,ghost.x))*38}%`;marker.style.top=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,ghost.y))*38}%`;dial.appendChild(marker);}}\n174:    if(app.session.finished&&!app.hubRound)finish();\n181:function finishHub(){if(!app.hubRound||app.hubEnded)return;const score=hubScore();app.hubEnded=true;app.hubRound=false;clearInterval(app.hubTimer);globalThis.AIHub.result({score});app.result={score};go('hub-finished');}\n183:  const window=medleyWindow(globalThis.AIHub.time());\n194:function sendHubState(){if(!app.hubRound||app.hubEnded||!app.session)return;const hub=globalThis.AIHub,score=hubScore();hub.progress({score,label:app.activity.name});hub.send({a:app.hubEvent,x:app.session.dot.x,y:app.session.dot.y,c:0,t:app.session.elapsed,s:score},{reliable:false});}\n195:function setupHub(){const hub=globalThis.AIHub;if(!hub?.active)return;hub.on('card',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;go('hub-card');});hub.on('start',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;app.hubRound=true;app.hubEnded=false;app.hubScores={};app.hubTotal=0;app.hubPicks=pickMedley(hub.rng('medley'));beginHubEvent(0);clearInterval(app.hubTimer);sendHubState();app.hubTimer=setInterval(sendHubState,100);});hub.on('message',(data,from)=>{app.hubScores[from]=data;});hub.on('time-up',finishHub);hub.on('end',()=>{clearInterval(app.hubTimer);app.hubRound=false;app.hubEnded=true;app.hubClosed=true;sound.context?.suspend();});hub.connect({mode:'ghost',seats:[1,4],card:true}).then(info=>{if(info)hub.ready();});}\n196:window.__GAME__={go:(screen,args={})=>{if(args.id)app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===args.id);if(screen==='game'&&app.activity)begin(app.activity);else go(screen);},state:()=>({screen:app.screen,day:profile()?.day,activity:app.activity?.id,elapsed:app.session?.elapsed,score:app.session?.result().score,attract:app.attract,profiles:app.profiles,hubScores:app.hubScores}),setDriver:skill=>{app.driver=skill;},get tunables(){return app.tuning;},finishActivity:()=>{if(app.session){app.session.elapsed=app.session.duration;app.session.finished=true;finish();}}};\n\n--- build ---\nimport {readFileSync,writeFileSync,mkdirSync} from 'node:fs';\nimport {execFileSync} from 'node:child_process';\nimport {TITLE} from '../src/data/title.js';\nimport {about} from '../src/data/about.js';\n\nmkdirSync('.build',{recursive:true});\nexecFileSync('esbuild',['src/main.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--platform=browser','--target=esnext','--charset=utf8','--outfile=.build/game.js','--log-level=warning'],{stdio:'inherit'});\nconst safe=source=>source.replace(/<\\/script/gi,'<\\\\/script');\nconst css=readFileSync('src/ui/style.css','utf8')+readFileSync('src/ui/overrides.css','utf8');\nconst hub=safe(readFileSync('vendor/hub/session.js','utf8'));\nconst game=safe(readFileSync('.build/game.js','utf8'));\nconst html=`<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><script>${hub}</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#cbe9dc\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three delightfully wobbly events.\"><meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick or WASD: lean. R2 or Space: breathe. L1/R1 or F/J: step.\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n<title>${TITLE}</title><style>${css}</style></head>\n<body><div id=\"world\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><div class=\"fallback-island\"><i></i><b></b><em></em></div></div><div id=\"ui\"><main class=\"loading\">A little moment, please<span>● ● ●</span></main></div><script type=\"module\">${game}</script></body></html>`;\nwriteFileSync(`../${TITLE}-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846.html`,html);\nwriteFileSync('../exit-interview.json',JSON.stringify(about,null,2)+'\\n');\nconsole.log(`Built standalone HTML (${(Buffer.byteLength(html)/1048576).toFixed(1)} MB).`);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
