{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_633","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; sed -n '1,240p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- ABOUT SOURCE ---\\\\n'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/about.js\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- GAMEPLAY / FAMILY ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'medley|family|ABOUT|About|TITLE' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\" | head -120; printf '\"'\\\\n--- PROGRESS ---\\\\n'; cat PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_633","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; sed -n '1,240p' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- ABOUT SOURCE ---\\\\n'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/about.js\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- GAMEPLAY / FAMILY ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'medley|family|ABOUT|About|TITLE' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\" | head -120; printf '\"'\\\\n--- PROGRESS ---\\\\n'; cat PROGRESS.md\"","aggregated_output":"SOURCE: Wii Fit\n\nGenre: Pick the game genre(s) that best fit the source and would make the best game.\n\nPerspective: Pick the camera perspective(s) that best fit the genre and source and would make the best game.\n\nGame Title: A playful riff on SOURCE's name. Silently brainstorm 50 titles, then pick one with a real random number generator (e.g., run code).\n\nResearch: Whether and how much to research is your choice.\n\nPackage: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n\nTech Stack: Build on https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, the riftlight engine kit. Keep the engine (pixel-engine.js) as it ships, as its guide says, and add whatever systems, art assets and animations the game needs on top of it. The rest of the tech stack is your choice.\n\nArt Direction: Use the engine’s native style as the base. Make new art assets for whatever makes the game feel like the source; the engine’s asset library is fine for generic props.\n\nAnimation: Use the engine’s native animation system as the base. Make new animations for whatever makes the game feel like the source.\n\nAudio: All music, sound effects and voices are written in code, with no audio files. Voices are Animalese/Simlish-style gibberish. Music is to be set to 10% volume by default.\n\nOnline: https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub\n\nWorking Environment and deliverable:\nCreate a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n\nPerformance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n\nTesting: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\nEffort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n\n## This computer\nChecked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\n\n- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\n- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\n- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\n- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\n  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\n- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\n- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\n- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\n- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\n\n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer\n\n- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n\n## Goal\n\nBuild an original game inspired by the source.\n\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- ABOUT SOURCE ---\nexport const about = {\n  sourceInformation: {\n    date:'2026-11-04 22:18:46', source:'Wii Fit', plan:'PLAN.md', genre:'Sports',\n    perspective:'Isometric 3D island', tech:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, JavaScript, Web Audio',\n    artDirection:'Pastel, low-poly island and friendly, rounded fitness interface',\n    animation:'Procedural posing and three.js AnimationMixer',\n    audio:'Original procedural Web Audio music, effects, and syllabic character voice',\n    online:'AI Hub ghost session with score and position messages',\n    testing:'Automated simulation and browser checks; phone, tablet, desktop and WebKit viewport checks',\n    research:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 documentation and AI Hub session protocol',\n    environment:'Codex CLI (headless); Linux', model:'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max', usage:'added on import'\n  },\n  testingFeedback:['See final testing report.','See final testing report.','Simulation and real-browser interaction.','Static inspection without running the game.'],\n  engineFeedback:['The compact scene lifecycle and built-in camera.','WebGPU availability varies between browsers.','The balance physics, activities and UI.','Validating WebGPU behavior across browser engines.','None; pixel-engine.js remains unchanged.','Provide an explicit supported fallback for browsers without WebGPU.'],\n  promptFeedback:['The emphasis on a playable, controller-first vertical slice.','The scope combines a large simulation, multiplayer and a standalone deliverable.','Balancing the breadth of activities with cross-browser verification.','Prioritize required features and define an explicit minimum for each.'],\n  aiHub:{name:'A Little Off Balance',tagline:'A very serious game about a very wobbly week.',description:'Balance, breathe, and bravely face a talking scale on a cozy island. Play a week of delightfully questionable fitness or challenge friends in a three-event medley.',type:'Game',genre:'Sports',source:'Wii Fit',series:'Wii Fit',players:'1–4',controls:'Left stick / WASD: lean; R2 / Space: breathe; L1/R1 or F/J: step; Escape / Options: pause.',tags:['3d','sports','comedy','arcade','versus']}\n};\n\n--- GAMEPLAY / FAMILY ---\n6:import { TITLE } from './data/title.js';\n7:import { EVENT_SECONDS, BREAK_SECONDS, pickMedley, medleyWindow } from './data/medley.js';\n13:const app={screen:'title',session:null,settings:{music:.1,effects:.7,glyphs:'ps',contrast:false,motion:false,...stored('alob-settings',{})},profiles:stored('alob-profiles',[null,null,null]),slot:0,activity:null,result:null,tuning:{...DEFAULT_TUNABLES},input:{x:0,y:0,breath:false,left:false,right:false},keys:new Set(),lastInput:performance.now(),inputKind:'keyboard',focus:0,paused:false,attract:false,attractIndex:0,medley:null,weigh:null,hubRound:false,hubEnded:false,hubScores:{},hubClock:0,gamepadButtons:[],driver:null};\n25:const iconFor=family=>({still:'✳',reps:'↕',hoop:'◌',header:'◉',step:'♪',slack:'〰',tray:'♧',jog:'➜',jump:'↗'})[family]||'✳';\n32:    content=panel(`${brand}<h1 class=\"title\">${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(0,2).join(' '))}<br><span>${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(2).join(' '))}.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">A week of movement, a talking scale, and absolutely no pressure to be graceful.</p><div class=\"title-tag\">YOUR ISLAND IS READY</div>${notice()?`<p class=\"description\" style=\"margin-top:18px\"><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong></p><div class=\"menu\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}</div>`:`<div class=\"menu\">${button('Begin your week','slots','','primary')}<div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Drop-in','dropin','','ghost')}${button('Family Hour','family','','ghost')}</div><div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}${button('About','about','','ghost')}</div></div>${footer()}`}`,'title-screen')+`<div class=\"hero-note\">WELCOME TO LITTLE ISLAND<strong>Take it one wobble at a time.</strong>EST. WHENEVER YOU ARE READY</div>`;\n37:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge sun\">✦ ${player.drips} DRIPS</span></div>${heading(`DAY ${day} / 7 · ${DAY_NAMES[day-1]}`,'Good to see you. ',`Ounce says: “${day===7?'Today, we stand together. And I owe you an explanation.':'The island is ready when you are.'}”`)}<div class=\"stats\"><span class=\"badge\">${escape(player.name)}</span> <span class=\"badge\">${player.stars} STARS</span> <span class=\"badge\">WOBBLE AGE ${player.history.length?wobbleAge(player):'—'}</span></div><div class=\"stack\"><button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"weigh\"><span class=\"icon\">◉</span><span><span class=\"name\">Daily weigh-in</span><span class=\"sub\">THREE LITTLE BALANCE CHECKS</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>${day===7?`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"finale\"><span class=\"icon\">✦</span><span><span class=\"name\">The Long Stand</span><span class=\"sub\">YOUR WEEK FINALE</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`:''}</div><div class=\"eyebrow\" style=\"margin-top:20px\">PICK A PRACTICE · ${activities.length} OPEN</div><div class=\"scroll-list stack\">${activities.map(activity=>`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"intro\" data-id=\"${activity.id}\"><span class=\"icon\">${iconFor(activity.family)}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${escape(activity.name)}</span><span class=\"sub\">${escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())} · ${activity.duration} SEC ${player.played[activity.id]?`· ${'★'.repeat(player.played[activity.id])}`:''}</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu-row\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">${button('Day report','day-report','','small')}${button('Settings','settings','','small ghost')}</div>${footer()}`,'island-screen');\n41:  }else if(app.screen==='game'&&app.medley){\n42:    const medley=app.medley, activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===medley.picks[medley.event]);\n43:    const ranking=medley.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n44:    content=`<section class=\"screen family-game\"><div class=\"family-game-shell\"><div class=\"family-game-top\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">FAMILY HOUR · EVENT ${medley.event+1} / 3</div><h1>${medley.phase==='break'?'Time for a breather':escape(activity.name)}</h1><p>${medley.phase==='break'?'Next event starts shortly.':escape(activity.instruction)}</p></div><div class=\"family-clock\"><strong id=\"family-time\">${medley.phase==='break'?Math.ceil(medley.breakTime):EVENT_SECONDS}</strong><small>SECONDS</small></div></div>${medley.phase==='break'?`<div class=\"family-break\"><strong>ROUND COMPLETE</strong>${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div><span>${index+1}. ${familyName(medley.members[entry.index],entry.index)}</span><b>${entry.score} PTS</b></div>`).join('')}</div>`:`<div class=\"family-grid\">${medley.members.map((member,index)=>`<div class=\"family-lane\"><div class=\"family-lane-title\"><strong>${familyName(member,index)}</strong><span>${member.kind==='bot'?'BOT':member.kind==='keyboard'?'KEYBOARD':`PAD ${member.index+1}`}</span></div><div class=\"family-lane-body\"><div class=\"dial family-dial\"><span class=\"dot\" id=\"family-dot-${index}\"></span></div><div><strong id=\"family-score-${index}\">0</strong><small>POINTS</small></div></div><p id=\"family-cue-${index}\">${escape(activity.instruction)}</p></div>`).join('')}</div>`}</div><div class=\"family-game-tip\">F / J OR L1 / R1: STEP · ESC / OPTIONS: PAUSE</div></section>`;\n52:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">PRACTICE COMPLETE</span></div>${heading('NICE WORK',escape(app.activity.name),escape(app.activity.quip||'THE ISLAND IS PROUD OF YOU.'))}<div class=\"score-hero\">${result.score}<small style=\"font-size:20px;color:#8ca397\"> / 100</small></div><div class=\"stars\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars)}${'☆'.repeat(3-result.stars)}</div><div class=\"result-box\"><span>+ ${result.drips} DRIPS</span><span>${Math.round(result.seconds)} SECONDS OF YOU TIME</span></div><div class=\"menu\">${button(app.medley?'Next player / event':app.weigh?'Continue weigh-in':'Back to the island','continue','','primary')}${!app.medley&&!app.weigh?button('Try again','start','','ghost'):''}</div>${footer()}`);\n60:  }else if(app.screen==='family'){\n61:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">LOCAL MULTIPLAYER</span></div>${heading('PLAY TOGETHER','Family Hour','Join up to four players for three simultaneous events.')}<div class=\"family-roster\">${app.medley.members.map((member,index)=>`<span class=\"badge\">${familyName(member,index)} · ${member.kind==='pad'?`PAD ${member.index+1}`:member.kind.toUpperCase()}</span>`).join('')||'<span class=\"badge\">NO PLAYERS YET</span>'}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Join with keyboard','family-join','', 'ghost')}${button('Add a bot','family-bot','', 'ghost')}${button('Start the medley','family-start',app.medley.members.length?'':'disabled','primary')}</div><p class=\"family-help\">ENTER: join keyboard · CROSS / A: join controller<br>SPACE / OPTIONS: start · B: add bot</p>${footer()}`);\n62:  }else if(app.screen==='medley-board'){\n63:    const ranking=app.medley.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n64:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">FAMILY HOUR</span></div>${heading('MEDLEY COMPLETE','A standing ovation.','A little wobble is better together.')}<div class=\"stack\">${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div class=\"list-item\"><span class=\"icon\">${index+1}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${familyName(app.medley.members[entry.index],entry.index)}</span><span class=\"sub\">${entry.score} POINTS</span></span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Back to title','title','','primary')}</div>`);\n71:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">CREDITS</span></div>${heading('THE FINE PRINT','About the island','A Little Off Balance is a playful tribute, not medical advice.')}<div class=\"about-text\">${section('Source Information',Object.entries(about.sourceInformation).map(([key,value])=>`${key}: ${value}`))}${section('Testing Feedback',about.testingFeedback)}${section('Engine Feedback',about.engineFeedback)}${section('Prompt Feedback',about.promptFeedback)}</div>${footer()}`);\n96:function familyName(member,index){return member.kind==='bot'?`BOT ${index+1}`:`PLAYER ${index+1}`;}\n98:function familyJoin(kind,index){const medley=app.medley;if(!medley||medley.members.length>=4||kind!=='bot'&&medley.members.some(member=>member.kind===kind&&member.index===index))return;medley.members.push({kind,index});medley.scores.push(0);render();}\n100:  const medley=app.medley;\n101:  app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(activity=>activity.id===medley.picks[medley.event]);\n102:  medley.phase='event';\n103:  medley.sessions=medley.members.map(()=>new ActivitySession(app.activity,{duration:EVENT_SECONDS,random:seededRandom(medley.seed+medley.event),hard:false,tuning:{...app.tuning,timeScale:1}}));\n104:  app.session=medley.sessions[0];app.paused=false;go('game');\n107:  const medley=app.medley;\n108:  medley.sessions.forEach((session,index)=>{medley.scores[index]+=session.result().score*10;});\n109:  if(medley.event===2){go('medley-board');return;}\n110:  medley.phase='break';medley.breakTime=BREAK_SECONDS;render();\n117:  if(action==='title'){app.session=null;app.medley=null;app.guest=null;go('title');}\n121:  else if(action==='island'){app.medley=null;app.weigh=null;go('island');}\n130:  else if(action==='family'){const seed=Math.floor(Math.random()*4294967296);app.medley={members:[],scores:[],seed,event:0,picks:pickMedley(seededRandom(seed)),padButtons:{},padEdges:{}};go('family');}\n131:  else if(action==='family-join')familyJoin('keyboard');\n132:  else if(action==='family-bot')familyJoin('bot');\n133:  else if(action==='family-start'&&app.medley.members.length)startMedley();\n139:  else if(action==='leave'){app.session=null;app.medley=null;app.weigh=null;go(profile()?'island':'title');}\n149:window.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(app.screen!=='family'||event.repeat)return;const key=event.key.toLowerCase();if(!['enter',' ','b','escape'].includes(key))return;event.preventDefault();event.stopImmediatePropagation();app.keyboardSeen=true;app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='keyboard';sound.unlock();if(key==='enter')familyJoin('keyboard');else if(key==='b')familyJoin('bot');else if(key===' '&&app.medley.members.length)startMedley();else if(key==='escape')act('title');},true);\n157:function gamepad(){if(app.medley&&['family','game'].includes(app.screen))return null;const pad=Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.()||[]).find(Boolean);if(!pad)return null;const down=index=>!!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed;const just=index=>down(index)&&!app.gamepadButtons[index];if(just(9)){app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='gamepad';pause();}if(app.screen==='hub-card'&&just(3))globalThis.AIHub?.answer('more');if(app.screen!=='game'){if(just(12))menuMove(-1);if(just(13))menuMove(1);if(just(0)){const buttons=Array.from(ui.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled)'));buttons[app.focus]?.click();}if(just(1))ui.querySelector('.back')?.click();}else{if(just(4))app.input.left=true;if(just(5))app.input.right=true;}if(pad.axes.some(value=>Math.abs(value)>.2)||pad.buttons.some(item=>item.pressed)){app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='gamepad';if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return null;}}app.gamepadButtons=pad.buttons.map(item=>item.pressed);return pad;}\n159:  if(!app.medley||!['family','game'].includes(app.screen))return;\n160:  const medley=app.medley;medley.padEdges={};\n162:    const previous=medley.padButtons[pad.index]||[],just=index=>!!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed&&!previous[index];\n163:    medley.padEdges[pad.index]={left:just(4),right:just(5)};medley.padButtons[pad.index]=pad.buttons.map(item=>item.pressed);\n165:    if(app.screen==='family'){\n166:      if(just(0))familyJoin('pad',pad.index);\n167:      if(just(2))familyJoin('bot');\n168:      if(just(9)&&medley.members.length)startMedley();\n175:  if(activity.family==='reps'){\n180:  if(activity.family==='header')return Math.floor(time/2.4)%2===0?'← HEAD LEFT':'HEAD RIGHT →';\n181:  if(activity.family==='step')return Math.abs(time/.7-Math.round(time/.7))<.23?'STEP NOW · F OR J':'WAIT FOR THE BEAT';\n182:  if(activity.family==='jog')return 'ALTERNATE F AND J';\n183:  if(activity.family==='slack')return 'F / J TO WALK THE LINE';\n184:  if(activity.family==='jump')return 'SPACE / R2 TO JUMP';\n185:  if(activity.family==='hoop')return `CIRCLE THE STICK · ${Math.round(session.hoopLift*100)}% LIFT`;\n190:  const medley=app.medley,timeLabel=document.getElementById('family-time');\n191:  if(medley.phase==='break'){\n192:    medley.breakTime-=dt;\n193:    if(timeLabel)timeLabel.textContent=Math.max(0,Math.ceil(medley.breakTime));\n194:    if(medley.breakTime<=0){medley.event++;startMedley();}\n198:  medley.sessions.forEach((session,index)=>{\n199:    const member=medley.members[index],pad=member.kind==='pad'?pads.find(item=>item?.index===member.index):null;\n206:      input.x=pad.axes[0]||0;input.y=pad.axes[1]||0;input.breath=!!pad.buttons[7]?.pressed;Object.assign(input,medley.padEdges[pad.index]);\n208:      const time=session.elapsed,family=session.activity.family;\n209:      if(family==='hoop'){input.x=Math.cos(time*7);input.y=Math.sin(time*7);}\n210:      else if(family==='reps'){const phase=(time/3.2)%1;input.y=-(phase<.4?phase/.4:phase<.55?1:phase<.9?1-(phase-.55)/.35:0);}\n211:      else if(family==='header'){const beat=Math.floor((time+dt-1.2)/2.4);input.x=beat%2===0?-.8:.8;}\n217:    const dot=document.getElementById(`family-dot-${index}`),score=document.getElementById(`family-score-${index}`),cue=document.getElementById(`family-cue-${index}`);\n219:    if(score)score.textContent=medley.scores[index]+session.result().score*10;\n225:  if(medley.sessions.every(session=>session.finished))finishFamilyEvent();\n233:  if(app.screen==='game'&&app.medley){updateFamily(dt);requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n240:    if(app.attract){const time=app.session.elapsed;x=app.session.activity.family==='hoop'?Math.cos(time*7):Math.sin(time*1.2)*.2;y=app.session.activity.family==='hoop'?Math.sin(time*7):Math.cos(time)*.2;if(Math.floor(time*3)%2===0)app.input.left=true;else app.input.right=true;}\n248:    if(score)score.textContent=`${app.session.result().score} POINTS · ${app.medley?`PLAYER ${app.medley.player+1}`:'KEEP GOING'}`;\n260:  const window=medleyWindow(globalThis.AIHub.time());\n272:function setupHub(){const hub=globalThis.AIHub;if(!hub?.active)return;hub.on('card',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;go('hub-card');});hub.on('start',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;app.hubRound=true;app.hubEnded=false;app.hubScores={};app.hubTotal=0;app.hubPicks=pickMedley(hub.rng('medley'));beginHubEvent(0);clearInterval(app.hubTimer);sendHubState();app.hubTimer=setInterval(sendHubState,100);});hub.on('message',(data,from)=>{app.hubScores[from]=data;});hub.on('time-up',finishHub);hub.on('end',()=>{clearInterval(app.hubTimer);app.hubRound=false;app.hubEnded=true;app.hubClosed=true;sound.context?.suspend();});hub.connect({mode:'ghost',seats:[1,4],card:true}).then(info=>{if(info)hub.ready();});}\n273:window.__GAME__={go:(screen,args={})=>{if(args.id)app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===args.id);if(screen==='game'&&app.activity)begin(app.activity);else go(screen);},state:()=>({screen:app.screen,day:profile()?.day,activity:app.activity?.id,elapsed:app.session?.elapsed,score:app.session?.result().score,attract:app.attract,profiles:app.profiles,hubScores:app.hubScores,family:app.medley?{phase:app.medley.phase,event:app.medley.event,players:app.medley.members.length,scores:[...app.medley.scores],picks:[...app.medley.picks],dots:app.medley.sessions?.map(session=>({x:session.dot.x,y:session.dot.y}))}:null}),setDriver:skill=>{app.driver=skill;},get tunables(){return app.tuning;},finishActivity:()=>{if(app.medley?.phase==='event'){app.medley.sessions.forEach(session=>{session.elapsed=session.duration;session.finished=true;});finishFamilyEvent();}else if(app.session){app.session.elapsed=app.session.duration;app.session.finished=true;finish();}},finishBreak:()=>{if(app.medley?.phase==='break'){app.medley.event++;startMedley();}}};\n\n--- PROGRESS ---\n# Progress\n\n## Project\n- Title selected by `crypto.randomInt` from 50 candidates: **A Little Off Balance**.\n- Deliverable basename: `A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846`.\n- Read `TASK.md` and `PLAN.md`; downloaded the unmodified Pixel Engine 0.46.0 and AI Hub client into the development folder.\n- Implemented the activity catalog, unstable balance physics, progression, synthesized audio, 3D island, screens, local profiles, family sessions, and AI Hub client integration. The standalone HTML builds successfully.\n\n## Work plan\n1. Read the complete design and integration documentation; obtain the unmodified engine and hub client.\n2. Build the core game, island, activities, progression, input, audio, and multiplayer.\n3. Bundle the standalone HTML, run focused playthrough and viewport tests, and fix findings.\n4. Complete About/Credits, `exit-interview.json`, and this progress record.\n\n## Current checkpoint\n- Source lives in the development folder's `src/`; build the standalone deliverable with `npm run build` there.\n- The last completed `npm test` run passed 28 checks, including activity simulations, profile/day progression, family play, the WebGPU scene, and Chromium/Firefox/WebKit browser flows. Simultaneous Family Hour has since been implemented and its updated tests are in progress.\n- The viewport matrix reports 24 clean phone, foldable, tablet, and desktop configurations. Selected WebKit and Chromium screenshots have been inspected.\n- Fixed an unsupported-WebGPU startup overlay and an oversized title encountered during browser testing.\n- The official AI Hub harness passed one-, two-, and four-player simulations, including latency, packet loss, and host/player departures. Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit opened the standalone `file://` build.\n- Fixed an AI Hub ready/welcome race and phone gameplay hint overflow. Added a CSS fallback character for browsers without WebGPU.\n- Next: finish simultaneous Family Hour tests and viewport inspection; replace interview placeholders and rebuild the final artifacts.\n- The implementation is a simplified interpretation of the extensive plan: activities share the island scene rather than having full bespoke animated environments.\n\n## Constraints\n- Only work in this directory and the required development subfolder; use OS-assigned localhost ports and stop only our own processes.\n- Keep `pixel-engine.js` unchanged; synthesize audio in code; default music volume 10%.\n- Test small phones, tablets, wide screens, WebKit, and scripted game flows; no physical controller or real iOS device is available.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_634","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- TASK OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS ---'; rg -n -A85 'Interview|Feedback|About|deliver|Hand|JSON' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- ABOUT ---\\\\n'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/about.js\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- FAMILY TESTS ---\\\\n'; rg -n -A85 -B5 'family' \\\"\"'$DEV/tests/browser.py\" | tail -150; printf '\"'\\\\n--- FAMILY MAIN ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,275p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_634","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- TASK OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS ---'; rg -n -A85 'Interview|Feedback|About|deliver|Hand|JSON' TASK.md; printf '\\\\n--- ABOUT ---\\\\n'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/about.js\"; printf '\"'\\\\n--- FAMILY TESTS ---\\\\n'; rg -n -A85 -B5 'family' \\\"\"'$DEV/tests/browser.py\" | tail -150; printf '\"'\\\\n--- FAMILY MAIN ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,275p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\"'","aggregated_output":"--- TASK OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS ---\n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24-Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846].html in root when you’re done. You may use external CDN dependencies. Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine’s ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine’s headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\n25-\n26-Performance: Treat the performance budget as unlimited. Add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights, and shadows as the scene needs. Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization.\n27-\n28-Testing: Test as much as you like with headless tools: scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole game. Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can’t check. Don’t use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n29-\n30-Effort: Spend effort however you see fit.\n31-\n32-## This computer\n33-Checked 2026-11-04 20:05 (America/Vancouver) by node check-environment.mjs.\n34-\n35-- **Computer:** Worki9: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900K, 32 cores, 20 GB RAM, 8 GB swap. Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS on WSL2 (Linux 6.18.33.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2).\n36-- **Space:** 850 GB free in the home folder. /tmp: 9.8 GB, in memory (tmpfs), 8.2 GB free when checked.\n37-- **Display:** none for runs (they run with DISPLAY unset), so a headed browser needs xvfb-run.\n38-- **Browsers:** Playwright 1.63.0 for Python (from playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright), with Chromium 153.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered; WebGPU, software-rendered, when started with --enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader), Firefox 155.0 (WebGL 2, software-rendered), WebKit 26.6 (WebGL 2) already downloaded. Phone and tablet device profiles are built in.\n39-  WebGPU only works on a secure page: file:// or http://127.0.0.1. A WebGPU canvas can come out blank in a headless screenshot, so check the game's state instead.\n40-  For Node, `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder uses the browsers already downloaded; another version downloads its own.\n41-  Playwright runs here with PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 (already set for runs): this OS isn't one it supports by name.\n42-- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\n43-- **Rust:** rustup's toolchains 1.96.0, 1.98.1, stable; the wasm32-unknown-unknown target on 1.98.1.\n44-- **Not installed:** sox, bun, deno.\n45-- **Network:** internet works (github.com, registry.npmjs.org).\n46-- **Memory:** earlyoom is on: when memory runs out it ends the biggest browser, so \"Target closed\", \"page crashed\" or \"browser has been closed\" means memory ran out, not a bug in your game. Run fewer browsers at once rather than retrying.\n47-\n48-### What this computer doesn't have\n49-\n50-No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n51-\n52-- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n53-- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n54-- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n55-- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n56-- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n57-- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n58-\n59-### Sharing this computer\n60-\n61-- Other agents run here at the same time. Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\n62-- Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\n63-- The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\n64-- The system Python has Playwright and nothing else. For one (Pillow, numpy …), use uv: `uv run --with pillow python script.py`, adding `--with playwright==1.63.0` when the script drives a browser too (a newer Playwright can't find the browsers here).\n65-\n66-## Goal\n67-\n68-Build an original game inspired by the source.\n69-\n70-Scope\n71-\n72-Create a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n73-\n74-Include a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n75-\n76-Attract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n77-\n78-Multiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n79-\n80-Narrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n81-\n82-## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\n83-Design the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n84-\n85-Do not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n86-\n87-Touch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n88-\n89-## Done\n90-No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n91-\n92-## Source Information\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n94-- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n95-- Source: the work it's based on\n96-- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n97-- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n98-- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n99-- Art Direction: style used\n100-- Animation: system used\n101-- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n102-- Online: network features used, or none\n103-- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n104-- Research: research done, or none\n105-- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n106-- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n107:- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n108-\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n110-{\n111-  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n112:  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n113:  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n114:  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n115-  \"aiHub\": {\n116-    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n117-    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n118-    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n119-    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n120-    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n121-    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n122-    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n123-    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n124-    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n125-    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n126-  }\n127-}\n128-The catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n129-\n130:Testing Feedback\n131-\n132-- How many issues did testing catch?\n133-- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n134-- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n135-- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n136-\n137:Engine Feedback\n138-\n139-- What did you like most about the engine?\n140-- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n141-- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n142-- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n143-- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n144-- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n145-\n146:Prompt Feedback\n147-\n148-- What did you like most about this prompt?\n149-- What was confusing?\n150-- What was the hardest thing to do?\n151-- What would you change in this prompt?\n\n--- ABOUT ---\nexport const about = {\n  sourceInformation: {\n    date:'2026-11-04 22:18:46', source:'Wii Fit', plan:'PLAN.md', genre:'Sports',\n    perspective:'Isometric 3D island', tech:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, JavaScript, Web Audio',\n    artDirection:'Pastel, low-poly island and friendly, rounded fitness interface',\n    animation:'Procedural posing and three.js AnimationMixer',\n    audio:'Original procedural Web Audio music, effects, and syllabic character voice',\n    online:'AI Hub ghost session with score and position messages',\n    testing:'Automated simulation and browser checks; phone, tablet, desktop and WebKit viewport checks',\n    research:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 documentation and AI Hub session protocol',\n    environment:'Codex CLI (headless); Linux', model:'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max', usage:'added on import'\n  },\n  testingFeedback:['See final testing report.','See final testing report.','Simulation and real-browser interaction.','Static inspection without running the game.'],\n  engineFeedback:['The compact scene lifecycle and built-in camera.','WebGPU availability varies between browsers.','The balance physics, activities and UI.','Validating WebGPU behavior across browser engines.','None; pixel-engine.js remains unchanged.','Provide an explicit supported fallback for browsers without WebGPU.'],\n  promptFeedback:['The emphasis on a playable, controller-first vertical slice.','The scope combines a large simulation, multiplayer and a standalone deliverable.','Balancing the breadth of activities with cross-browser verification.','Prioritize required features and define an explicit minimum for each.'],\n  aiHub:{name:'A Little Off Balance',tagline:'A very serious game about a very wobbly week.',description:'Balance, breathe, and bravely face a talking scale on a cozy island. Play a week of delightfully questionable fitness or challenge friends in a three-event medley.',type:'Game',genre:'Sports',source:'Wii Fit',series:'Wii Fit',players:'1–4',controls:'Left stick / WASD: lean; R2 / Space: breathe; L1/R1 or F/J: step; Escape / Options: pause.',tags:['3d','sports','comedy','arcade','versus']}\n};\n\n--- FAMILY TESTS ---\n128-    finally:\n129-        context.close()\n130-        browser.close()\n131-\n132-\n133:def family(engine, url):\n134-    browser = engine.launch(headless=True)\n135-    page = browser.new_page()\n136-    errors = []\n137-    page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n138-    try:\n139-        page.goto(url, wait_until='load')\n140:        click(page, 'family')\n141:        click(page, 'family-join')\n142:        click(page, 'family-bot')\n143:        assert state(page)['family']['players'] == 2\n144:        click(page, 'family-start')\n145-        for event in range(3):\n146-            screen(page, 'game')\n147:            assert state(page)['family']['event'] == event\n148:            assert page.locator('.family-lane').count() == 2\n149-            page.wait_for_timeout(25)\n150-            finish(page)\n151-            if event < 2:\n152:                assert state(page)['family']['phase'] == 'break'\n153-                page.evaluate('window.__GAME__.finishBreak()')\n154-        screen(page, 'medley-board')\n155-        assert page.get_by_text('PLAYER 1', exact=True).count() == 1\n156-        assert page.get_by_text('BOT 2', exact=True).count() == 1\n157-        assert not errors, errors\n158-    finally:\n159-        browser.close()\n160-\n161-\n162:def family_gamepads(engine, url):\n163-    browser = engine.launch(headless=True)\n164-    page = browser.new_page()\n165-    errors = []\n166-    page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n167-    try:\n168-        page.goto(url, wait_until='load')\n169-        page.evaluate('''() => {\n170-            window.fakePads = Array.from({length: 4}, (_, index) => ({\n171-                index, axes: [0, 0], connected: true,\n172-                buttons: Array.from({length: 16}, () => ({pressed: false, value: 0}))\n173-            }));\n174-            Object.defineProperty(navigator, 'getGamepads', {configurable: true, value: () => window.fakePads});\n175-        }''')\n176:        click(page, 'family')\n177-        for index in range(4):\n178-            page.evaluate('(index) => window.fakePads[index].buttons[0].pressed = true', index)\n179-            page.wait_for_timeout(80)\n180-            page.evaluate('(index) => window.fakePads[index].buttons[0].pressed = false', index)\n181-            page.wait_for_timeout(80)\n182:        assert state(page)['family']['players'] == 4\n183:        click(page, 'family-start')\n184-        page.evaluate('window.fakePads[0].axes[0] = 1; window.fakePads[1].axes[0] = -1')\n185-        page.wait_for_timeout(350)\n186:        dots = state(page)['family']['dots']\n187-        assert len(dots) == 4 and abs(dots[0]['x'] - dots[1]['x']) > .02, dots\n188:        assert page.locator('.family-lane').count() == 4\n189-        assert not errors, errors\n190-    finally:\n191-        browser.close()\n192-\n193-\n194-def mobile(playwright, url):\n195-    browser = playwright.webkit.launch(headless=True)\n196-    context = browser.new_context(**playwright.devices['iPhone 17 Pro'])\n197-    page = context.new_page()\n198-    try:\n199-        page.goto(url, wait_until='load')\n200-        assert page.get_by_text('Controller or keyboard required').is_visible()\n201-        assert page.locator('[data-action=\"slots\"]').count() == 0\n202-        click(page, 'settings')\n203-        assert page.locator('#music').input_value() == '0.1'\n204-    finally:\n205-        context.close()\n206-        browser.close()\n207-\n208-\n209-def attract(engine, url):\n210-    browser = engine.launch(headless=True)\n211-    page = browser.new_page()\n212-    try:\n213-        page.goto(url, wait_until='load')\n214-        page.wait_for_function('window.__GAME__.state().attract', timeout=13000)\n215-        page.keyboard.press('Enter')\n216-        screen(page, 'title')\n217-    finally:\n218-        browser.close()\n219-\n220-\n221-def webgpu(playwright, url):\n222-    browser = playwright.chromium.launch(headless=True, args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu', '--enable-features=Vulkan', '--use-angle=swiftshader', '--use-vulkan=swiftshader', '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'])\n223-    page = browser.new_page()\n224-    errors = []\n225-    page.on('pageerror', lambda error: errors.append(str(error)))\n226-    try:\n227-        page.goto(url, wait_until='load')\n228-        page.wait_for_selector('#world canvas', timeout=12000)\n229-        assert not errors, errors\n230-    finally:\n231-        browser.close()\n232-\n233-\n234-handler = functools.partial(QuietHandler, directory=str(ROOT))\n235-server = http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer(('127.0.0.1', 0), handler)\n236-threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True).start()\n237-url = f'http://127.0.0.1:{server.server_port}/' + urllib.parse.quote(FILENAME)\n238-try:\n239-    with sync_playwright() as playwright:\n240-        for name in ('chromium', 'firefox', 'webkit'):\n241-            check(name + ' profile, activity, persistence', lambda name=name: smoke(getattr(playwright, name), url))\n242-        check('seven-day playthrough and all activities', lambda: complete_week(playwright.chromium, url))\n243:        check('family medley', lambda: family(playwright.chromium, url))\n244:        check('four simultaneous gamepad lanes', lambda: family_gamepads(playwright.chromium, url))\n245-        check('touch-only notice', lambda: mobile(playwright, url))\n246-        check('idle attract and wake', lambda: attract(playwright.chromium, url))\n247-        check('WebGPU island', lambda: webgpu(playwright, url))\n248-finally:\n249-    server.shutdown()\n250-print(json.dumps({'passed': passed, 'failures': failures}))\n\n--- FAMILY MAIN ---\nimport { ACTIVITIES, DAY_NAMES, activityForDay } from './data/activities.js';\nimport { makeProfile, wobbleAge, ActivitySession } from './core/session.js';\nimport { DEFAULT_TUNABLES } from './core/dot.js';\nimport { Sound } from './core/audio-runtime.js';\nimport { about } from './data/about.js';\nimport { TITLE } from './data/title.js';\nimport { EVENT_SECONDS, BREAK_SECONDS, pickMedley, medleyWindow } from './data/medley.js';\nimport { startWorld } from './world.js';\n\nconst ui=document.getElementById('ui');\nconst stored=(key,fallback)=>{try{return JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key))??fallback;}catch{return fallback;}};\nconst escape=value=>String(value).replace(/[&<>\"']/g,character=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\"':'&quot;',\"'\":'&#39;'}[character]));\nconst app={screen:'title',session:null,settings:{music:.1,effects:.7,glyphs:'ps',contrast:false,motion:false,...stored('alob-settings',{})},profiles:stored('alob-profiles',[null,null,null]),slot:0,activity:null,result:null,tuning:{...DEFAULT_TUNABLES},input:{x:0,y:0,breath:false,left:false,right:false},keys:new Set(),lastInput:performance.now(),inputKind:'keyboard',focus:0,paused:false,attract:false,attractIndex:0,medley:null,weigh:null,hubRound:false,hubEnded:false,hubScores:{},hubClock:0,gamepadButtons:[],driver:null};\nconst sound=new Sound(app.settings);\nconst save=()=>{try{localStorage.setItem('alob-profiles',JSON.stringify(app.profiles));localStorage.setItem('alob-settings',JSON.stringify(app.settings));}catch{}};\nconst profile=()=>app.guest||app.profiles[app.slot];\nconst brand='<div class=\"brand\"><span class=\"brand-icon\">✳</span> LITTLE ISLAND WELLNESS</div>';\nconst button=(label,action,extra='',style='')=>`<button class=\"button ${style}\" data-action=\"${action}\" ${extra}>${label}<span class=\"arrow\">↗</span></button>`;\nconst back=target=>`<button class=\"back\" data-action=\"${target}\" aria-label=\"Go back\">←</button>`;\nconst panel=(content,extra='')=>`<section class=\"screen ${extra}\"><div class=\"panel glass\">${content}</div></section>`;\nconst heading=(kicker,title,description)=>`<div class=\"eyebrow\">${kicker}</div><h1 class=\"heading\">${title}</h1><p class=\"description\">${description}</p>`;\nconst hint=()=>app.inputKind==='gamepad'?`<span class=\"key\">${app.settings.glyphs==='xbox'?'A':'✕'}</span> SELECT <span class=\"key\">${app.settings.glyphs==='xbox'?'B':'◯'}</span> BACK`:'<span class=\"key\">↑↓</span> CHOOSE <span class=\"key\">ENTER</span> SELECT';\nconst footer=()=>`<div class=\"footnote\">${hint()}</div>`;\nconst notice=()=>matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)').matches&&!app.keyboardSeen&&!Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.()||[]).some(Boolean);\nconst iconFor=family=>({still:'✳',reps:'↕',hoop:'◌',header:'◉',step:'♪',slack:'〰',tray:'♧',jog:'➜',jump:'↗'})[family]||'✳';\n\nfunction render(){\n  document.body.classList.toggle('high-contrast',app.settings.contrast);\n  document.body.classList.toggle('reduce-motion',app.settings.motion);\n  let content='';\n  if(app.screen==='title'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}<h1 class=\"title\">${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(0,2).join(' '))}<br><span>${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(2).join(' '))}.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">A week of movement, a talking scale, and absolutely no pressure to be graceful.</p><div class=\"title-tag\">YOUR ISLAND IS READY</div>${notice()?`<p class=\"description\" style=\"margin-top:18px\"><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong></p><div class=\"menu\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}</div>`:`<div class=\"menu\">${button('Begin your week','slots','','primary')}<div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Drop-in','dropin','','ghost')}${button('Family Hour','family','','ghost')}</div><div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}${button('About','about','','ghost')}</div></div>${footer()}`}`,'title-screen')+`<div class=\"hero-note\">WELCOME TO LITTLE ISLAND<strong>Take it one wobble at a time.</strong>EST. WHENEVER YOU ARE READY</div>`;\n  }else if(app.screen==='slots'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">YOUR WEEK</span></div>${heading('A PLACE TO BEGIN','Who is stepping on?','Choose a profile. Your island remembers your progress on this device.')}<div class=\"stack\">${app.profiles.map((item,index)=>`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"slot\" data-index=\"${index}\"><span class=\"icon\">${index+1}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${item?escape(item.name):'Start a new week'}</span><span class=\"sub\">${item?`DAY ${item.day} · ${item.drips} DRIPS`:'EMPTY PROFILE'}</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`).join('')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='island'){\n    const player=profile(), day=Math.min(player.day,7), activities=activityForDay(day);\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge sun\">✦ ${player.drips} DRIPS</span></div>${heading(`DAY ${day} / 7 · ${DAY_NAMES[day-1]}`,'Good to see you. ',`Ounce says: “${day===7?'Today, we stand together. And I owe you an explanation.':'The island is ready when you are.'}”`)}<div class=\"stats\"><span class=\"badge\">${escape(player.name)}</span> <span class=\"badge\">${player.stars} STARS</span> <span class=\"badge\">WOBBLE AGE ${player.history.length?wobbleAge(player):'—'}</span></div><div class=\"stack\"><button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"weigh\"><span class=\"icon\">◉</span><span><span class=\"name\">Daily weigh-in</span><span class=\"sub\">THREE LITTLE BALANCE CHECKS</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>${day===7?`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"finale\"><span class=\"icon\">✦</span><span><span class=\"name\">The Long Stand</span><span class=\"sub\">YOUR WEEK FINALE</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`:''}</div><div class=\"eyebrow\" style=\"margin-top:20px\">PICK A PRACTICE · ${activities.length} OPEN</div><div class=\"scroll-list stack\">${activities.map(activity=>`<button class=\"list-item\" data-action=\"intro\" data-id=\"${activity.id}\"><span class=\"icon\">${iconFor(activity.family)}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${escape(activity.name)}</span><span class=\"sub\">${escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())} · ${activity.duration} SEC ${player.played[activity.id]?`· ${'★'.repeat(player.played[activity.id])}`:''}</span></span><span class=\"arrow\">→</span></button>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu-row\" style=\"margin-top:12px\">${button('Day report','day-report','','small')}${button('Settings','settings','','small ghost')}</div>${footer()}`,'island-screen');\n  }else if(app.screen==='intro'){\n    const activity=app.activity;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back(app.returnScreen||'island')}<span class=\"badge sun\">${escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())}</span></div>${heading('TODAY’S PRACTICE',escape(activity.name),escape(activity.instruction)+'.')}<div class=\"instruction-card\"><strong>LET’S KEEP IT SIMPLE</strong><p>Lean with the left stick or WASD. Press Space / R2 to breathe; use F and J / L1 and R1 to step.</p><p>Find your own rhythm. Ounce is not a medical professional, despite the nametag.</p></div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Let’s go','start','','primary')}${button(`Hard mode: ${app.hard?'ON':'OFF'}`,'hard','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='game'&&app.medley){\n    const medley=app.medley, activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===medley.picks[medley.event]);\n    const ranking=medley.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n    content=`<section class=\"screen family-game\"><div class=\"family-game-shell\"><div class=\"family-game-top\"><div><div class=\"eyebrow\">FAMILY HOUR · EVENT ${medley.event+1} / 3</div><h1>${medley.phase==='break'?'Time for a breather':escape(activity.name)}</h1><p>${medley.phase==='break'?'Next event starts shortly.':escape(activity.instruction)}</p></div><div class=\"family-clock\"><strong id=\"family-time\">${medley.phase==='break'?Math.ceil(medley.breakTime):EVENT_SECONDS}</strong><small>SECONDS</small></div></div>${medley.phase==='break'?`<div class=\"family-break\"><strong>ROUND COMPLETE</strong>${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div><span>${index+1}. ${familyName(medley.members[entry.index],entry.index)}</span><b>${entry.score} PTS</b></div>`).join('')}</div>`:`<div class=\"family-grid\">${medley.members.map((member,index)=>`<div class=\"family-lane\"><div class=\"family-lane-title\"><strong>${familyName(member,index)}</strong><span>${member.kind==='bot'?'BOT':member.kind==='keyboard'?'KEYBOARD':`PAD ${member.index+1}`}</span></div><div class=\"family-lane-body\"><div class=\"dial family-dial\"><span class=\"dot\" id=\"family-dot-${index}\"></span></div><div><strong id=\"family-score-${index}\">0</strong><small>POINTS</small></div></div><p id=\"family-cue-${index}\">${escape(activity.instruction)}</p></div>`).join('')}</div>`}</div><div class=\"family-game-tip\">F / J OR L1 / R1: STEP · ESC / OPTIONS: PAUSE</div></section>`;\n  }else if(app.screen==='game'){\n    const activity=app.session.activity;\n    content=`<section class=\"screen game-screen\"><div class=\"game-hud\"><div class=\"game-top\"><div class=\"game-title\"><small>${app.attract?'ISLAND DEMO · PRESS ANY KEY TO PLAY':app.hubRound?'AI HUB · THREE-EVENT MEDLEY':escape(activity.place.toUpperCase())}</small><strong>${escape(activity.name)}</strong></div><div class=\"game-time\" id=\"seconds\">${Math.ceil(app.session.duration)}</div></div><div class=\"game-bottom\"><div class=\"balance-card\"><div class=\"balance-inner\"><div class=\"dial\" id=\"dial\" aria-label=\"Balance indicator\"><div class=\"dial-ring\"></div><div class=\"dot\" id=\"balance-dot\"></div></div><div class=\"balance-text\"><strong>Find your center.</strong><p id=\"live-score\">A little wobble is normal.</p><div class=\"meter\"><span id=\"meter\" style=\"width:0%\"></span></div></div></div></div><div class=\"game-tip\">${escape(activity.instruction)}<br><strong id=\"live-cue\"></strong><br><span class=\"key\">WASD / L</span> LEAN <span class=\"key\">SPACE / R2</span> BREATHE<br><span class=\"key\">F / J · L1 / R1</span> STEP · ESC PAUSE</div></div></div></section>`;\n  }else if(app.screen==='pause'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge\">TAKE YOUR TIME</span></div>${heading('PAUSED','A little breather.','Your island will be right here.')}<div class=\"menu\">${button('Resume','resume','','primary')}${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}${button('Dev tools','dev','','ghost')}${button('Leave practice','leave','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='results'){\n    const result=app.result;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">PRACTICE COMPLETE</span></div>${heading('NICE WORK',escape(app.activity.name),escape(app.activity.quip||'THE ISLAND IS PROUD OF YOU.'))}<div class=\"score-hero\">${result.score}<small style=\"font-size:20px;color:#8ca397\"> / 100</small></div><div class=\"stars\">${'★'.repeat(result.stars)}${'☆'.repeat(3-result.stars)}</div><div class=\"result-box\"><span>+ ${result.drips} DRIPS</span><span>${Math.round(result.seconds)} SECONDS OF YOU TIME</span></div><div class=\"menu\">${button(app.medley?'Next player / event':app.weigh?'Continue weigh-in':'Back to the island','continue','','primary')}${!app.medley&&!app.weigh?button('Try again','start','','ghost'):''}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='weigh-result'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge\">DAILY CHECK-IN</span></div>${heading('A NUMBER, NOT A VERDICT','Your wobble age','Ounce has reviewed your three balance checks with tremendous confidence.')}<div class=\"score-hero\">${wobbleAge(profile())}</div><p class=\"description\">This is just a playful score, not a measure of health. Keep moving at your own pace.</p><div class=\"menu\">${button('Back to the island','island','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='day-report'){\n    const player=profile();\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('island')}<span class=\"badge sun\">DAY ${player.day}</span></div>${heading('YOUR DAY REPORT','Every wobble counts.',`You have collected ${player.drips} drips and ${player.stars} stars. You showed up; the rest is gravy.`)}<div class=\"instruction-card\"><strong>OUNCE’S NOTE</strong><p>${player.day===6?'Tomorrow is the Long Stand. Ounce seems unusually quiet.':player.day>=7?'The island is still yours to enjoy.':'A little movement is better than a perfectly planned nap. Usually.'}</p></div><div class=\"menu\">${button(player.day>=7?'Back to the island':'Start the next day','next-day','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='reveal'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('THE LONG STAND','Ounce comes clean.','“I added seven years to everyone’s wobble age. I thought you would come back if the number worried you. That was wrong.”')}<p class=\"description\" style=\"margin-top:16px\">The island agrees: a number should never tell you your worth. Your wobble age is now honest, and the island remains open.</p><div class=\"menu\">${button('A fresh start','island','','primary')}</div>`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='family'){\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">LOCAL MULTIPLAYER</span></div>${heading('PLAY TOGETHER','Family Hour','Join up to four players for three simultaneous events.')}<div class=\"family-roster\">${app.medley.members.map((member,index)=>`<span class=\"badge\">${familyName(member,index)} · ${member.kind==='pad'?`PAD ${member.index+1}`:member.kind.toUpperCase()}</span>`).join('')||'<span class=\"badge\">NO PLAYERS YET</span>'}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Join with keyboard','family-join','', 'ghost')}${button('Add a bot','family-bot','', 'ghost')}${button('Start the medley','family-start',app.medley.members.length?'':'disabled','primary')}</div><p class=\"family-help\">ENTER: join keyboard · CROSS / A: join controller<br>SPACE / OPTIONS: start · B: add bot</p>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='medley-board'){\n    const ranking=app.medley.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">FAMILY HOUR</span></div>${heading('MEDLEY COMPLETE','A standing ovation.','A little wobble is better together.')}<div class=\"stack\">${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div class=\"list-item\"><span class=\"icon\">${index+1}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${familyName(app.medley.members[entry.index],entry.index)}</span><span class=\"sub\">${entry.score} POINTS</span></span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Back to title','title','','primary')}</div>`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='settings'||app.screen==='dev'){\n    const dev=app.screen==='dev';\n    const ranges=dev?Object.entries(app.tuning).map(([key,value])=>`<div class=\"field\"><label for=\"${key}\">${escape(key)}</label><input id=\"${key}\" data-tune=\"${key}\" type=\"range\" min=\"${key==='timeScale'?.25:0}\" max=\"${key==='timeScale'?4:key==='dotLag'?.5:8}\" step=\".01\" value=\"${value}\"></div>`).join(''):`<div class=\"field\"><label for=\"music\">Music ${Math.round(app.settings.music*100)}%</label><input id=\"music\" data-setting=\"music\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\".05\" value=\"${app.settings.music}\"></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"effects\">Effects ${Math.round(app.settings.effects*100)}%</label><input id=\"effects\" data-setting=\"effects\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\".05\" value=\"${app.settings.effects}\"></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"glyphs\">Controller prompts</label><select id=\"glyphs\" data-setting=\"glyphs\"><option value=\"ps\" ${app.settings.glyphs==='ps'?'selected':''}>PlayStation</option><option value=\"xbox\" ${app.settings.glyphs==='xbox'?'selected':''}>Xbox</option></select></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"contrast\">High contrast</label><input id=\"contrast\" data-setting=\"contrast\" type=\"checkbox\" ${app.settings.contrast?'checked':''}></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"motion\">Reduce motion</label><input id=\"motion\" data-setting=\"motion\" type=\"checkbox\" ${app.settings.motion?'checked':''}></div>`;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('settings-back')}<span class=\"badge\">${dev?'LIVE TUNING':'MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE'}</span></div>${heading(dev?'DEVELOPER TOOLS':'YOUR PREFERENCES',dev?'Tune the wobble.':'Settings',dev?'Changes apply immediately, including during a paused practice.':'Make the island feel like yours.')}<div class=\"stack\">${ranges}</div><div class=\"menu\">${dev?button('Reset tuning','reset-tuning','','ghost'):''}${button('Done','settings-back','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='about'){\n    const section=(title,entries)=>`<h3>${title}</h3>${entries.map(entry=>`<p>${escape(entry)}</p>`).join('')}`;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">CREDITS</span></div>${heading('THE FINE PRINT','About the island','A Little Off Balance is a playful tribute, not medical advice.')}<div class=\"about-text\">${section('Source Information',Object.entries(about.sourceInformation).map(([key,value])=>`${key}: ${value}`))}${section('Testing Feedback',about.testingFeedback)}${section('Engine Feedback',about.engineFeedback)}${section('Prompt Feedback',about.promptFeedback)}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='hub-card'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('AI HUB · GHOST MEDLEY','Ready to wobble?','Three events, one shared clock. Earn points and watch your fellow islanders as ghosts.')}<div class=\"menu\">${button('Ready','hub-ready','','primary')}${button('I need more time','hub-more','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='hub-finished'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('AI HUB · GHOST MEDLEY','Well wobbled.','Your score is in. The hub will show the final standings.')}<div class=\"badge sun\">${app.result?.score||0} POINTS</div>`);\n  }\n  ui.innerHTML=content;\n  app.focus=0;\n  const first=ui.querySelector('button:not(:disabled)');if(first&&app.inputKind==='gamepad')first.classList.add('focused');\n}\n\nfunction go(screen){app.screen=screen;render();}\nfunction begin(activity,options={}){\n  app.activity=activity;app.session=new ActivitySession(activity,{hard:app.hard,tuning:app.tuning,...options});app.paused=false;go('game');\n}\nfunction finish(){\n  if(!app.session)return;\n  app.result=app.session.result();\n  if(app.attract){app.attractIndex++;startAttract();return;}\n  if(app.hubRound)return;\n  if(app.weigh){app.weigh.push(app.result.score/100);if(app.weigh.length<3){startWeigh();return;}profile().history.push(...app.weigh);profile().history=profile().history.slice(-3);app.weigh=null;save();go('weigh-result');return;}\n  if(profile()){const player=profile();player.drips+=app.result.drips;player.stars+=Math.max(0,app.result.stars-(player.played[app.activity.id]||0));player.played[app.activity.id]=Math.max(app.result.stars,player.played[app.activity.id]||0);if(app.activity.id==='finale'){player.revealed=true;save();go('reveal');return;}save();}\n  sound.effect('good');go('results');\n}\nfunction startWeigh(){const index=app.weigh.length;const names=['Still water','A gentle shift','Chase the breeze'];begin({...ACTIVITIES[0],id:['tree','heron','tax'][index],name:names[index],place:'Weigh-in',duration:8,ring:.38,instruction:['KEEP YOUR DOT IN THE RING','COUNTER THE DRIFT','STAY NEAR THE CENTER'][index]});}\nfunction familyName(member,index){return member.kind==='bot'?`BOT ${index+1}`:`PLAYER ${index+1}`;}\nfunction seededRandom(seed){let state=seed>>>0;return ()=>{state=(Math.imul(state,1664525)+1013904223)>>>0;return state/4294967296;};}\nfunction familyJoin(kind,index){const medley=app.medley;if(!medley||medley.members.length>=4||kind!=='bot'&&medley.members.some(member=>member.kind===kind&&member.index===index))return;medley.members.push({kind,index});medley.scores.push(0);render();}\nfunction startMedley(){\n  const medley=app.medley;\n  app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(activity=>activity.id===medley.picks[medley.event]);\n  medley.phase='event';\n  medley.sessions=medley.members.map(()=>new ActivitySession(app.activity,{duration:EVENT_SECONDS,random:seededRandom(medley.seed+medley.event),hard:false,tuning:{...app.tuning,timeScale:1}}));\n  app.session=medley.sessions[0];app.paused=false;go('game');\n}\nfunction finishFamilyEvent(){\n  const medley=app.medley;\n  medley.sessions.forEach((session,index)=>{medley.scores[index]+=session.result().score*10;});\n  if(medley.event===2){go('medley-board');return;}\n  medley.phase='break';medley.breakTime=BREAK_SECONDS;render();\n}\nfunction startAttract(){app.attract=true;const sequence=['tree','hoop','step','header','slackline'];const activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===sequence[app.attractIndex%sequence.length]);begin(activity,{duration:12});}\nfunction leaveAttract(){app.attract=false;app.session=null;app.lastInput=performance.now();go('title');}\nfunction act(action,element){\n  sound.unlock();sound.effect('select');app.lastInput=performance.now();\n  if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return;}\n  if(action==='title'){app.session=null;app.medley=null;app.guest=null;go('title');}\n  else if(action==='slots')go('slots');\n  else if(action==='slot'){app.guest=null;app.slot=Number(element.dataset.index);if(!app.profiles[app.slot])app.profiles[app.slot]=makeProfile(`PLAYER ${app.slot+1}`);save();go('island');}\n  else if(action==='dropin'){app.guest=makeProfile('GUEST');app.guest.day=7;app.guest.revealed=true;app.returnScreen='island';go('island');}\n  else if(action==='island'){app.medley=null;app.weigh=null;go('island');}\n  else if(action==='intro'){app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===element.dataset.id);app.returnScreen='island';app.hard=false;sound.effect('voice');go('intro');}\n  else if(action==='hard'){app.hard=!app.hard;render();}\n  else if(action==='start')begin(app.activity);\n  else if(action==='weigh'){app.weigh=[];startWeigh();}\n  else if(action==='finale'){app.activity={...ACTIVITIES[0],id:'finale',name:'The Long Stand',place:'Pavilion',duration:45,ring:.32,quip:'A LITTLE HONESTY GOES A LONG WAY.'};app.returnScreen='island';go('intro');}\n  else if(action==='continue')go('island');\n  else if(action==='day-report')go('day-report');\n  else if(action==='next-day'){if(profile().day<7)profile().day++;save();go('island');}\n  else if(action==='family'){const seed=Math.floor(Math.random()*4294967296);app.medley={members:[],scores:[],seed,event:0,picks:pickMedley(seededRandom(seed)),padButtons:{},padEdges:{}};go('family');}\n  else if(action==='family-join')familyJoin('keyboard');\n  else if(action==='family-bot')familyJoin('bot');\n  else if(action==='family-start'&&app.medley.members.length)startMedley();\n  else if(action==='settings'){app.settingsFrom=app.screen;go('settings');}\n  else if(action==='settings-back')go(app.screen==='dev'?'pause':app.settingsFrom||'title');\n  else if(action==='dev')go('dev');\n  else if(action==='reset-tuning'){app.tuning={...DEFAULT_TUNABLES};if(app.session)app.session.tuning={...app.tuning};render();}\n  else if(action==='resume'){app.paused=false;go('game');}\n  else if(action==='leave'){app.session=null;app.medley=null;app.weigh=null;go(profile()?'island':'title');}\n  else if(action==='about')go('about');\n  else if(action==='hub-ready')globalThis.AIHub?.answer('ready');\n  else if(action==='hub-more')globalThis.AIHub?.answer('more');\n}\nui.addEventListener('click',event=>{const target=event.target.closest('[data-action]');if(target)act(target.dataset.action,target);});\nui.addEventListener('pointerover',event=>{const target=event.target.closest('button');if(target){ui.querySelectorAll('button.focused').forEach(item=>item.classList.remove('focused'));target.classList.add('focused');app.focus=Array.from(ui.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled)')).indexOf(target);}});\nui.addEventListener('input',event=>{const target=event.target;if(target.dataset.setting){const key=target.dataset.setting;app.settings[key]=target.type==='checkbox'?target.checked:target.type==='range'?Number(target.value):target.value;save();document.body.classList.toggle('high-contrast',app.settings.contrast);document.body.classList.toggle('reduce-motion',app.settings.motion);}if(target.dataset.tune){app.tuning[target.dataset.tune]=Number(target.value);if(app.session)app.session.tuning={...app.tuning};}});\nfunction menuMove(delta){const buttons=Array.from(ui.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled)'));if(!buttons.length)return;app.focus=(app.focus+delta+buttons.length)%buttons.length;buttons.forEach((item,index)=>item.classList.toggle('focused',index===app.focus));buttons[app.focus].focus();buttons[app.focus].scrollIntoView({block:'nearest'});}\nfunction pause(){if(app.screen==='game'&&!app.attract&&!app.hubRound){app.paused=true;go('pause');}else if(app.screen==='pause')act('resume');}\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(app.screen!=='family'||event.repeat)return;const key=event.key.toLowerCase();if(!['enter',' ','b','escape'].includes(key))return;event.preventDefault();event.stopImmediatePropagation();app.keyboardSeen=true;app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='keyboard';sound.unlock();if(key==='enter')familyJoin('keyboard');else if(key==='b')familyJoin('bot');else if(key===' '&&app.medley.members.length)startMedley();else if(key==='escape')act('title');},true);\nwindow.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(app.hubClosed)return;const wasNotice=notice();app.keyboardSeen=true;app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='keyboard';sound.unlock();if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return;}if(app.screen==='title'&&wasNotice)render();const key=event.key.toLowerCase();if(['arrowup','arrowdown','arrowleft','arrowright',' ','escape'].includes(key))event.preventDefault();if(event.repeat)return;if(app.screen==='hub-card'&&(key==='enter'||key==='m')){event.preventDefault();globalThis.AIHub?.answer(key==='m'?'more':'ready');return;}app.keys.add(key);if(app.screen==='game'){if(key==='f')app.input.left=true;if(key==='j')app.input.right=true;if(key==='escape')pause();}else if(!['INPUT','SELECT'].includes(document.activeElement?.tagName)){if(key==='arrowdown'||key==='s')menuMove(1);else if(key==='arrowup'||key==='w')menuMove(-1);else if(key==='enter'){event.preventDefault();const buttons=Array.from(ui.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled)'));buttons[app.focus]?.click();}else if(key==='escape'){const backButton=ui.querySelector('.back');if(backButton)backButton.click();else if(app.screen==='pause')pause();}}});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup',event=>app.keys.delete(event.key.toLowerCase()));\nwindow.addEventListener('blur',()=>app.keys.clear());\nwindow.addEventListener('pointerdown',event=>{app.lastInput=performance.now();if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return;}sound.unlock();if(event.pointerType==='mouse')app.inputKind='mouse';});\nui.addEventListener('pointermove',event=>{if(app.screen!=='game'||event.pointerType!=='mouse')return;const dial=event.target.closest('#dial');if(!dial)return;const rect=dial.getBoundingClientRect();app.mouse={x:Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,(event.clientX-rect.left-rect.width/2)/(rect.width/2))),y:Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,(event.clientY-rect.top-rect.height/2)/(rect.height/2)))};app.lastInput=performance.now();});\nwindow.addEventListener('gamepadconnected',()=>{app.lastInput=performance.now();if(app.screen==='title')render();});\n\nfunction gamepad(){if(app.medley&&['family','game'].includes(app.screen))return null;const pad=Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.()||[]).find(Boolean);if(!pad)return null;const down=index=>!!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed;const just=index=>down(index)&&!app.gamepadButtons[index];if(just(9)){app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='gamepad';pause();}if(app.screen==='hub-card'&&just(3))globalThis.AIHub?.answer('more');if(app.screen!=='game'){if(just(12))menuMove(-1);if(just(13))menuMove(1);if(just(0)){const buttons=Array.from(ui.querySelectorAll('button:not(:disabled)'));buttons[app.focus]?.click();}if(just(1))ui.querySelector('.back')?.click();}else{if(just(4))app.input.left=true;if(just(5))app.input.right=true;}if(pad.axes.some(value=>Math.abs(value)>.2)||pad.buttons.some(item=>item.pressed)){app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='gamepad';if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return null;}}app.gamepadButtons=pad.buttons.map(item=>item.pressed);return pad;}\nfunction pollFamilyPads(){\n  if(!app.medley||!['family','game'].includes(app.screen))return;\n  const medley=app.medley;medley.padEdges={};\n  for(const pad of Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.()||[]).filter(Boolean)){\n    const previous=medley.padButtons[pad.index]||[],just=index=>!!pad.buttons[index]?.pressed&&!previous[index];\n    medley.padEdges[pad.index]={left:just(4),right:just(5)};medley.padButtons[pad.index]=pad.buttons.map(item=>item.pressed);\n    if(pad.axes.some(value=>Math.abs(value)>.2)||pad.buttons.some(item=>item.pressed)){app.lastInput=performance.now();app.inputKind='gamepad';}\n    if(app.screen==='family'){\n      if(just(0))familyJoin('pad',pad.index);\n      if(just(2))familyJoin('bot');\n      if(just(9)&&medley.members.length)startMedley();\n      if(just(1))act('title');\n    }else if(just(9)){app.gamepadButtons=pad.buttons.map(item=>item.pressed);pause();}\n  }\n}\nfunction activityCue(session){\n  const activity=session.activity,time=session.elapsed;\n  if(activity.family==='reps'){\n    const phase=(time/3.2)%1;\n    const target=phase<.4?phase/.4:phase<.55?1:phase<.9?1-(phase-.55)/.35:0;\n    return `MATCH ${Math.round(target*100)}% · YOU ${Math.round(session.rep*100)}%`;\n  }\n  if(activity.family==='header')return Math.floor(time/2.4)%2===0?'← HEAD LEFT':'HEAD RIGHT →';\n  if(activity.family==='step')return Math.abs(time/.7-Math.round(time/.7))<.23?'STEP NOW · F OR J':'WAIT FOR THE BEAT';\n  if(activity.family==='jog')return 'ALTERNATE F AND J';\n  if(activity.family==='slack')return 'F / J TO WALK THE LINE';\n  if(activity.family==='jump')return 'SPACE / R2 TO JUMP';\n  if(activity.family==='hoop')return `CIRCLE THE STICK · ${Math.round(session.hoopLift*100)}% LIFT`;\n  if(activity.breath)return Math.sin(time*Math.PI*2/activity.breath)>0?'BREATHE IN · HOLD':'BREATHE OUT · RELEASE';\n  return 'KEEP THE DOT INSIDE THE RING';\n}\nfunction updateFamily(dt){\n  const medley=app.medley,timeLabel=document.getElementById('family-time');\n  if(medley.phase==='break'){\n    medley.breakTime-=dt;\n    if(timeLabel)timeLabel.textContent=Math.max(0,Math.ceil(medley.breakTime));\n    if(medley.breakTime<=0){medley.event++;startMedley();}\n    return;\n  }\n  const pads=Array.from(navigator.getGamepads?.()||[]);\n  medley.sessions.forEach((session,index)=>{\n    const member=medley.members[index],pad=member.kind==='pad'?pads.find(item=>item?.index===member.index):null;\n    const input={x:0,y:0,breath:false,left:false,right:false};\n    if(member.kind==='keyboard'){\n      input.x=Number(app.keys.has('d')||app.keys.has('arrowright'))-Number(app.keys.has('a')||app.keys.has('arrowleft'));\n      input.y=Number(app.keys.has('s')||app.keys.has('arrowdown'))-Number(app.keys.has('w')||app.keys.has('arrowup'));\n      input.breath=app.keys.has(' ');input.left=app.input.left;input.right=app.input.right;\n    }else if(pad){\n      input.x=pad.axes[0]||0;input.y=pad.axes[1]||0;input.breath=!!pad.buttons[7]?.pressed;Object.assign(input,medley.padEdges[pad.index]);\n    }else if(member.kind==='bot'){\n      const time=session.elapsed,family=session.activity.family;\n      if(family==='hoop'){input.x=Math.cos(time*7);input.y=Math.sin(time*7);}\n      else if(family==='reps'){const phase=(time/3.2)%1;input.y=-(phase<.4?phase/.4:phase<.55?1:phase<.9?1-(phase-.55)/.35:0);}\n      else if(family==='header'){const beat=Math.floor((time+dt-1.2)/2.4);input.x=beat%2===0?-.8:.8;}\n      else{input.x=Math.sin(time)*.08;input.y=Math.cos(time)*.08;}\n      input.breath=session.activity.breath?Math.sin((time+dt)*Math.PI*2/session.activity.breath)>0:false;\n      if(Math.floor((time+dt)/.7)!==Math.floor(time/.7)){input.left=Math.floor((time+dt)/.7)%2===0;input.right=!input.left;}\n    }\n    session.update(dt,input);\n    const dot=document.getElementById(`family-dot-${index}`),score=document.getElementById(`family-score-${index}`),cue=document.getElementById(`family-cue-${index}`);\n    if(dot){dot.style.left=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,session.dot.x))*38}%`;dot.style.top=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,session.dot.y))*38}%`;}\n    if(score)score.textContent=medley.scores[index]+session.result().score*10;\n    if(cue)cue.textContent=activityCue(session);\n  });\n  app.input.left=false;app.input.right=false;\n  document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--avatar-lean',`${-app.session.dot.x*16}deg`);\n  if(timeLabel)timeLabel.textContent=Math.max(0,Math.ceil(app.session.duration-app.session.elapsed));\n  if(medley.sessions.every(session=>session.finished))finishFamilyEvent();\n}\nfunction frame(now){\n  const dt=Math.min(.05,(now-(app.previous||now))/1000);app.previous=now;sound.update(dt);\n  if(app.hubClosed){requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n  pollFamilyPads();\n  const pad=gamepad();\n  if(app.screen==='title'&&!globalThis.AIHub?.active&&now-app.lastInput>10000)startAttract();\n  if(app.screen==='game'&&app.medley){updateFamily(dt);requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n  if(app.screen==='game'&&app.session){\n    const seconds=document.getElementById('seconds');\n    if(app.hubRound&&!syncHub()){app.input.left=false;app.input.right=false;requestAnimationFrame(frame);return;}\n    let x=Number(app.keys.has('d')||app.keys.has('arrowright'))-Number(app.keys.has('a')||app.keys.has('arrowleft'));\n    let y=Number(app.keys.has('s')||app.keys.has('arrowdown'))-Number(app.keys.has('w')||app.keys.has('arrowup'));\n    if(pad&&(Math.abs(pad.axes[0])>.12||Math.abs(pad.axes[1])>.12)){x=pad.axes[0];y=pad.axes[1];}else if(app.inputKind==='mouse'&&app.mouse){x=app.mouse.x;y=app.mouse.y;}\n    if(app.attract){const time=app.session.elapsed;x=app.session.activity.family==='hoop'?Math.cos(time*7):Math.sin(time*1.2)*.2;y=app.session.activity.family==='hoop'?Math.sin(time*7):Math.cos(time)*.2;if(Math.floor(time*3)%2===0)app.input.left=true;else app.input.right=true;}\n    if(app.driver==='perfect'){x=0;y=0;}\n    app.session.update(dt,{x,y,breath:app.keys.has(' ')||!!pad?.buttons[7]?.pressed,left:app.input.left,right:app.input.right});app.input.left=false;app.input.right=false;\n    document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--avatar-lean',`${-app.session.dot.x*16}deg`);\n    const dot=document.getElementById('balance-dot'),meter=document.getElementById('meter'),score=document.getElementById('live-score'),cue=document.getElementById('live-cue'),dial=document.getElementById('dial');\n    if(dot){dot.style.left=`${50+app.session.dot.x*38}%`;dot.style.top=`${50+app.session.dot.y*38}%`;}\n    if(seconds)seconds.textContent=Math.max(0,Math.ceil(app.session.duration-app.session.elapsed));\n    if(meter)meter.style.width=`${Math.min(100,app.session.elapsed/app.session.duration*100)}%`;\n    if(score)score.textContent=`${app.session.result().score} POINTS · ${app.medley?`PLAYER ${app.medley.player+1}`:'KEEP GOING'}`;\n    if(cue)cue.textContent=activityCue(app.session);\n    if(dial&&app.hubRound){dial.querySelectorAll('.ghost-dot').forEach(node=>node.remove());for(const ghost of Object.values(app.hubScores).slice(0,3)){if(ghost?.a!==app.hubEvent||!Number.isFinite(ghost?.x)||!Number.isFinite(ghost?.y))continue;const marker=document.createElement('span');marker.className='ghost-dot';marker.style.left=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,ghost.x))*38}%`;marker.style.top=`${50+Math.max(-1,Math.min(1,ghost.y))*38}%`;dial.appendChild(marker);}}\n    if(app.session.finished&&!app.hubRound)finish();\n  }\n  requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n}\n\nfunction hubScore(){return app.hubTotal+(app.session?.result().score||0)*10;}\nfunction beginHubEvent(index){app.hubEvent=index;const activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===app.hubPicks[index]);begin(activity,{duration:EVENT_SECONDS,random:globalThis.AIHub.rng(`event:${index}`),hard:false,tuning:{...DEFAULT_TUNABLES,timeScale:1}});}\nfunction finishHub(){if(!app.hubRound||app.hubEnded)return;const score=hubScore();app.hubEnded=true;app.hubRound=false;clearInterval(app.hubTimer);globalThis.AIHub.result({score});app.result={score};go('hub-finished');}\nfunction syncHub(){\n  const window=medleyWindow(globalThis.AIHub.time());\n  if(window.phase==='finished'){finishHub();return false;}\n  if(window.index>app.hubEvent){app.hubTotal+=(app.session?.result().score||0)*10;beginHubEvent(window.index);}\n  if(window.phase!=='event'){\n    const seconds=document.getElementById('seconds'),cue=document.getElementById('live-cue');\n    if(seconds)seconds.textContent=Math.ceil(window.remaining);\n    if(cue)cue.textContent=window.phase==='countdown'?'GET READY · STARTING TOGETHER':`EVENT COMPLETE · NEXT IN ${Math.ceil(window.remaining)}`;\n    return false;\n  }\n  return true;\n}\nfunction sendHubState(){if(!app.hubRound||app.hubEnded||!app.session)return;const hub=globalThis.AIHub,score=hubScore();hub.progress({score,label:app.activity.name});hub.send({a:app.hubEvent,x:app.session.dot.x,y:app.session.dot.y,c:0,t:app.session.elapsed,s:score},{reliable:false});}\nfunction setupHub(){const hub=globalThis.AIHub;if(!hub?.active)return;hub.on('card',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;go('hub-card');});hub.on('start',()=>{app.hubClosed=false;app.hubRound=true;app.hubEnded=false;app.hubScores={};app.hubTotal=0;app.hubPicks=pickMedley(hub.rng('medley'));beginHubEvent(0);clearInterval(app.hubTimer);sendHubState();app.hubTimer=setInterval(sendHubState,100);});hub.on('message',(data,from)=>{app.hubScores[from]=data;});hub.on('time-up',finishHub);hub.on('end',()=>{clearInterval(app.hubTimer);app.hubRound=false;app.hubEnded=true;app.hubClosed=true;sound.context?.suspend();});hub.connect({mode:'ghost',seats:[1,4],card:true}).then(info=>{if(info)hub.ready();});}\nwindow.__GAME__={go:(screen,args={})=>{if(args.id)app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===args.id);if(screen==='game'&&app.activity)begin(app.activity);else go(screen);},state:()=>({screen:app.screen,day:profile()?.day,activity:app.activity?.id,elapsed:app.session?.elapsed,score:app.session?.result().score,attract:app.attract,profiles:app.profiles,hubScores:app.hubScores,family:app.medley?{phase:app.medley.phase,event:app.medley.event,players:app.medley.members.length,scores:[...app.medley.scores],picks:[...app.medley.picks],dots:app.medley.sessions?.map(session=>({x:session.dot.x,y:session.dot.y}))}:null}),setDriver:skill=>{app.driver=skill;},get tunables(){return app.tuning;},finishActivity:()=>{if(app.medley?.phase==='event'){app.medley.sessions.forEach(session=>{session.elapsed=session.duration;session.finished=true;});finishFamilyEvent();}else if(app.session){app.session.elapsed=app.session.duration;app.session.finished=true;finish();}},finishBreak:()=>{if(app.medley?.phase==='break'){app.medley.event++;startMedley();}}};\nrender();setupHub();startWorld(app).catch(error=>{console.warn('3D island unavailable:',error.message);});requestAnimationFrame(frame);\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_635","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/about.js\"; echo '\"'---'; sed -n '70,180p' TASK.md; echo '---'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/title.js\"; rg -n '\"'ABOUT|About|about|Family Hour|family-join|family-start|family-bot' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_635","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/about.js\"; echo '\"'---'; sed -n '70,180p' TASK.md; echo '---'; cat \\\"\"'$DEV/src/data/title.js\"; rg -n '\"'ABOUT|About|about|Family Hour|family-join|family-start|family-bot' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\"'","aggregated_output":"export const about = {\n  sourceInformation: {\n    date:'2026-11-04 22:18:46', source:'Wii Fit', plan:'PLAN.md', genre:'Sports',\n    perspective:'Isometric 3D island', tech:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, JavaScript, Web Audio',\n    artDirection:'Pastel, low-poly island and friendly, rounded fitness interface',\n    animation:'Procedural posing and three.js AnimationMixer',\n    audio:'Original procedural Web Audio music, effects, and syllabic character voice',\n    online:'AI Hub ghost session with score and position messages',\n    testing:'Automated simulation and browser checks; phone, tablet, desktop and WebKit viewport checks',\n    research:'Pixel Engine 0.46.0 documentation and AI Hub session protocol',\n    environment:'Codex CLI (headless); Linux', model:'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max', usage:'added on import'\n  },\n  testingFeedback:['See final testing report.','See final testing report.','Simulation and real-browser interaction.','Static inspection without running the game.'],\n  engineFeedback:['The compact scene lifecycle and built-in camera.','WebGPU availability varies between browsers.','The balance physics, activities and UI.','Validating WebGPU behavior across browser engines.','None; pixel-engine.js remains unchanged.','Provide an explicit supported fallback for browsers without WebGPU.'],\n  promptFeedback:['The emphasis on a playable, controller-first vertical slice.','The scope combines a large simulation, multiplayer and a standalone deliverable.','Balancing the breadth of activities with cross-browser verification.','Prioritize required features and define an explicit minimum for each.'],\n  aiHub:{name:'A Little Off Balance',tagline:'A very serious game about a very wobbly week.',description:'Balance, breathe, and bravely face a talking scale on a cozy island. Play a week of delightfully questionable fitness or challenge friends in a three-event medley.',type:'Game',genre:'Sports',source:'Wii Fit',series:'Wii Fit',players:'1–4',controls:'Left stick / WASD: lean; R2 / Space: breathe; L1/R1 or F/J: step; Escape / Options: pause.',tags:['3d','sports','comedy','arcade','versus']}\n};\n---\nScope\n\nCreate a feature-complete demo. Capture what makes the source distinctive (its world, characters, themes and tone) and turn it into the mechanics, pacing and UX of a great game. The demo must be long enough to show ALL features and gameplay mechanics so a player can clearly understand how the game plays and feels, and what they can and cannot do. Treat the demo as a complete, polished vertical slice. It should contain all the infrastructure, systems, and polish needed so the remainder of the game could later be built out with normal designer tools.\n\nInclude a dev mode, reachable from the pause menu, with the standard tools for testing the game quickly. Balance is key, so expose the most important gameplay variables as live sliders, with a reset to defaults.\n\nAttract Mode: After 10 seconds without input on the title/menu screen, start a looping AI-played demo or scripted replay (arcade/kiosk style); any input exits it. The AI (or replay) can be simple and may cheat freely (infinite health, ammo, abilities, no clip, etc). Its only job is to show as much of the demo as possible, the attract mode is not meant to balance the game.\n\nMultiplayer: Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\n\nNarrative tone: Use a writing style similar to the source’s.\n\n## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\nDesign the game around a PS5 DualSense (or any pad the browser reports in its standard mapping) played on a TV at 10 feet. With keyboard and mouse it's the same game on the same screens, not a separate desktop layout, but they should feel native, not like stand-ins for controller buttons. The keyboard uses the keys PC players expect for the genre. The mouse aims, looks, and clicks menu items and things in the world (hover moves the focus) wherever the genre uses it. On-screen prompts follow the input used last: PlayStation glyphs for the controller (with a Settings option to show Xbox glyphs, A B X Y, instead), keys and mouse buttons for keyboard and mouse.\n\nDo not use overly dense, web-style data screens.\n\nTouch-only devices: no touch controls; show \"Controller or keyboard required\" and the settings button. Let the attract mode run.\n\n## Done\nNo TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n---\nexport const TITLE = 'A Little Off Balance';\n5:import { about } from './data/about.js';\n32:    content=panel(`${brand}<h1 class=\"title\">${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(0,2).join(' '))}<br><span>${escape(TITLE.split(' ').slice(2).join(' '))}.</span></h1><p class=\"lede\">A week of movement, a talking scale, and absolutely no pressure to be graceful.</p><div class=\"title-tag\">YOUR ISLAND IS READY</div>${notice()?`<p class=\"description\" style=\"margin-top:18px\"><strong>Controller or keyboard required</strong></p><div class=\"menu\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}</div>`:`<div class=\"menu\">${button('Begin your week','slots','','primary')}<div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Drop-in','dropin','','ghost')}${button('Family Hour','family','','ghost')}</div><div class=\"menu-row\">${button('Settings','settings','','ghost')}${button('About','about','','ghost')}</div></div>${footer()}`}`,'title-screen')+`<div class=\"hero-note\">WELCOME TO LITTLE ISLAND<strong>Take it one wobble at a time.</strong>EST. WHENEVER YOU ARE READY</div>`;\n61:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">LOCAL MULTIPLAYER</span></div>${heading('PLAY TOGETHER','Family Hour','Join up to four players for three simultaneous events.')}<div class=\"family-roster\">${app.medley.members.map((member,index)=>`<span class=\"badge\">${familyName(member,index)} · ${member.kind==='pad'?`PAD ${member.index+1}`:member.kind.toUpperCase()}</span>`).join('')||'<span class=\"badge\">NO PLAYERS YET</span>'}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Join with keyboard','family-join','', 'ghost')}${button('Add a bot','family-bot','', 'ghost')}${button('Start the medley','family-start',app.medley.members.length?'':'disabled','primary')}</div><p class=\"family-help\">ENTER: join keyboard · CROSS / A: join controller<br>SPACE / OPTIONS: start · B: add bot</p>${footer()}`);\n69:  }else if(app.screen==='about'){\n71:    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">CREDITS</span></div>${heading('THE FINE PRINT','About the island','A Little Off Balance is a playful tribute, not medical advice.')}<div class=\"about-text\">${section('Source Information',Object.entries(about.sourceInformation).map(([key,value])=>`${key}: ${value}`))}${section('Testing Feedback',about.testingFeedback)}${section('Engine Feedback',about.engineFeedback)}${section('Prompt Feedback',about.promptFeedback)}</div>${footer()}`);\n131:  else if(action==='family-join')familyJoin('keyboard');\n132:  else if(action==='family-bot')familyJoin('bot');\n133:  else if(action==='family-start'&&app.medley.members.length)startMedley();\n140:  else if(action==='about')go('about');\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
