{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_649","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i -C 3 'about|credits|source information|testing feedback|engine feedback|prompt feedback|family hour|scroll' PLAN.md TASK.md | tail -180; DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; sed -n '62,76p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\"; sed -n '\"'108,146p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\" | cut -c1-1000; cat \"$DEV/src/ui/overrides.css\" | tail -c 4500'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_649","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n -i -C 3 'about|credits|source information|testing feedback|engine feedback|prompt feedback|family hour|scroll' PLAN.md TASK.md | tail -180; DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; sed -n '62,76p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\"; sed -n '\"'108,146p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/main.js\" | cut -c1-1000; cat \"$DEV/src/ui/overrides.css\" | tail -c 4500'","aggregated_output":"PLAN.md-426-- How many stairs is too many? *One. / All of them. / Depends who's watching.*\nPLAN.md:427:- How do you feel about your ankles? *Fine. / We don't speak. / Which ones?*\nPLAN.md-428-- What is your relationship with the floor? *Distant. / Improving. / It's complicated.*\nPLAN.md-429-- If your knees could talk, what would they say? *Please. / Why. / Nothing. They've given up.*\nPLAN.md-430-- Day 7: Are you happy? *Yes. / No. / Is this graded?* → \"It's all graded.\"\n--\nPLAN.md-440-- **Use `aspect: 'fill'` ✔.** It removes letterboxing at every window size (`adaptive` gives thick black borders at 1280×720). Art size then varies: 480×270 at 1080p and 4K, 427×240 at 720p, 640×360 in a small frame, 400×300 at 800×600. **Lay out from `hud.width` and `hud.height` with anchors**, never fixed coordinates. Keep a 12 art px safe margin.\nPLAN.md-441-- **Pointer to art pixels ✔:** `ax = (p.x + 1) / 2 * hud.width; ay = (1 - p.y) / 2 * hud.height`. The HUD canvas ignores pointer events, and its rect equals the game canvas's.\nPLAN.md-442-- **Text:** the 5×7 font at scale 1 is 20×28 px at 1080p, the minimum. Scale 2 for menu rows and headings, 3-4 for the title and big numbers.\nPLAN.md:443:- **No dense screens:** at most 8 menu rows; at most 3 lines of dialogue; one idea per screen; one activity per records page. Page rather than scroll, wherever you can.\nPLAN.md-444-\nPLAN.md-445-### Mixed-case text ✔\nPLAN.md-446-\n--\nPLAN.md-486-| Hub: jump, wave, sit | ✕, △, □ (A, Y, X) | Space, V, B | Click to walk |\nPLAN.md-487-\nPLAN.md-488-- **Hero wrapper ✔:** call `readMoveInput(ctx, hero, input)`, then OR in `PadCross` (`consumePress` → `input.jump`, `isDown` → `input.jumpHeld`) and the same for wave and sit. In the hub ✕ interacts when a prompt is showing, otherwise jumps.\nPLAN.md:489:- **Menus** read the d-pad, stick (with repeat), arrows and WASD. Hover moves focus; left click confirms; a wheel scrolls lists; sliders drag.\nPLAN.md-490-- **Keep the mouse native:** the Dot follows the mouse as soon as the mouse moves, and goes back to stick or keys as soon as those are used.\nPLAN.md-491-- **Respect the hub's chord:** ignore Options while Create is held.\nPLAN.md-492-\n--\nPLAN.md-497-\nPLAN.md-498-### Screens\nPLAN.md-499-\nPLAN.md:500:- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\nPLAN.md-501-- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\nPLAN.md-502-- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\nPLAN.md-503-- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\n--\nPLAN.md-506-\nPLAN.md-507-`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\nPLAN.md-508-\nPLAN.md:509:Resume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\nPLAN.md-510-\nPLAN.md-511-### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\nPLAN.md-512-\n--\nPLAN.md-542-\nPLAN.md-543-After **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\nPLAN.md-544-\nPLAN.md:545:- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\nPLAN.md-546-- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \"Press any button.\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\"This is a recording...\").\nPLAN.md-547-- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\nPLAN.md-548-- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\n--\nPLAN.md-555-\nPLAN.md-556-### The Medley\nPLAN.md-557-\nPLAN.md:558:Three events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\"Stillest\", \"Most Apologetic\") and Ounce's remarks.\nPLAN.md-559-\nPLAN.md:560:### On its own: Family Hour\nPLAN.md-561-\nPLAN.md-562-Join screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\nPLAN.md-563-\n--\nPLAN.md-647-\nPLAN.md-648-```js\nPLAN.md-649-export const ounce = model({\nPLAN.md:650:  id: 'ounce', about: 'Ounce: a mint retro bathroom scale whose round dial is its face', tags: ['character'], size: [1.1, 1.05, 1.1],\nPLAN.md-651-  palette: { body: 'cyan', base: 'teal', tread: 'sky', face: 'white', rim: 'slate', tick: 'mist', needle: 'red', eye: 'ink' },\nPLAN.md-652-  parts: [\nPLAN.md-653-    { name: 'base', box: [1.04, 0.08, 1.04], at: [0, 0.04, 0], c: 'base' },\n--\nPLAN.md-677-\nPLAN.md-678-### Surfaces and scene effects\nPLAN.md-679-\nPLAN.md:680:- **Tile floor ✔:** `textureDef({ id:'clinic-tile', size:[16,16], tile:true, palette:{ grout:'mist', a:'white', b:'white' }, layers:[{ pattern:'tiles', colors:['grout','a','b'], w:16, h:16, mortar:1, seed:3 }], about:'...', tags:['floor'] })`, added to `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`. **Never stretch a map over a box ✔** (it gave one giant tile): use a `PlaneGeometry` and scale its UVs by metres ÷ (16 / `DEFAULT_TEXEL`), as the kit's market example does.\nPLAN.md-681-- **World:** `WaterSurface` ✔, `GrassField` ✔, sand and lawn as flat boxes ✔, `RippleField` at splashes, `Precipitation` in the finale, `Boids` gulls, `Decals` footprints on sand.\nPLAN.md-682-- **Light:** `ctx.lights` for pavilion lanterns at dusk; `applySky(skyAt(h))` for morning and evening.\nPLAN.md-683-- **Game feel:** `hitstop`, `shake`, `screen.flash`, `screen.shockwave` on the splash, iris transitions (`screen.cover`/`reveal` ✔, also resolve headless), `Trail` behind the jogger, custom particles ('sweat' in cyan, 'confetti', 'splash', 'zen' motes).\n--\nPLAN.md-721-### Music\nPLAN.md-722-\nPLAN.md-723-- **`ctx.audio.setVolume('music', savedMusic ?? 0.10)` at boot, every boot**, from your own settings key. The engine's default is 60%, and its stored volume key (`pixel-engine:audio`) is shared by every engine game on the origin, so don't rely on it.\nPLAN.md:724:- **Write instruments loud:** track `volume` 0.45-0.8. The kit's examples use about 0.12, written for a 60% bus; at 10% × master .8 that is near silence. A test checks each song: sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 ≥ 0.03.\nPLAN.md-725-- Songs are `Song` data, in `src/audio/songs.js`, each original, none imitating the source:\nPLAN.md-726-\nPLAN.md-727-| Song | Feel |\nPLAN.md-728-|---|---|\nPLAN.md:729:| Title / Plaza | gentle waiting-room bossa, about 92 BPM, soft triangle plucks |\nPLAN.md-730-| Holding Still | slow, sparse, breath-paced, 60 BPM |\nPLAN.md-731-| Rep Shed | light funk bass, 110 BPM |\nPLAN.md-732-| Beat Beach (Hoop) and Step Class | bright, four-on-the-floor; Step is 104 BPM exactly |\n--\nPLAN.md-772-src/audio/     voice.js songs.js sfx.js\nPLAN.md-773-src/art/       avatar.js models.js textures.js clips.js glyphs.js portraits.js\nPLAN.md-774-src/data/      title.js activities.js poses.js reps.js charts.js boards.js week.js lines.js\nPLAN.md:775:               questions.js unlocks.js classmates.js stations.js medley.js about.js\nPLAN.md-776-src/scenes/    base.js boot.js title.js attract.js hub.js weighin.js report.js locker.js records.js jar.js\nPLAN.md-777-               card.js medley.js join.js ending.js  activity/{base,poses,reps,hoop,step,header,slackline,tray,jog,pier,longstand}.js\nPLAN.md-778-tools/         build.mjs test.mjs clip-sheet.mjs shot.mjs\n--\nPLAN.md-786-- Each scene is a `Game`, swapped with `engine.loadGame(scene, { camera })`. It frees everything per level; keep persistent state in `App`. Transition: `await screen.cover('iris')`, `await loadGame`, `await screen.reveal('iris')`.\nPLAN.md-787-- `BaseScene` owns the frame order: `update` → `App.device.update` → overlays (pause, dialogue, dev) take input first → the scene's own update → `hud.clear()` → scene draw → overlays draw. Gameplay goes in `fixedUpdate`, skipped automatically while `timeScale` is 0.\nPLAN.md-788-- **Rules from the guide that matter here:** gameplay in `fixedUpdate` with `consumePress`; `wasPressed` only in `update`; all randomness from `ctx.random` forks (never `Math.random`); time from `ctx.time` (never `performance.now`); no `new PointLight`. Modules guard `document`, `window`, `navigator` and `localStorage`, so **everything runs in Node** ✔.\nPLAN.md:789:- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\nPLAN.md-790-- **Debug API**, kept in the shipped game (`globalThis.__GAME__ = App`): `go(id, args)`, `state()` as JSON, `setDriver(skill)`, `tunables`. Give every scene a real `status()` line (`activity hoop | play | t 31.2 | score 412`) and a `fingerprint()` (score, Dot state).\nPLAN.md-791-\nPLAN.md-792----\nPLAN.md-793-\nPLAN.md-794-## 17. Verified recipes\nPLAN.md-795-\nPLAN.md:796:### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\nPLAN.md-797-\nPLAN.md-798-```js\nPLAN.md-799-// tools/build.mjs (esbuild is on this machine)\n--\nPLAN.md-813-writeFileSync(OUTPUT_HTML, html);   // OUTPUT_HTML: the deliverable name your brief gives, in root\nPLAN.md-814-```\nPLAN.md-815-\nPLAN.md:816:The session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Output is about 5.4 MB.\nPLAN.md-817-\nPLAN.md-818-### Browser flags ✔\nPLAN.md-819-\n--\nPLAN.md-868-\nPLAN.md-869-### Headless facts ✔\nPLAN.md-870-\nPLAN.md:871:- 600 frames with mixers takes about 80 ms, and boot about 240 ms, so full playthroughs are cheap.\nPLAN.md-872-- `Engine.headless(game, { camera })`: built-ins load with no asset reader.\nPLAN.md-873-- `recording()` and `replay()` reproduce the fingerprint across `loadGame`.\nPLAN.md-874-- `input.setPointer(x, y, true)` drives the mouse.\n--\nPLAN.md-886-2. **Clips:** `validateClip` empty and `analyzeClip(...).problems` empty for every clip you wrote.\nPLAN.md-887-3. **Data:** every model (`checkModel`) and texture (`validateTexture`) clean; all ids resolve; `parseSong` on every song; each song passes the level check in §15; every line fits its box; every character of every string has a glyph.\nPLAN.md-888-4. **Every activity:** idle bot finishes with 0★ and no error; expert bot ≥ 2★ (≥ 3★ on easy ones); sloppy < expert; result written; Drips correct.\nPLAN.md:889:5. **Full scripted playthrough:** drive the real menus with `setKey` from a fresh save, bots inside activities: new week → all 7 days → every station → goals → unlock schedule → Jar milestones → Long Stand → confession subtracts exactly 7 → credits → Week 2. Assert the state at each step.\nPLAN.md-890-6. **Save:** reload mid-week restores; corrupt JSON falls back safely; no storage works.\nPLAN.md-891-7. **Pause:** `timeScale` 0, `fixedUpdate` frozen, menu navigable, resume exact.\nPLAN.md-892-8. **Dev:** every slider changes live behaviour; reset restores defaults; every tool works.\n--\nPLAN.md-901-14. Boots on WebGPU with no errors; title visible; **music volume is exactly 0.10** on first run.\nPLAN.md-902-15. Pad stub: ✕ confirms; prompts show PlayStation glyphs; the Settings option gives Xbox; a key press switches to keycaps; mouse move switches to mouse prompts; hover moves focus; click activates. Record each prompt state in `App.state()` so no picture is needed.\nPLAN.md-903-16. Phone profile with touch: message showing, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract runs.\nPLAN.md:904:17. Family Hour with 2 stub pads plus keyboard: three lanes move independently.\nPLAN.md-905-18. Audio after a real click: an `AnalyserNode` on the destination reads non-silent for SFX and music; voice in `OfflineAudioContext` has RMS > .02, and Ounce's mean pitch exceeds Coach's.\nPLAN.md-906-19. No layout overflow at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 640×360: widgets record their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\nPLAN.md-907-20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no `navigator.gpu` on this machine ✔, so they can only test failure: the engine's \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable\" message shows ✔ and no page error is thrown. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\n--\nPLAN.md-922-3. **One activity, fully.** Holding Still end to end with avatars, Coach, results, voice and music. **Stop and judge the feel here**, since this is the whole game in miniature: check the bot table, then capture a run as frames and confirm the body language reads the Dot.\nPLAN.md-923-4. **The island and the week.** Hub, Weigh-In, stations, Report, Jar, schedule, saves. Scripted playthrough started.\nPLAN.md-924-5. **Other activities**, in this order: Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Tray, Pier Jump, Jog.\nPLAN.md:925:6. **The Medley.** Lanes, Family Hour, session card, ghosts. Harness at full spec.\nPLAN.md-926-7. **Attract, Dev tools tab, touch-only, Locker Room, Hall of Numbers.**\nPLAN.md-927-8. **The story and the finish.** Ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession, ending; line bank to 120+; all songs; every model and particle.\nPLAN.md:928:9. **Wrap-up.** About & Credits, exit interview, final tests, one look at each screen at 1920×1080.\nPLAN.md-929-\nPLAN.md:930:**If you must cut scope,** remove whole activities from the data, in this order: Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage. Nothing half-built ships, and nothing may look stubbed. **Never cut:** the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, the Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, About.\nPLAN.md-931-\nPLAN.md-932----\nPLAN.md-933-\n--\nPLAN.md-935-\nPLAN.md-936-**No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or dead menu items.** Every screen works with pad, keyboard and mouse.\nPLAN.md-937-\nPLAN.md:938:### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\nPLAN.md-939-\nPLAN.md:940:Credits; \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"; **Source Information** (every field your brief lists; `unknown` for anything you can't confirm; Usage: `added on import`); **Testing Feedback**; **Engine Feedback**; **Prompt Feedback**; the kit's `CREDITS.md`, shipped as the kit asks: a summary page, then the full text in a scrollable view.\nPLAN.md-941-\nPLAN.md:942:**Keep one source of truth:** `src/data/about.js` feeds the screen, and `tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview file from it, then re-parses it to confirm it is valid JSON. Answer the feedback questions honestly, from your real run, not from this plan.\nPLAN.md-943-\nPLAN.md:944:For Source Information: Source is Wii Fit; Genre and Perspective as in section 1; Tech: Pixel Engine with its version, three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it, esbuild for packaging; Art: the engine's native pixel look; Animation: engine `ClipDef`s with `AnimationMixer`; Audio: engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant voice; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local. For Research, describe what you did yourself, and note that the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\nPLAN.md-945-\nPLAN.md-946-### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\nPLAN.md-947-\n--\nPLAN.md-954-\nPLAN.md-955-### Your final chat reply\nPLAN.md-956-\nPLAN.md:957:It must contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as your brief says.\nPLAN.md-958-\nPLAN.md-959----\nPLAN.md-960-\n--\nPLAN.md-988-| No dense web-style screens | §9 |\nPLAN.md-989-| Touch-only: no touch controls, message, settings button, attract runs | §9, §18 test 16 |\nPLAN.md-990-| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §19, §20 |\nPLAN.md:991:| Source Information and all feedback in the chat reply and About/Credits | §20 |\nPLAN.md-992-| Exit interview in the exact shape, parses as JSON | §20 |\n  }else if(app.screen==='medley-board'){\n    const ranking=app.medley.scores.map((score,index)=>({score,index})).sort((left,right)=>right.score-left.score);\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\"><span class=\"badge sun\">FAMILY HOUR</span></div>${heading('MEDLEY COMPLETE','A standing ovation.','A little wobble is better together.')}<div class=\"stack\">${ranking.map((entry,index)=>`<div class=\"list-item\"><span class=\"icon\">${index+1}</span><span><span class=\"name\">${familyName(app.medley.members[entry.index],entry.index)}</span><span class=\"sub\">${entry.score} POINTS</span></span></div>`).join('')}</div><div class=\"menu\">${button('Back to title','title','','primary')}</div>`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='settings'||app.screen==='dev'){\n    const dev=app.screen==='dev';\n    const ranges=dev?Object.entries(app.tuning).map(([key,value])=>`<div class=\"field\"><label for=\"${key}\">${escape(key)}</label><input id=\"${key}\" data-tune=\"${key}\" type=\"range\" min=\"${key==='timeScale'?.25:0}\" max=\"${key==='timeScale'?4:key==='dotLag'?.5:8}\" step=\".01\" value=\"${value}\"></div>`).join(''):`<div class=\"field\"><label for=\"music\">Music ${Math.round(app.settings.music*100)}%</label><input id=\"music\" data-setting=\"music\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\".05\" value=\"${app.settings.music}\"></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"effects\">Effects ${Math.round(app.settings.effects*100)}%</label><input id=\"effects\" data-setting=\"effects\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"1\" step=\".05\" value=\"${app.settings.effects}\"></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"glyphs\">Controller prompts</label><select id=\"glyphs\" data-setting=\"glyphs\"><option value=\"ps\" ${app.settings.glyphs==='ps'?'selected':''}>PlayStation</option><option value=\"xbox\" ${app.settings.glyphs==='xbox'?'selected':''}>Xbox</option></select></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"contrast\">High contrast</label><input id=\"contrast\" data-setting=\"contrast\" type=\"checkbox\" ${app.settings.contrast?'checked':''}></div><div class=\"field\"><label for=\"motion\">Reduce motion</label><input id=\"motion\" data-setting=\"motion\" type=\"checkbox\" ${app.settings.motion?'checked':''}></div>`;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('settings-back')}<span class=\"badge\">${dev?'LIVE TUNING':'MAKE YOURSELF COMFORTABLE'}</span></div>${heading(dev?'DEVELOPER TOOLS':'YOUR PREFERENCES',dev?'Tune the wobble.':'Settings',dev?'Changes apply immediately, including during a paused practice.':'Make the island feel like yours.')}<div class=\"stack\">${ranges}</div><div class=\"menu\">${dev?button('Reset tuning','reset-tuning','','ghost'):''}${button('Done','settings-back','','primary')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='about'){\n    const section=(title,entries)=>`<h3>${title}</h3>${entries.map(entry=>`<p>${escape(entry)}</p>`).join('')}`;\n    content=panel(`<div class=\"topline\">${back('title')}<span class=\"badge\">CREDITS</span></div>${heading('THE FINE PRINT','About the island','A Little Off Balance is a playful tribute, not medical advice.')}<div class=\"about-text\">${section('Source Information',Object.entries(about.sourceInformation).map(([key,value])=>`${key}: ${value}`))}${section('Testing Feedback',about.testingFeedback)}${section('Engine Feedback',about.engineFeedback)}${section('Prompt Feedback',about.promptFeedback)}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='hub-card'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('AI HUB · GHOST MEDLEY','Ready to wobble?','Three events, one shared clock. Earn points and watch your fellow islanders as ghosts.')}<div class=\"menu\">${button('Ready','hub-ready','','primary')}${button('I need more time','hub-more','','ghost')}</div>${footer()}`);\n  }else if(app.screen==='hub-finished'){\n    content=panel(`${brand}${heading('AI HUB · GHOST MEDLEY','Well wobbled.','Your score is in. The hub will show the final standings.')}<div class=\"badge sun\">${app.result?.score||0} POINTS</div>`);\n  }\n  medley.sessions.forEach((session,index)=>{medley.scores[index]+=session.result().score*10;});\n  if(medley.event===2){go('medley-board');return;}\n  medley.phase='break';medley.breakTime=BREAK_SECONDS;render();\n}\nfunction startAttract(){app.attract=true;const sequence=['tree','hoop','step','header','slackline'];const activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===sequence[app.attractIndex%sequence.length]);begin(activity,{duration:12});}\nfunction leaveAttract(){app.attract=false;app.session=null;app.lastInput=performance.now();go('title');}\nfunction act(action,element){\n  sound.unlock();sound.effect('select');app.lastInput=performance.now();\n  if(app.attract){leaveAttract();return;}\n  if(action==='title'){app.session=null;app.medley=null;app.guest=null;go('title');}\n  else if(action==='slots')go('slots');\n  else if(action==='slot'){app.guest=null;app.slot=Number(element.dataset.index);if(!app.profiles[app.slot])app.profiles[app.slot]=makeProfile(`PLAYER ${app.slot+1}`);save();go('island');}\n  else if(action==='dropin'){app.guest=makeProfile('GUEST');app.guest.day=7;app.guest.revealed=true;app.returnScreen='island';go('island');}\n  else if(action==='island'){app.medley=null;app.weigh=null;go('island');}\n  else if(action==='intro'){app.activity=ACTIVITIES.find(item=>item.id===element.dataset.id);app.returnScreen='island';app.hard=false;sound.effect('voice');go('intro');}\n  else if(action==='hard'){app.hard=!app.hard;render();}\n  else if(action==='start')begin(app.activity);\n  else if(action==='weigh'){app.weigh=[];startWeigh();}\n  else if(action==='finale'){app.activity={...ACTIVITIES[0],id:'finale',name:'The Long Stand',place:'Pavilion',duration:45,ring:.32,quip:'A LITTLE HONESTY GOES A LONG WAY.'};app.returnScreen='island';go('intro');}\n  else if(action==='continue')go('island');\n  else if(action==='day-report')go('day-report');\n  else if(action==='next-day'){if(profile().day<7)profile().day++;save();go('island');}\n  else if(action==='family'){const seed=Math.floor(Math.random()*4294967296);app.medley={members:[],scores:[],seed,event:0,picks:pickMedley(seededRandom(seed)),padButtons:{},padEdges:{}};go('family');}\n  else if(action==='family-join')familyJoin('keyboard');\n  else if(action==='family-bot')familyJoin('bot');\n  else if(action==='family-start'&&app.medley.members.length)startMedley();\n  else if(action==='settings'){app.settingsFrom=app.screen;go('settings');}\n  else if(action==='settings-back')go(app.screen==='dev'?'pause':app.settingsFrom||'title');\n  else if(action==='dev')go('dev');\n  else if(action==='reset-tuning'){app.tuning={...DEFAULT_TUNABLES};if(app.sessi