{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_653","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '90,160p' TASK.md; sed -n '938,958p' PLAN.md; DEV='A Little Off Balance-Wii Fit-gpt-6.1-terra-max-20261104-221846'; sed -n '1,160p' \\\"\"'$DEV/src/world.js\" | head -90; sed -n '\"'1,80p' \\\"\"'$DEV/package.json\"'","aggregated_output":"No TODOs, placeholders, or stubbed features. The demo is complete.\n\n## Source Information\nCRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n- Date: 2026-11-04 22:18:46\n- Source: the work it's based on\n- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\n- Genre and Perspective: genre and camera perspective used\n- Tech: stack, libraries/engines, with versions if applicable\n- Art Direction: style used\n- Animation: system used\n- Audio: music, sound effects and voice used\n- Online: network features used, or none\n- Testing: testing parameters allowed\n- Research: research done, or none\n- Environment: Codex CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: OpenAI, gpt-6.1-terra, reasoning effort max\n- Usage: write \"added on import\". You can't see your own cost, so don't estimate it: the runner records the real cost, tokens and time, and the agent that imports the game into AI Hub puts them on your About/Credits screen.\n\nExit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\"date\": \"\", \"source\": \"\", \"plan\": \"\", \"genre\": \"\", \"perspective\": \"\", \"tech\": \"\", \"artDirection\": \"\", \"animation\": \"\", \"audio\": \"\", \"online\": \"\", \"testing\": \"\", \"research\": \"\", \"environment\": \"\", \"model\": \"\", \"usage\": \"added on import\"},\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Testing Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Engine Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\"your answer to each Prompt Feedback question, in order\"],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"the game's title, as on its title screen\",\n    \"tagline\": \"a few words to go under the title\",\n    \"description\": \"one or two sentences for the catalogue\",\n    \"type\": \"Game, Tech demo or Tool\",\n    \"genre\": \"one of Action, Adventure, Fighting, Flight, Horror, Kids & Learning, Life Sim, Platformer, Puzzle, Racing, RPG, Shooter, Simulation, Sports, Stealth, Strategy\",\n    \"source\": \"the work it's based on, e.g. Moby-Dick\",\n    \"series\": \"its franchise, e.g. Star Fox, or empty\",\n    \"players\": \"how many can play: 1, 1–2 or 1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"the controls, in one line\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3 to 6 lowercase tags, e.g. 2d, 3d, arcade, story, co-op, versus, first-person, third-person, top-down, side-scrolling, pixel art, low-poly, retro, sci-fi, fantasy, comedy, vehicles, boss fights, exploration\"]\n  }\n}\nThe catalogue's model, effort, CLI, date and usage come from the run's record after you finish, so they aren't asked here.\n\nTesting Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch?\n- How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?\n- What was the most helpful test you ran?\n- What was the least helpful test you ran?\n\nEngine Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about the engine?\n- Did you get stuck or guess wrong?\n- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\n- What was the hardest part about using the engine?\n- What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)\n- If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?\n\nPrompt Feedback\n\n- What did you like most about this prompt?\n- What was confusing?\n- What was the hardest thing to do?\n- What would you change in this prompt?\n### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\n\nCredits; \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"; **Source Information** (every field your brief lists; `unknown` for anything you can't confirm; Usage: `added on import`); **Testing Feedback**; **Engine Feedback**; **Prompt Feedback**; the kit's `CREDITS.md`, shipped as the kit asks: a summary page, then the full text in a scrollable view.\n\n**Keep one source of truth:** `src/data/about.js` feeds the screen, and `tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview file from it, then re-parses it to confirm it is valid JSON. Answer the feedback questions honestly, from your real run, not from this plan.\n\nFor Source Information: Source is Wii Fit; Genre and Perspective as in section 1; Tech: Pixel Engine with its version, three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it, esbuild for packaging; Art: the engine's native pixel look; Animation: engine `ClipDef`s with `AnimationMixer`; Audio: engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant voice; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local. For Research, describe what you did yourself, and note that the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n\n### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\n\nUse the exact shape in your brief. Suggested values:\n\n- `name`: {TITLE}; `tagline`: yours.\n- `type`: `Game`; `genre`: `Sports`; `source`: `Wii Fit`; `series`: `Wii Fit`; `players`: `1–4`.\n- `controls`: `Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.`\n- `tags`: `[\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"3d\", \"story\"]`.\n\n### Your final chat reply\n\nIt must contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as your brief says.\n\nimport { Engine, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\n\nconst { BoxGeometry, CylinderGeometry, SphereGeometry, ConeGeometry, Mesh, Group, Vector3 } = THREE;\n\nclass IslandScene {\n  name = 'A Little Off Balance';\n  target = new Vector3(0, .6, 0);\n  constructor(game) { this.game = game; }\n  setup({ scene, engine }) {\n    engine.sun.intensity = 1.8;\n    const material = color => toonMaterial(color);\n    const box = (parent, color, size, position) => {\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(...size), material(color));\n      mesh.position.set(...position); mesh.castShadow = true; mesh.receiveShadow = true; parent.add(mesh); return mesh;\n    };\n    const cylinder = (parent, color, top, bottom, height, position, sides = 24) => {\n      const mesh = new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(top, bottom, height, sides), material(color));\n      mesh.position.set(...position); mesh.castShadow = true; mesh.receiveShadow = true; parent.add(mesh); return mesh;\n    };\n    cylinder(scene, 0xc8a578, 5.6, 5.15, .65, [0, -.38, 0], 48);\n    cylinder(scene, 0x8cbe8b, 5.5, 5.6, .18, [0, 0, 0], 48);\n    cylinder(scene, 0xf5e3bc, 2.45, 2.45, .035, [0, .11, .1], 48);\n    for (const [x,z,scale] of [[-4,-2,1.1],[-3.8,2.5,.8],[3.5,-2.8,1],[4.2,2,.85],[-1,-4.4,.8]]) {\n      cylinder(scene, 0x9a795d, .12, .18, 1.2*scale, [x,.6*scale,z], 8);\n      const crown = new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(.65*scale, 9, 7), material(0x5c9c70)); crown.position.set(x,1.45*scale,z); crown.castShadow=true; scene.add(crown);\n    }\n    for (const [x,z,color] of [[-2.7,-2.5,0xe38c70],[2.5,-2.7,0xe9b96f],[3.1,.45,0x82aec1]]) {\n      box(scene, 0xf7e8cf, [1.4,1.1,1.15], [x,.67,z]);\n      const roof=new Mesh(new ConeGeometry(1.14,.65,4),material(color)); roof.position.set(x,1.53,z); roof.rotation.y=Math.PI/4; roof.castShadow=true; scene.add(roof);\n      box(scene,0x759b91,[.25,.38,.03],[x,.65,z+.59]);\n    }\n    cylinder(scene,0x8cb7ba,.75,.75,.09,[2.4,.13,2.15]);\n    const board=box(scene,0xf8f4df,[.75,.15,.55],[-.3,.2,.5]); board.rotation.y=-.25;\n    this.hero=new Group(); this.hero.position.set(-.3,.3,.5); scene.add(this.hero);\n    cylinder(this.hero,0xe8866b,.27,.34,.65,[0,.58,0],12);\n    const head=new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(.29,12,10),material(0xf1c29d));head.position.set(0,1.13,0);this.hero.add(head);\n    box(this.hero,0x455d59,[.12,.42,.12],[-.17,.04,0]);box(this.hero,0x455d59,[.12,.42,.12],[.17,.04,0]);\n    const left=box(this.hero,0xe8b995,[.12,.5,.12],[-.36,.64,0]);left.rotation.z=-.7;\n    const right=box(this.hero,0xe8b995,[.12,.5,.12],[.36,.64,0]);right.rotation.z=.7;\n    this.mixer=new THREE.AnimationMixer(this.hero);\n    this.mixer.clipAction(new THREE.AnimationClip('idle',2,[new THREE.NumberKeyframeTrack('.position[y]',[0,1,2],[.3,.34,.3])])).play();\n    const ounce=box(scene,0xf9faf1,[.72,.45,.53],[.9,.35,1.3]);\n    box(scene,0x9cc5b6,[.38,.08,.015],[.9,.42,1.58]); ounce.rotation.y=-.2;\n  }\n  update(ctx, dt) {\n    this.mixer?.update(dt);\n    if (this.hero && this.game.session) {\n      this.hero.rotation.z = -this.game.session.dot.x*.27;\n      this.hero.rotation.x = this.game.session.dot.y*.2;\n    } else if (this.hero) { this.hero.rotation.z *= .95; this.hero.rotation.x *= .95; }\n    ctx.hud.clear();\n  }\n  cameraTarget() { return this.target; }\n  status() { return `island: ${this.game.screen}`; }\n}\n\nexport async function startWorld(game) {\n  if (!navigator.gpu) return;\n  try { if (!await navigator.gpu.requestAdapter()) return; } catch { return; }\n  return Engine.start(new IslandScene(game), withUrlOptions({container:document.getElementById('world'),aspect:'fill',touch:false,background:0xc9e8dc,camera:{preset:'iso',zoom:1.05}}));\n}\n{\"name\":\"a-little-off-balance\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"private\":true,\"type\":\"module\",\"scripts\":{\"build\":\"node tools/build.mjs\",\"test\":\"node tests/run.mjs\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
